/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:34:**Objective:** Everything recorded becomes readable, with its size known. Each message-producing event yields exactly one message with kind-appropriate typed blocks, verbatim content, the actor/harness carry, and a deterministic base-unit token estimate — written in the same walk iteration that records the event, so projection can never drift from its source.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:37:- `messages.createFromEvent` wired into the walk after each recorded event\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:46:**Dependencies:** Story 2 (real recorded events in a real pipeline).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:53:- **AC-2.3**: A `turn_end` event is recorded in the event order but produces no message.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:57:- **AC-2.5**: A `tool_result` payload is recorded and read back in full, regardless of size; intake never truncates or summarizes record content.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:59:- **AC-2.6**: Each event's actor and harness identifiers are recorded as given and carried onto its message.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:69:This story adds projection to Story 2's walk: each recorded message-producing event yields its message, blocks, and token estimate in the same iteration that recorded it, inside the same transaction — projection cannot drift from its source because they are never separated. The risk profile is fidelity, not logic: kind-correct block shapes, verbatim content, and the absence of any code path that could shorten a tool result. `messages.createFromEvent` is the first cross-domain surface call through the operation context, establishing the pattern `turns.applyEvent` follows in Story 4.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:80:- A projection failure must reject the whole batch — recorded events without messages is the stranded state the transaction exists to prevent.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:153:- [ ] Batch results carry `messageId` for recorded message-producing events\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:172:**What gets mocked: nothing.** This epic has no network, no inference provider, no clock-sensitive contract beyond injected `clock`, and its filesystem behavior *is* the product (durability, atomicity, restart survival). Every test runs against real SQLite files in a per-test temp directory. The injected clock is fixed per test for deterministic `recordedAt`/`queuedAt`/`createdAt`; the tokenizer runs real because golden-counting real output is stronger than stubbing it.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:197:| `threadWith(events)` | created thread + recorded batch via real SDK | post-Chunk-2: real pipeline output |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:239:| TC-3.4 | orphan turn_end | turn_end as first event | event recorded order 1; zero turns; zero work; next prompt opens t1 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:251:| TC-4.2 | first-failure index | valid, valid, invalid at index 2 | `eventIndex: 2`; events 0–1 not recorded |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:262:| TC-5.1 | full resend | record 5, resend same 5 | zero recorded; five skips with `duplicate_idempotency_key`; read-back unchanged |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:263:| TC-5.2 | partial resend | 3 recorded + 2 new | three skips, two recorded; orders continue dense (no gaps from skips) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:265:| TC-5.4 | skips inert | resend recorded prompt + turn_end mid-conversation | turn count/states unchanged; no transitions in result; work-item count unchanged; no duplicate message |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:266:| TC-5.5 | key wins | key K with payload A recorded; resend K with valid payload B | skipped; read-back returns A; B nowhere in any table (`openRaw` scan) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:344:    planSummary: \"Wired message projection into the Story 2 batch walk: each recorded message-producing event now yields one message with kind-appropriate typed blocks, verbatim content, actor/harness carry, and a deterministic o200k_base token estimate, written in the same transaction iteration that recorded the event (createFromEvent is the first cross-domain surface call through OperationContext). Added message/message_block tables to thread schema v1 (same extension pattern Story 2 used for the event table), deterministic m<eventOrder> ids, messageId in batch result entries, listMessages read-back, and a live CLI `messages list`. Followed Red→Green: projection.test.ts and cli-process-projection.test.ts written and manifest-recorded first (all 7 failing on assertions), then implemented to green. turnId stays null throughout (Story 4). Projection failure rejects the whole batch, proven by an induced real failure (walk-hook drops message_block mid-transaction) asserted via read-back, not the error result alone.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:354:        reason: \"Recorded the two new Red-phase files; re-recorded smoke.test.ts and cli-process.test.ts after stub-list maintenance\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:401:        command: \"pnpm run red-verify (after Red tests recorded; suite confirmed failing on assertions only)\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:415:        - \"Initial green-verify failed because smoke.test.ts and cli-process.test.ts still expected messages list to be a fail-closed stub; applied the established rolling stub-list maintenance (Story 1 precedent — both files re-recorded in the Red manifest) rather than leaving the live command asserted as a stub\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:439:No older response entries are recorded yet.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:531:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:532:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:582:Caller implication: Do not treat the run as advanced until evidence and ledger updates are durably recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:587:Meaning: A terminal public outcome has been recorded separately from lifecycleState and the story-lead loop will not continue automatically.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/epic/002-epic-reverify.json:1:{\"command\":\"epic-reverify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"needs-fixes\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"2f59cfea-fc4d-43e0-bae5-13c0220e382e\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"sessionId\":\"1ace89b2-5fb5-4f71-8bfc-880d4a4875dc\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"sessionId\":\"1ace89b2-5fb5-4f71-8bfc-880d4a4875dc\",\"operation\":\"epic-reverify\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"outcome\":\"needs-fixes\",\"confirmedIssues\":[\"REVERIFY-02-001 (new, blocking-candidate; introduced surface touched by fix-batch-001): cascadeTurnDelete omits the pair-counterpart cascade that the impl-lead ruling epic-fix-001 established. The ruling ('the call/result pair is a source dependency; deleting or editing one half is a source change for the counterpart's summary', recorded in team-impl-log.md) was applied to cascadeFromMessage and cascadeMessageDelete but not to cascadeTurnDelete in the same file (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts:279-306), even though turn delete deletes member messages that can be halves of cross-turn pairs. Dynamically verified end-to-end: batch [user_prompt, tool_call, turn_end] closes t1 with summary outcome 'unknown'; later batch [user_prompt, tool_result(same callId), turn_end] lands the late result in t2 and AC-2.8's intake repair rebuilds the t1 call summary to outcome 'succeeded' at sourceVersion 2 (cross-turn pairing is reachable: intake validation is shape-only and non-transition kinds stamp to whatever turn is open, pipeline.ts:195-198); turns.deleteTurn(t2) then returns cleared:[] — the t1 call summary is never cleared or requeued and remains ready/'succeeded', derived from a record no longer in the readable record (the AC-2.4/AC-6.1 staleness pattern of EPIC-02-BLOCK-002, surviving through the third mutation path that shares DD-8's one cascade module). With BLOCK-002a's read filter in place an explicit requeue now rebuilds 'unknown' correctly, so exposure is narrower than the original blocker, but nothing flags the stale form and the recorded cascade contract is violated. Quick fix: collect pairedCounterpartSubject for each deleted member (skipping counterparts that are themselves members of the deleted turn, deduped) in cascadeTurnDelete, plus a cross-turn regression test.\",\"E02-NB-001 (retained, non-blocking, minor): mutation and requeue operations still bypass the SDK-injected clock — five runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), ...) sites confirmed at messages/index.ts:331,421,503 and turns/index.ts:356,433. Recorded as deliberately out of fix-batch-001.\",\"E02-NB-003 (retained, non-blocking, observation): the deterministic provider remains the only registered named provider; by design per DD-11 and the epic's scope exclusion of real adapters.\",\"E02-NB-004 (retained, non-blocking, observation): thrown handler errors are still converted to retryable attempts (scheduler.ts:144), documented in place.\",\"E02-NB-005 (retained, non-blocking, observation): attempts accounting asymmetry between terminal paths still present (scheduler.ts:122 vs 162).\"],\"disputedOrUnconfirmedIssues\":[],\"readinessAssessment\":\"Both canonical blockers are fixed in their ruled scope and the fixes verify independently. EPIC-02-BLOCK-001: per-SDK-instance seam via AsyncLocalStorage (shared/context.ts InstanceSeam/runWithInstanceSeam/resolveInstancePoke; sdk.ts scopeSurface wraps intakeStream/messages/turns/work.drain; enqueue's poke rides ctx.poke) matches the per-instance-scoping ruling; the required regression tests exist and pass (test/epic-fix-02.test.ts, background-then-manual and manual-then-background, manual rows stay queued until explicit drain with a live-background positive control). The module-global slots survive only as a documented below-SDK default for direct non-SDK calls — a recorded deviation from the literal 'replace the slots' wording that cannot auto-drain a manual SDK (every manual sdk.* operation runs in the no-op seam); the unscoped sdk.threads surface is benign (no threads public operation opens a thread database — all openThreadDatabase callers are scoped surfaces or the scheduler). EPIC-02-BLOCK-002a: findPairedBlock and findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary now join message with deleted_at IS NULL; regression test proves a deleted result's call summary rebuilds outcome 'unknown'. EPIC-02-BLOCK-002b: edit and message-delete cascades clear+requeue the live pair counterpart; TC-6.2's cascade-scope assertion was amended per the recorded ruling with the red-manifest hash re-recorded (test-immutability passes); the cascade-scope clarification is recorded in the impl log (fix-batch item 4). Gates re-run independently: pnpm run verify-all exit 0 (build, typecheck, lint 76 files, boundaries, 30 test files / 234 tests including the 3 new regression tests) and pnpm run green-verify exit 0 (27 Red-phase files unchanged). However, the ruling's application is incomplete: cascadeTurnDelete — one of the three mutation close paths sharing the one cascade module — leaves a dynamically-reproduced stale-outcome path (REVERIFY-02-001), so the candidate cannot cleanly close against its own recorded cascade contract. Process notes for closeout: both epic-fix harness envelopes errored (PROVIDER_STALLED / PROVIDER_OUTPUT_INVALID) even though the fix work landed in the tree; the entire fix batch is uncommitted working-tree state; an unrelated Epic 03 spec edit (docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md) also sits uncommitted in the tree and should not ride an Epic 02 closeout commit. The four retained non-blocking findings stand as recorded and do not gate closeout.\",\"recommendedNextStep\":\"Run one small follow-up fix batch: extend cascadeTurnDelete to include pairedCounterpartSubject for each deleted member message whose live counterpart lies outside the deleted turn (dedupe against the drop set), add a cross-turn regression test (call in t1, late result in t2 via AC-2.8, delete t2 → t1 call summary cleared and requeued at the next source version, rebuilds outcome 'unknown'), re-run green-verify/verify-all, then commit fix-batch-001 plus this follow-up (excluding the unrelated Epic 03 doc edit) and re-run the reverify pass.\"},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/epic/002-epic-reverify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-11T09:29:15.642Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-11T09:39:40.500Z\"}\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:40:- Idempotency: skip set from recorded keys, validation-before-skip precedence, `skipReason: duplicate_idempotency_key`, skips consume no order numbers, key-wins-over-content\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:52:- **AC-2.1**: A batch of valid events is recorded in array order, with event order continuing from the thread's last recorded event; a following batch continues the same sequence.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:54:- **AC-2.9**: An empty batch is a caller error; nothing is recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:68:- **AC-5.1**: Resending a fully recorded batch records nothing, skips every event, and reports each skip with its idempotency key.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:69:  - **TC-5.1** (AC-5.1): Record five, resend identically → zero recorded, five skips each carrying `skipReason: duplicate_idempotency_key`; read-back unchanged.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:70:- **AC-5.2**: Resending a batch where some events are recorded and some are new skips the recorded ones and records the new ones in batch order.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:71:  - **TC-5.2** (AC-5.2): Three old plus two new → three skips, two recorded continuing the order densely.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:76:- **AC-5.5**: A valid event reusing a recorded key with different content is skipped; the original record is unchanged and the new content is not stored anywhere.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:77:  - **TC-5.5** (AC-5.5): Key K with payload A recorded; resend K with valid payload B → skipped, read-back returns A, B nowhere (`openRaw` scan).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:127:| TC-2.8 | `test/intake.test.ts` | empty array → `empty_batch`, nothing recorded |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:133:| TC-5.2 | `test/idempotency.test.ts` | partial resend: three skips, two recorded, dense order |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:153:- Event read-back: `{ eventOrder, eventKind, idempotencyKey, actor, harness, payload, recordedAt }`; `recordedAt` from the injected clock.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:155:- Order counter initializes from `MAX(event_order)` at transaction start; only recorded events increment it.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:183:- [ ] TC-2.1, TC-2.8, TC-4.1, TC-4.2, TC-4.3, TC-4.5, TC-5.1–5.5 green via SDK; TC-4.4 caller/system legs green with corruption leg recorded as Story 4's debt\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:204:**What gets mocked: nothing.** This epic has no network, no inference provider, no clock-sensitive contract beyond injected `clock`, and its filesystem behavior *is* the product (durability, atomicity, restart survival). Every test runs against real SQLite files in a per-test temp directory. The injected clock is fixed per test for deterministic `recordedAt`/`queuedAt`/`createdAt`; the tokenizer runs real because golden-counting real output is stronger than stubbing it.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:229:| `threadWith(events)` | created thread + recorded batch via real SDK | post-Chunk-2: real pipeline output |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:271:| TC-3.4 | orphan turn_end | turn_end as first event | event recorded order 1; zero turns; zero work; next prompt opens t1 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:283:| TC-4.2 | first-failure index | valid, valid, invalid at index 2 | `eventIndex: 2`; events 0–1 not recorded |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:294:| TC-5.1 | full resend | record 5, resend same 5 | zero recorded; five skips with `duplicate_idempotency_key`; read-back unchanged |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:295:| TC-5.2 | partial resend | 3 recorded + 2 new | three skips, two recorded; orders continue dense (no gaps from skips) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:297:| TC-5.4 | skips inert | resend recorded prompt + turn_end mid-conversation | turn count/states unchanged; no transitions in result; work-item count unchanged; no duplicate message |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:298:| TC-5.5 | key wins | key K with payload A recorded; resend K with valid payload B | skipped; read-back returns A; B nowhere in any table (`openRaw` scan) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:376:    planSummary: \"Implemented Story 2 end to end: three-layer closed validation in src/domains/intake-stream/internal/validate.ts (Effect Schema closed structs under onExcessProperty:'error' for thread-ref envelope, event object, and per-kind payload; server-generated fields denied by name; turn_end empty-payload as its own named rule; first-failure eventIndex); the batch transaction skeleton in internal/pipeline.ts (pure validate → BEGIN IMMEDIATE → per-event walk [dedup-check → record] → walk-time result assembly → COMMIT, MAX(event_order) counter so skips consume no order numbers, key-only skip set read at transaction start, whole rollback on any in-transaction failure wrapped as system_error); event table added to the thread-file schema v1 migration; messageEvents/listEvents wired on the surface; CLI message-events (stdin JSON array via an injectable reader seam, TTY/empty → empty_stdin before any SDK call) and list-events made real. A fixtures-exempt test seam (setIntakeWalkHook) induces real mid-walk failures by closing the handle inside the transaction. Closed Story 1's TC-1.4 deferral. Red manifest recorded for the four new suites plus the two updated Red files before gates ran.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:413:        reason: \"Intake commands removed from the fail-closed stub list (now real); re-recorded in red manifest — same pattern Story 1 used for threads\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:416:        reason: \"TC-1.4 it.todo replaced with a closure note pointing at intake.test.ts; re-recorded in red manifest\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:458:        - \"TC-1.4 read-back equality is asserted modulo recordedAt (wall clock; the public SDK surface has no clock parameter by design) — all contractual fields including eventOrder, payload, and BatchResult compare exactly; recordedAt is asserted to be valid ISO-8601 on both\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:460:        - \"smoke.test.ts and threads.test.ts are prior-story Red files updated by this story (stub list reduction; deferral closure) and re-recorded in the red manifest — the same precedent Story 1 set when it made the threads commands real\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:465:    recommendedNextStep: \"Hand to the story verifier: all TCs (2.1, 2.8, 4.1–4.5 caller/system legs, 5.1–5.5, 1.4) and the four architecture-risk tests are green via SDK and CLI; TC-4.4's corruption leg remains Story 4's recorded debt. After acceptance, proceed to Story 3 (message projection), which extends the same per-event walk.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:480:No older response entries are recorded yet.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:572:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:573:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:623:Caller implication: Do not treat the run as advanced until evidence and ledger updates are durably recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:628:Meaning: A terminal public outcome has been recorded separately from lifecycleState and the story-lead loop will not continue automatically.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:60:- **AC-3.5**: A `turn_end` arriving with no open turn has no turn effect and is still recorded as an event.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:61:  - **TC-3.4** (AC-3.5): `turn_end` as a thread's first event → recorded, no turn exists, no work queued, subsequent prompt opens turn 1 normally.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:67:  - **TC-3.7** (AC-3.9): Manufacture two open turns via the fixture → any batch fails `turn_state_corrupt`; read-back confirms nothing recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:120:| TC-3.4 | `test/turns.test.ts` | orphan turn_end inert, recorded, next prompt opens t1 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:123:| TC-3.7 | `test/turns.test.ts` | corrupt fixture → `turn_state_corrupt`, nothing recorded |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:137:- Rule table (golden contract): 0+prompt→open; 1+prompt→close_then_open; 1+turn_end→close; 0+turn_end→none (event still recorded); other kinds→none (stamp only); >1 open→`turn_state_corrupt` before the walk.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:147:- TC-3.7's \"nothing recorded\" is a full read-back diff against pre-batch baseline, not just the error code.\nd