test/fixtures/threads.ts\",\"packages/lhc/vitest.config.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Initial verification of Story 4 against AC-4.1 through AC-4.7, Flow 4 tech design, report/requeue production paths, CLI mirrors, focused tests, story gate, and epic gate.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-04-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"AC-4.7 turn/chunk read state attachment is deferred, not implemented\",\"evidence\":\"Story AC-4.7 requires reads of message, turn, or chunk records whose forms are not ready to return the record with form states, and TC-4.7 says message and turn reads return full records with states attached (stories/04-derivation-state-report-repair.md:40-43). The production TurnRecord shape has no forms field and listTurns returns readTurns(db) directly (src/domains/turns/index.ts:36-46,151-161). The TC-4.7 test asserts message forms on message reads, but for turns it only checks the records do not error, then reads turn form states through turns.report (test/report-repair.test.ts:528-558). The story deviation table explicitly says TurnRecord does not gain a forms key and turn/chunk form states surface through turns.report instead (stories/04-derivation-state-report-repair.md:147-148). That may be an intentional scope change, but there is no recorded human ruling accepting it as satisfying AC-4.7.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/04-derivation-state-report-repair.md\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/report-repair.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.7\",\"TC-4.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-04-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"AC-4.7 turn/chunk read state attachment is deferred, not implemented\",\"evidence\":\"Story AC-4.7 requires reads of message, turn, or chunk records whose forms are not ready to return the record with form states, and TC-4.7 says message and turn reads return full records with states attached (stories/04-derivation-state-report-repair.md:40-43). The production TurnRecord shape has no forms field and listTurns returns readTurns(db) directly (src/domains/turns/index.ts:36-46,151-161). The TC-4.7 test asserts message forms on message reads, but for turns it only checks the records do not error, then reads turn form states through turns.report (test/report-repair.test.ts:528-558). The story deviation table explicitly says TurnRecord does not gain a forms key and turn/chunk form states surface through turns.report instead (stories/04-derivation-state-report-repair.md:147-148). That may be an intentional scope change, but there is no recorded human ruling accepting it as satisfying AC-4.7.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/04-derivation-state-report-repair.md\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/report-repair.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.7\",\"TC-4.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-4.1\",\"TC-4.1\",\"AC-4.2\",\"TC-4.2\",\"AC-4.3\",\"TC-4.3\",\"AC-4.4\",\"TC-4.4\",\"AC-4.5\",\"TC-4.5\",\"AC-4.6\",\"TC-4.6\",\"CLI report/requeue parity\",\"Production path audit: report/requeue paths use real SDK/domain operations and live SQLite rows; no fake runtime adapters found\",\"Story gate\",\"Epic gate\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-4.7\",\"TC-4.7\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm vitest run test/report-repair.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"AC-4.7 is not satisfied on the turns read production path: turns.listTurns returns TurnRecord records without attached form states; implementation relies on turns.report for those states.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"needs-human-ruling\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"openQuestions\":[\"Does the story owner accept turns.report as the state attachment surface for turn/chunk form states under AC-4.7, or must turns.listTurns/any chunk read surface return form states directly?\"],\"additionalObservations\":[\"The configured story and epic gates both pass: green-verify reports 185 tests passed plus immutability OK, and verify-all reports 207 tests passed.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/004-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-11T05:40:25.461Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-11T05:44:51.237Z\"}\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:27:Messages and blocks projected from recorded events inside the batch transaction; token estimates stamped at creation; message read-back.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:32:**User Profile** (from epic): Everything recorded becomes readable — this is the layer operators will audit and later epics derive from. The integrator sees `messageId` appear in batch results.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:34:**Objective:** Everything recorded becomes readable, with its size known. Each message-producing event yields exactly one message with kind-appropriate typed blocks, verbatim content, the actor/harness carry, and a deterministic base-unit token estimate — written in the same walk iteration that records the event, so projection can never drift from its source.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:37:- `messages.createFromEvent` wired into the walk after each recorded event\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:46:**Dependencies:** Story 2 (real recorded events in a real pipeline).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:53:- **AC-2.3**: A `turn_end` event is recorded in the event order but produces no message.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:57:- **AC-2.5**: A `tool_result` payload is recorded and read back in full, regardless of size; intake never truncates or summarizes record content.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:59:- **AC-2.6**: Each event's actor and harness identifiers are recorded as given and carried onto its message.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:69:This story adds projection to Story 2's walk: each recorded message-producing event yields its message, blocks, and token estimate in the same iteration that recorded it, inside the same transaction — projection cannot drift from its source because they are never separated. The risk profile is fidelity, not logic: kind-correct block shapes, verbatim content, and the absence of any code path that could shorten a tool result. `messages.createFromEvent` is the first cross-domain surface call through the operation context, establishing the pattern `turns.applyEvent` follows in Story 4.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:80:- A projection failure must reject the whole batch — recorded events without messages is the stranded state the transaction exists to prevent.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:153:- [ ] Batch results carry `messageId` for recorded message-producing events\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:172:**What gets mocked: nothing.** This epic has no network, no inference provider, no clock-sensitive contract beyond injected `clock`, and its filesystem behavior *is* the product (durability, atomicity, restart survival). Every test runs against real SQLite files in a per-test temp directory. The injected clock is fixed per test for deterministic `recordedAt`/`queuedAt`/`createdAt`; the tokenizer runs real because golden-counting real output is stronger than stubbing it.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:197:| `threadWith(events)` | created thread + recorded batch via real SDK | post-Chunk-2: real pipeline output |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:239:| TC-3.4 | orphan turn_end | turn_end as first event | event recorded order 1; zero turns; zero work; next prompt opens t1 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:251:| TC-4.2 | first-failure index | valid, valid, invalid at index 2 | `eventIndex: 2`; events 0–1 not recorded |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:262:| TC-5.1 | full resend | record 5, resend same 5 | zero recorded; five skips with `duplicate_idempotency_key`; read-back unchanged |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:263:| TC-5.2 | partial resend | 3 recorded + 2 new | three skips, two recorded; orders continue dense (no gaps from skips) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:265:| TC-5.4 | skips inert | resend recorded prompt + turn_end mid-conversation | turn count/states unchanged; no transitions in result; work-item count unchanged; no duplicate message |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:266:| TC-5.5 | key wins | key K with payload A recorded; resend K with valid payload B | skipped; read-back returns A; B nowhere in any table (`openRaw` scan) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:360:        reason: \"Re-recorded thread-migration.test.ts hash after appending the F-03-002 tests\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:434:    planSummary: \"Wired message projection into the Story 2 batch walk: each recorded message-producing event now yields one message with kind-appropriate typed blocks, verbatim content, actor/harness carry, and a deterministic o200k_base token estimate, written in the same transaction iteration that recorded the event (createFromEvent is the first cross-domain surface call through OperationContext). Added message/message_block tables to thread schema v1 (same extension pattern Story 2 used for the event table), deterministic m<eventOrder> ids, messageId in batch result entries, listMessages read-back, and a live CLI `messages list`. Followed Red→Green: projection.test.ts and cli-process-projection.test.ts written and manifest-recorded first (all 7 failing on assertions), then implemented to green. turnId stays null throughout (Story 4). Projection failure rejects the whole batch, proven by an induced real failure (walk-hook drops message_block mid-transaction) asserted via read-back, not the error result alone.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:444:        reason: \"Recorded the two new Red-phase files; re-recorded smoke.test.ts and cli-process.test.ts after stub-list maintenance\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:491:        command: \"pnpm run red-verify (after Red tests recorded; suite confirmed failing on assertions only)\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:505:        - \"Initial green-verify failed because smoke.test.ts and cli-process.test.ts still expected messages list to be a fail-closed stub; applied the established rolling stub-list maintenance (Story 1 precedent — both files re-recorded in the Red manifest) rather than leaving the live command asserted as a stub\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:592:          - \"Story 3 dependency: Story 2 real recorded events\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:611:          - \"Story 3 dependency: Story 2 real recorded events\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:618:        - \"AC-2.3 / TC-2.2 on current-schema threads: `turn_end` is recorded in events and absent from messages, verified by `test/projection.test.ts`.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:687:    planSummary: \"Fixed F-03-001 with a real migration path. Restored the v1 thread-file migration to the exact accepted Story 2 schema (thread_metadata + event) and moved the message/message_block tables into a new version-2 migration, so the schema is a versioned history rather than a rewritten creation script. Added threads.openThreadDatabase — open + runMigrations to current version — and routed every thread-file open through it: runMessageEvents (migration completes before the batch BEGIN IMMEDIATE), runListEvents, and messages.listMessages. An existing Story 2 file with user_version=1 now gains the message tables on its first open by Story 3 code, on both the write and read paths. Proven with a new fixture that reproduces the accepted Story 2 on-disk layout byte-for-byte (below-SDK writer, sanctioned like corrupt.ts because current code can no longer create that shape) and three focused tests: messageEvents on a legacy file (upgrade, order continuation, m2 projection, legacy event intact, user_version 1→2), listMessages on an untouched legacy file (read-path upgrade, empty list, records unchanged), and a Story 2-recorded idempotency key still skipping after upgrade with no message created.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:703:        reason: \"Fixture building a thread file with the exact accepted Story 2 schema (user_version=1, thread_metadata + event only, optional recorded events) plus a schemaVersionOf reader\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:717:        - \"test/thread-migration.test.ts: an idempotency key recorded under Story 2 still skips after the upgrade and creates no message\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:992:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:993:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:1070:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:1071:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:1148:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:1149:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:1199:Caller implication: Do not treat the run as advanced until evidence and ledger updates are durably recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:1204:Meaning: A terminal public outcome has been recorded separately from lifecycleState and the story-lead loop will not continue automatically.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/05-inference-host-routing.md:6:Wire LHC derivation calls through PI's model registry and auth, classify provider failures, and prove capture-to-derivation recorded outcomes.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/05-inference-host-routing.md:50:**AC-4.5:** A captured thread's background derivation work invokes the injected model-call function and records a result against the thread: a queued derivation runs through LHC's scheduler, calls the function, and persists either a ready derived form or a classified failure, queryable through inspect/health. This closes the loop end to end — capture to derivation to recorded outcome — not just the function in isolation.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/05-inference-host-routing.md:52:**TC-4.5** — A captured thread with queued derivation work, drained through LHC's scheduler with the injected function wired, persists at least one ready derived form (function returns text) and one classified failure (function returns a failure), both queryable through inspect/health — proving the capture→derivation→recorded-outcome loop, not just the function in isolation.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/05-inference-host-routing.md:148:- The capture-to-derivation-to-recorded-outcome loop is proven with queryable results.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:60:- **AC-3.5**: A `turn_end` arriving with no open turn has no turn effect and is still recorded as an event.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:61:  - **TC-3.4** (AC-3.5): `turn_end` as a thread's first event → recorded, no turn exists, no work queued, subsequent prompt opens turn 1 normally.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:67:  - **TC-3.7** (AC-3.9): Manufacture two open turns via the fixture → any batch fails `turn_state_corrupt`; read-back confirms nothing recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:120:| TC-3.4 | `test/turns.test.ts` | orphan turn_end inert, recorded, next prompt opens t1 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:123:| TC-3.7 | `test/turns.test.ts` | corrupt fixture → `turn_state_corrupt`, nothing recorded |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:137:- Rule table (golden contract): 0+prompt→open; 1+prompt→close_then_open; 1+turn_end→close; 0+turn_end→none (event still recorded); other kinds→none (stamp only); >1 open→`turn_state_corrupt` before the walk.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:147:- TC-3.7's \"nothing recorded\" is a full read-back diff against pre-batch baseline, not just the error code.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:170:- [ ] TC-3.1, TC-3.2, TC-3.4, TC-3.5, TC-3.7, TC-3.8 green; TC-3.3/TC-3.6 transition-and-membership halves green with work-item halves recorded as Story 5's debt\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:191:**What gets mocked: nothing.** This epic has no network, no inference provider, no clock-sensitive contract beyond injected `clock`, and its filesystem behavior *is* the product (durability, atomicity, restart survival). Every test runs against real SQLite files in a per-test temp directory. The injected clock is fixed per test for deterministic `recordedAt`/`queuedAt`/`createdAt`; the tokenizer runs real because golden-counting real output is stronger than stubbing it.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:216:| `threadWith(events)` | created thread + recorded batch via real SDK | post-Chunk-2: real pipeline output |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:258:| TC-3.4 | orphan turn_end | turn_end as first event | event recorded order 1; zero turns; zero work; next prompt opens t1 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:270:| TC-4.2 | first-failure index | valid, valid, invalid at index 2 | `eventIndex: 2`; events 0–1 not recorded |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:281:| TC-5.1 | full resend | record 5, resend same 5 | zero recorded; five skips with `duplicate_idempotency_key`; read-back unchanged |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:282:| TC-5.2 | partial resend | 3 recorded + 2 new | three skips, two recorded; orders continue dense (no gaps from skips) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:284:| TC-5.4 | skips inert | resend recorded prompt + turn_end mid-conversation | turn count/states unchanged; no transitions in result; work-item count unchanged; no duplicate message |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:285:| TC-5.5 | key wins | key K with payload A recorded; resend K with valid payload B | skipped; read-back returns A; B nowhere in any table (`openRaw` scan) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:340:No prior bounded child response is recorded yet.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:344:No older response entries are recorded yet.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:385:No prior runtime self-notes are recorded yet.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:434:Caller implication: Do not treat the run as advanced until evidence and ledger updates are durably recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:439:Meaning: A terminal public outcome has been recorded separately from lifecycleState and the story-lead loop will not continue automatically.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:40:- Idempotency: skip set from recorded keys, validation-before-skip precedence, `skipReason: duplicate_idempotency_key`, skips consume no order numbers, key-wins-over-content\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:52:- **AC-2.1**: A batch of valid events is recorded in array order, with event order continuing from the thread's last recorded event; a following batch continues the same sequence.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:54:- **AC-2.9**: An empty batch is a caller error; nothing is recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:68:- **AC-5.1**: Resending a fully recorded batch records nothing, skips every event, and reports each skip with its idempotency key.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:69:  - **TC-5.1** (AC-5.1): Record five, resend identically → zero recorded, five skips each carrying `skipReason: duplicate_idempotency_key`; read-back unchanged.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:70:- **AC-5.2**: Resending a batch where some events are recorded and some are new skips the recorded ones and records the new ones in batch order.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:71:  - **TC-5.2** (AC-5.2): Three old plus two new → three skips, two recorded continuing the order densely.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:76:- **AC-5.5**: A valid event reusing a recorded key with different content is skipped; the original record is unchanged and the new content is not stored anywhere.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:77:  - **TC-5.5** (AC-5.5): Key K with payload A recorded; resend K with valid payload B → skipped, read-back returns A, B nowhere (`openRaw` scan).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:127:| TC-2.8 | `test/intake.test.ts` | empty array → `empty_batch`, nothing recorded |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:133:| TC-5.2 | `test/idempotency.test.ts` | partial resend: three skips, two recorded, dense order |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:153:- Event read-back: `{ eventOrder, eventKind, idempotencyKey, actor, harness, payload, recordedAt }`; `recordedAt` from the injected clock.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:155:- Order counter initializes from `MAX(event_order)` at transaction start; only recorded events increment it.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:183:- [ ] TC-2.1, TC-2.8, TC-4.1, TC-4.2, TC-4.3, TC-4.5, TC-5.1–5.5 green via SDK; TC-4.4 caller/system legs green with corruption leg recorded as Story 4's debt\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:204:**What gets mocked: nothing.** This epic has no network, no inference provider, no clock-sensitive contract beyond injected `clock`, and its filesystem behavior *is* the product (durability, atomicity, restart survival). Every test runs against real SQLite files in a per-test temp directory. The injected clock is fixed per test for deterministic `recordedAt`/`queuedAt`/`createdAt`; the tokenizer runs real because golden-counting real output is stronger than stubbing it.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:229:| `threadWith(events)` | created thread + recorded batch via real SDK | post-Chunk-2: real pipeline output |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:271:| TC-3.4 | orphan turn_end | turn_end as first event | event recorded order 1; zero turns; zero work; next prompt opens t1 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:283:| TC-4.2 | first-failure index | valid, valid, invalid at index 2 | `eventIndex: 2`; events 0–1 not recorded |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:294:| TC-5.1 | full resend | record 5, resend same 5 | zero recorded; five skips with `duplicate_idempotency_key`; read-back unchanged |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:295:| TC-5.2 | partial resend | 3 recorded + 2 new | three skips, two recorded; orders continue dense (no gaps from skips) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:297:| TC-5.4 | skips inert | resend recorded prompt + turn_end mid-conversation | turn count/states unchanged; no transitions in result; work-item count unchanged; no duplicate message |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:298:| TC-5.5 | key wins | key K with payload A recorded; resend K with valid payload B | skipped; read-back returns A; B nowhere in any table (`openRaw` scan) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:388:    reviewScopeSummary: \"Follow-up verification focused on F-02-001 and directly touched intake surfaces. The fix adds a deterministic intake clock seam, updates TC-1.4 to compare exact read-back including recordedAt, and the focused test plus configured gates pass.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:393:        rationale: \"Resolved. `packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:24-33` adds `setIntakeClock`; `runMessageEvents` sources the default clock from that seam at `pipeline.ts:73-77` and still writes recordedAt through `clock().toISOString()` at `pipeline.ts:128-135`. `packages/lhc/test/intake.test.ts:95-139` now sets a fixed clock, sends the same batch through id and path forms, compares `readById.value` exactly to `readByPath`, and asserts recordedAt equals the injected instant. Focused `vitest run test/intake.test.ts -t \\\"TC-1.4\\\"` passed.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:400:        - \"AC-1.6 / TC-1.4: exact id/path read-back equivalence is now verified, including recordedAt, by the updated TC-1.4 test.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:463:    planSummary: \"Implemented Story 2 end to end: three-layer closed validation in src/domains/intake-stream/internal/validate.ts (Effect Schema closed structs under onExcessProperty:'error' for thread-ref envelope, event object, and per-kind payload; server-generated fields denied by name; turn_end empty-payload as its own named rule; first-failure eventIndex); the batch transaction skeleton in internal/pipeline.ts (pure validate → BEGIN IMMEDIATE → per-event walk [dedup-check → record] → walk-time result assembly → COMMIT, MAX(event_order) counter so skips consume no order numbers, key-only skip set read at transaction start, whole rollback on any in-transaction failure wrapped as system_error); event table added to the thread-file schema v1 migration; messageEvents/listEvents wired on the surface; CLI message-events (stdin JSON array via an injectable reader seam, TTY/empty → empty_stdin before any SDK call) and list-events made real. A fixtures-exempt test seam (setIntakeWalkHook) induces real mid-walk failures by closing the handle inside the transaction. Closed Story 1's TC-1.4 deferral. Red manifest recorded for the four new suites plus the two updated Red files before gates ran.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:500:        reason: \"Intake commands removed from the fail-closed stub list (now real); re-recorded in red manifest — same pattern Story 1 used for threads\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:503:        reason: \"TC-1.4 it.todo replaced with a closure note pointing at intake.test.ts; re-recorded in red manifest\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:545:        - \"TC-1.4 read-back equality is asserted modulo recordedAt (wall clock; the public SDK surface has no clock parameter by design) — all contractual fields including eventOrder, payload, and BatchResult compare exactly; recordedAt is asserted to be valid ISO-8601 on both\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:547:        - \"smoke.test.ts and threads.test.ts are prior-story Red files updated by this story (stub list reduction; deferral closure) and re-recorded in the red manifest — the same precedent Story 1 set when it made the threads commands real\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:552:    recommendedNextStep: \"Hand to the story verifier: all TCs (2.1, 2.8, 4.1–4.5 caller/system legs, 5.1–5.5, 1.4) and the four architecture-risk tests are green via SDK and CLI; TC-4.4's corruption leg remains Story 4's recorded debt. After acceptance, proceed to Story 3 (message projection), which extends the same per-event walk.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:626:        title: \"TC-1.4 exact read-back equivalence is not satisfied for recordedAt\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:627:        evidence: \"Epic TC-1.4 requires sending the same batch to one thread by id and a second identical thread by path to produce identical results and identical read-back. The Story 2 test deliberately strips `recordedAt` before comparing read-back in `packages/lhc/test/intake.test.ts:114-128`. Public `messageEvents` calls `runMessageEvents` without a fixed clock in `packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/index.ts:58-63`; `runMessageEvents` defaults to `() => new Date()` and writes that value at `packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:62-66` and `117-124`; `listEvents` returns `recordedAt` at `pipeline.ts:189-203`. A public SDK check with a 20ms delay between the id-form and path-form writes returned `same:false` solely because the two `recordedAt` values differed. Therefore AC-1.6/TC-1.4 is not fully proven and is not satisfied under the story/test-plan wording unless `recordedAt` is ruled out of the TC or a deterministic clock path is added for this contract proof.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:643:        title: \"TC-1.4 exact read-back equivalence is not satisfied for recordedAt\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:644:        evidence: \"Epic TC-1.4 requires sending the same batch to one thread by id and a second identical thread by path to produce identical results and identical read-back. The Story 2 test deliberately strips `recordedAt` before comparing read-back in `packages/lhc/test/intake.test.ts:114-128`. Public `messageEvents` calls `runMessageEvents` without a fixed clock in `packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/index.ts:58-63`; `runMessageEvents` defaults to `() => new Date()` and writes that value at `packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:62-66` and `117-124`; `listEvents` returns `recordedAt` at `pipeline.ts:189-203`. A public SDK check with a 20ms delay between the id-form and path-form writes returned `same:false` solely because the two `recordedAt` values differed. Therefore AC-1.6/TC-1.4 is not fully proven and is not satisfied under the story/test-plan wording unless `recordedAt` is ruled out of the TC or a deterministic clock path is added for this contract proof.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:668:        - \"AC-1.6 / TC-1.4 exact read-back equality, because the Story 2 test excludes recordedAt and the public SDK path writes wall-clock recordedAt values.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:677:      - \"F-02-001: production `messageEvents` stamps `recordedAt` from wall clock, so TC-1.4 exact read-back equality across id/path twin threads is not met under the current requirement wording.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:723:      {\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"signature_delta\",\"signature\":\"\"}},\"session_id\":\"73841117-4412-4191-bf6e-d9dac3fc51d8\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"2ae4540b-1a5f-4ffa-b147-e58d98834456\"}\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:724:      {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_01749apntELdWGmnRU4Wu89Y\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:853:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:854:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:931:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:932:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:1041:Caller implication: Do not treat the run as advanced until evidence and ledger updates are durably recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:1046:Meaning: A terminal public outcome has been recorded separately from lifecycleState and the story-lead loop will not continue automatically.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/00-foundation.md:6:Build the walking skeleton for the pi-lhc extension: package scaffold, PI hook registration rail, plain-data-only state holder, stubbed LHC init/dispose seam, corpus fixture loader, and typed fail-closed stubs.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/00-foundation.md:20:- Test fixture and corpus-loading harness that can load recorded PI corpora and expected intake-event shapes.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/00-foundation.md:41:- Fixture loader reads recorded corpus fixtures and produces structurally valid intake-event expectations.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/00-foundation.md:72:| Fixtures | `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/thread.ts` |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/00-foundation.md:87:| None | `test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts`, extension-load smoke, package script checks | Foundation has no story-owned TC; smoke checks prove load, hook rail, fail-closed stubs, fixture validity, and verification-script availability. |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/00-foundation.md:93:| Fixture validity | `test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts` | Corpus loader yields valid `MessageEventInput` shapes and lifecycle-coherent sequences; named invalid builders produce intended malformed shapes. | Story 0 owns no AC/TC, but later capture tests depend on trustworthy fixtures. |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/00-foundation.md:129:- Fixture loader can load corpus files and expected intake-event shapes.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:27:The `turns` derivation layer: turn rendering composed from message-level forms with recorded fallback gaps, lower-band projection, deterministic chunk close policy, and the two chunk summaries.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:40:- Chunk placement at turn derivation: a turn whose projection succeeded joins the open chunk, placement recorded with the turn; when accumulated projected size plus the incoming turn's would cross the close target, the chunk closes *without* the incoming turn, which starts the next chunk (AC-3.6); a single turn whose projection alone meets the max forms its own chunk immediately (AC-3.7)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:54:  - **TC-3.2** (AC-3.2): Close a turn where one prompt's smoothing failed → rendering `ready`, contains that message's raw content, other forms composed, gap recorded naming the message and form.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:59:- **AC-3.5**: A turn whose lower-band projection succeeded joins the open chunk; placement is recorded with the turn and readable through `turns`.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:75:The `turns` derivation layer, and the epic's biggest single handler: `turn_derivation` composes the rendering from message-level forms (`compose.ts`: ready forms verbatim; non-ready fall back to raw/truncated content, one gap recorded per fallback; consecutive tool activity grouped into outcome-explicit run accounts), sends it through `composeTurnRendering` then `projectLowerBand`, lands both as turn forms — then placement runs *in the completion transaction*: append to the open chunk, close on the accumulated policy (DD-9), and closing enqueues both summary kinds as separate items with independent lifecycles.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:77:Two invariants govern: **gaps are recorded facts, not live links** (AC-3.3 — a repaired dependency changes nothing until the dependent is explicitly rebuilt; this is the no-auto-cascade rule the epic's reviewers converged on), and **placement is pure arithmetic** (DD-9 — close decisions from stored projected token counts only, so identical streams re-chunk identically, AC-3.9). The close rule: when accumulated + incoming would cross the target, the chunk closes *without* the incoming turn, which opens the next chunk; a single projection ≥ max forms its own chunk. This is the v1 bug's fix — the MVP checked only the incoming turn's size, so small turns accumulated forever.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:137:**Dependency Gap contract** (epic Data Contracts): recorded on the composed artifact at derivation time; names the source record (messageId or turnId) and the form that fell back; the artifact is `ready` and usable. Lifecycle: created with the composition, persists through dependency repair (no auto-cascade — AC-3.3's no-silent-rebuild rule), cleared only by explicit rebuild of the gapped artifact (Flow 4 re-queue or mutation cascade).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:244:| TC-3.2 | Fail one prompt's smoothing past budget; close turn; drain | Rendering ready; contains raw prompt text; gap recorded `{message, smoothed_prompt}` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:288:Two Epic 02 changes touch Epic 01's exact assertions. Both amendments are **sanctioned in advance** — the red-manifest immutability gate requires regenerating `test/red-manifest.json` as an explicit step of the story that makes each change, recorded in its deviation notes:\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:354:    planSummary: \"Implemented the turns derivation layer (Story 3, TC-3.1–3.9). Added a completion-transaction hook to the work-queue util (complete() gains an optional onApplied callback invoked inside the completion's BEGIN IMMEDIATE, only when the version-checked form writes hit, with onCommit registrations flushed post-commit) so chunk placement and the close→summary enqueues ride the same commit as the rendering/projection writes — the story's placement-atomicity requirement — while the util stays domain-blind. New turns-internal modules: compose.ts (pure (messages, forms) → {parts, gaps}: ready forms verbatim, non-ready fall back to raw/truncated content with one DependencyGap per fallback, tool parts carry mechanically derived outcomes in message order so a run's outcome structurally cannot be lost), chunks.ts (placeTurn with the DD-9 accumulated close policy — close when accumulated + incoming ≥ target excluding the incoming turn, single projection ≥ max self-chunks immediately, empty chunks never close, already-placed turns keep their placement on rebuild — plus enqueueChunkSummaries and placement read-back), forms.ts (deleted-filtered turn/member/form/projection reads), derive.ts (turn_derivation handler: compose → composeTurnRendering → projectLowerBand → two form writes + placement hook with estimateTokens computed exactly once at landing; chunk_summary_detailed/brief handlers reading member projections in member_idx order). Registered turns.workHandlers; turn read-back now carries chunkId/memberIdx. Gaps are recorded facts: repair of a dependency changes nothing (TC-3.3 byte-equal assertion); explicit re-queues in tests drive the queue util directly per the story note.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:463:No older response entries are recorded yet.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:555:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:556:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:606:Caller implication: Do not treat the run as advanced until evidence and ledger updates are durably recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:611:Meaning: A terminal public outcome has been recorded separately from lifecycleState and the story-lead loop will not continue automatically.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:243:| TC-3.2 | Fail one prompt's smoothing past budget; close turn; drain | Rendering ready; contains raw prompt text; gap recorded `{message, smoothed_prompt}` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:287:Two Epic 02 changes touch Epic 01's exact assertions. Both amendments are **sanctioned in advance** — the red-manifest immutability gate requires regenerating `test/red-manifest.json` as an explicit step of the story that makes each change, recorded in its deviation notes:\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:384:        reason: \"recorded the two new test files' hashes (green may add files; the record step locks them)\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:445:No older response entries are recorded yet.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:537:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:538:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:588:Caller implication: Do not treat the run as advanced until evidence and ledger updates are durably recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:593:Meaning: A terminal public outcome has been recorded separately from lifecycleState and the story-lead loop will not continue automatically.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution.md:47:**AC-1.4:** On `session_shutdown`, the extension disposes the LHC instance with flush and cleanup. A subsequent run that resolves the same thread finds it complete through the last event recorded before shutdown — no trailing loss.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:27:Verify capture by replaying recorded PI corpora through the converter and matching deterministic thread read-back and inspect surfaces.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:34:**Objective:** Prove capture correctness from recorded corpora without serving context to a model.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:41:- Inspect overview and health assertions for counts, last recorded position, gaps, and failed derivations.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:45:- Creating M0 corpora. This story consumes M0 corpora as fixtures.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:49:**Dependencies:** Story 2. M0 corpora are fixture inputs.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:54:**AC-6.1:** Replaying a recorded PI corpus through the converter produces a thread whose read-back — events, messages, and turns — matches the fixture's expectation, including the chatty, tool-heavy, parallel-tool, error-result, and aborted-turn corpora.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:56:**TC-6.1** — Each corpus (chatty, tool-heavy, parallel-tool, error-result, aborted-turn) replays to a thread whose read-back matches the fixture.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:58:**AC-6.2:** Replay is deterministic: the same corpus replayed twice produces identical thread read-back. The deterministic-ID property holds through the converter, so a re-replay does not perturb IDs or ordering.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:60:**TC-6.2** — The same corpus replayed twice yields identical read-back (IDs and order stable).\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:62:**AC-6.3:** inspect surfaces (overview, health) reflect the captured session: event and message counts, the last recorded event position, and any capture gaps or failed derivations are visible rather than hidden.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:71:Story 3 is the proof layer for capture. It replays recorded PI corpora through the real converter and LHC intake path, then compares the thread read-back without serving context to a model.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:84:- M0 corpora breadth determines final fixture coverage; the replay machinery should widen as corpora arrive.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:92:| Corpus fixtures | `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts` |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:94:| Verification tests | `packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts` |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:112:| TC-6.1 | `test/verify/replay.test.ts` | Each available recorded corpus replays through the converter to a thread whose events, messages, and turns match fixture expectation. |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:113:| TC-6.2 | `test/verify/replay.test.ts` | Replaying the same corpus twice yields identical read-back, including deterministic IDs and order. |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:114:| TC-6.3 | `test/verify/replay.test.ts` | Inspect overview/health report event/message counts, last recorded position, gaps, and failed derivations. |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:120:| Fixture validity | `test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts` | Corpus loader yields valid `MessageEventInput` shapes and lifecycle-coherent sequences. | Replay tests can pass against bad fixtures unless the fixture substrate is checked independently. |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:124:- `replayCorpus(corpus, threadRef)` should return a structured compare result with a readable diff.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:136:- Registration/default path: tests feed recorded corpora into the same converter/intake path used by live capture.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:141:- Targeted: `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify -- test/verify/replay.test.ts test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts`\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:153:- Fixture replay compares events, messages, and turns for all available M0 corpora.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:170:This plan maps every TC to one or more tests, assigns each to a chunk, and lays out the Red/Green sequence per chunk. The mock boundary is fixed by the tech design: the PI hook surface (fed by synthetic events and recorded corpora) and the `ModelCall` (a deterministic fake) are the only external edges; everything LHC runs real against a temp SQLite thread. Connector modules are exercised through their entry points, never mocked against each other.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:216:| TC-2.1 | User/assistant/toolResult record ordered; assistant fans out thinking→text→toolCall | synthetic sequence | events recorded in source order; assistant fan-out order exact |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:224:| TC-2.2 | One-prompt-two-tools-then-answer → exactly one LHC turn, `turn_end` at agent_end | the Flow 2 worked-example corpus | exactly one `turn_end`; emitted at `agent_end`; per-step PI `turn_end`s produce none |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:239:| TC-2.6 | Graceful interrupt: partial content + aborted disposition; turn closes complete-but-aborted | aborted-turn corpus (`stopReason:aborted`, agent_end fires) | partial assistant content recorded; aborted disposition carried; turn closed at agent_end |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:241:> Hard-kill (no `agent_end`) is covered as a deterministic-boundary golden in `turn-derivation.test.ts`: open turn left open, tolerated as a no-op on reattach (no duplication of the recorded prefix).\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:287:| TC-6.1 | Each corpus replays to a thread whose read-back matches the fixture | chatty, tool-heavy, parallel, error, aborted corpora | read-back (events/messages/turns) matches fixture expectation per corpus |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:288:| TC-6.2 | Same corpus replayed twice → identical read-back | one corpus, two replays | byte-identical read-back; IDs and order stable |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:291:### `test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts` *(risk: fixture validity)*\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:295:| Corpus loader yields valid MessageEventInput shapes + lifecycle-coherent sequences | every loaded corpus parses to well-formed events; named invalid builder produces the intended malformed shape |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:306:- **Red:** fixture-invariant tests (corpus shapes, synthetic coherence, temp-thread create+reopen); extension-loads smoke; package verification scripts/config present.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:329:- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 4 tests pass. Consumes M0 corpora; widens as they arrive.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:362:| Manual: load into real PI, run a session, inspect | manual | the wide pass; not automated, recorded in tech-design Testing Strategy |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:407:    planSummary: \"Story 3 (Capture Verification) implements verify/replay.ts plus its tests; net-new code only (src/verify/replay.ts impl + test/verify/replay.test.ts new). replayCorpus(corpus, threadRef) builds a real background LhcInstance via lhc.createSdk with a local observe-only fail-closed provider (verify has no pinned boundary edge to lifecycle, so it cannot import initInstance), then drives each corpus's source AgentMessages through the REAL Story-2 converter (mapMessage -> TurnAccumulator -> capture), reconstructing the PI hook stream: each message is a message_end, and an agent_end closes the LHC turn at every agent-run boundary (before a fresh user prompt, and once at end-of-stream) so PI's 'new prompt = new run' yields exactly one turn_end per run. It drains settled, reads the durable thread back via intakeStream.listEvents + inspect.overview, and compares events (kind+payload, in source order), messages (visible + byKind), and turns (closed/open) to the fixture with a readable diff — never writing the fixture's expected events to the thread, never comparing counts alone (anti-shim). A deterministic corpus-derived piSessionId ('replay:<name>') plus a per-message entryId make the converter's idempotency keys identical across replays, so the same corpus replayed into two fresh threads is byte-identical (AC-6.2). The pinned ReplayResult {matches, diff} and the (corpus, threadRef) signature are kept exactly; Corpus is unchanged. Run story gate `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify` and epic gate `verify-all` both pass (15 test files / 79 tests). Verification serves nothing to a model.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:411:        reason: \"Replaced the foundation fail-closed stub with the real replayCorpus harness: build a background observe-only LhcInstance, drive corpus.source through the Story-2 converter into a real temp thread, synthesize agent-run (agent_end) boundaries, drain, read the durable thread back (listEvents + inspect.overview), and compare events/messages/turns to the fixture with a readable diff. Kept the pinned ReplayResult {matches, diff} and the (corpus, threadRef) signature.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:414:        reason: \"New Story-3 tests. TC-6.1: describe.each over all five corpora (chatty/tool-heavy/parallel-tool/error-result/aborted-turn) replays to a read-back matching the fixture. TC-6.2: same corpus into two fresh threads yields byte-identical read-back incl. real, stable idempotency keys, and re-replay into the same thread is a dedup no-op. TC-6.3: inspect overview/health report event/message counts, last recorded position, an induced capture gap, and failed derivations.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:417:        - \"test/verify/replay.test.ts :: TC-6.1 corpus replay read-back matches fixture — chatty, tool-heavy, parallel-tool, error-result, aborted-turn (5 cases via describe.each)\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:418:        - \"test/verify/replay.test.ts :: TC-6.2 same corpus into two fresh threads -> identical read-back, real/stable idempotency keys\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:420:        - \"test/verify/replay.test.ts :: TC-6.3 inspect overview/health report counts, last recorded position, capture gap, and failed derivations\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:429:        command: \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec vitest run test/verify/replay.test.ts test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts (targeted)\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:443:        - \"Determinism (AC-6.2): derive piSessionId from the corpus name (not the random temp-thread path) and stamp a deterministic per-message entryId, so the converter's Tier-1 idempotency keys are identical across replays — verified by comparing two fresh threads byte-for-byte.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:444:        - \"Anti-shim: replay drives the real converter (mapMessage + TurnAccumulator + capture) and compares events + messages + turns in order, never writing corpus.expected to the thread and never comparing counts alone.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:449:        - \"replay derives agent-run (agent_end) boundaries from the source message stream (a new user prompt closes the prior run) because Corpus.source is a flat AgentMessage[] with no explicit run markers. This reconstruction is validated against every fixture's expected turn_end (the compare fails loudly if wrong). If M0 recordings encode explicit run/agent_end boundaries, driveCorpus should consume those instead of inferring them.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:451:      - \"M0 corpora breadth: the five synthetic corpora stand in until M0 delivers real PI recordings; the replay machinery is real and widens automatically as named corpora arrive (CORPUS_LOADERS / loadAllCorpora).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:470:No older response entries are recorded yet.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:562:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:563:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:613:Caller implication: Do not treat the run as advanced until evidence and ledger updates are durably recorded.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:618:Meaning: A terminal public outcome has been recorded separately from lifecycleState and the story-lead loop will not continue automatically.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:40:- Idempotency: skip set from recorded keys, validation-before-skip precedence, `skipReason: duplicate_idempotency_key`, skips consume no order numbers, key-wins-over-content\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:52:- **AC-2.1**: A batch of valid events is recorded in array order, with event order continuing from the thread's last recorded event; a following batch continues the same sequence.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:54:- **AC-2.9**: An empty batch is a caller error; nothing is recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:68:- **AC-5.1**: Resending a fully recorded batch records nothing, skips every event, and reports each skip with its idempotency key.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:69:  - **TC-5.1** (AC-5.1): Record five, resend identically → zero recorded, five skips each carrying `skipReason: duplicate_idempotency_key`; read-back unchanged.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:70:- **AC-5.2**: Resending a batch where some events are recorded and some are new skips the recorded ones and records the new ones in batch order.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:71:  - **TC-5.2** (AC-5.2): Three old plus two new → three skips, two recorded continuing the order densely.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:76:- **AC-5.5**: A valid event reusing a recorded key with different content is skipped; the original record is unchanged and the new content is not stored anywhere.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:77:  - **TC-5.5** (AC-5.5): Key K with payload A recorded; resend K with valid payload B → skipped, read-back returns A, B nowhere (`openRaw` scan).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:127:| TC-2.8 | `test/intake.test.ts` | empty array → `empty_batch`, nothing recorded |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:133:| TC-5.2 | `test/idempotency.test.ts` | partial resend: three skips, two recorded, dense order |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:153:- Event read-back: `{ eventOrder, eventKind, idempotencyKey, actor, harness, payload, recordedAt }`; `recordedAt` from the injected clock.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:155:- Order counter initializes from `MAX(event_order)` at transaction start; only recorded events increment it.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:183:- [ ] TC-2.1, TC-2.8, TC-4.1, TC-4.2, TC-4.3, TC-4.5, TC-5.1–5.5 green via SDK; TC-4.4 caller/system legs green with corruption leg recorded as Story 4's debt\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:204:**What gets mocked: nothing.** This epic has no network, no inference provider, no clock-sensitive contract beyond injected `clock`, and its filesystem behavior *is* the product (durability, atomicity, restart survival). Every test runs against real SQLite files in a per-test temp directory. The injected clock is fixed per test for deterministic `recordedAt`/`queuedAt`/`createdAt`; the tokenizer runs real because golden-counting real output is stronger than stubbing it.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:229:| `threadWith(events)` | created thread + recorded batch via real SDK | post-Chunk-2: real pipeline output |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:271:| TC-3.4 | orphan turn_end | turn_end as first event | event recorded order 1; zero turns; zero work; next prompt opens t1 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:283:| TC-4.2 | first-failure index | valid, valid, invalid at index 2 | `eventIndex: 2`; events 0–1 not recorded |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:294:| TC-5.1 | full resend | record 5, resend same 5 | zero recorded; five skips with `duplicate_idempotency_key`; read-back unchanged |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:295:| TC-5.2 | partial resend | 3 recorded + 2 new | three skips, two recorded; orders continue dense (no gaps from skips) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:297:| TC-5.4 | skips inert | resend recorded prompt + turn_end mid-conversation | turn count/states unchanged; no transitions in result; work-item count unchanged; no duplicate message |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:298:| TC-5.5 | key wins | key K with payload A recorded; resend K with valid payload B | skipped; read-back returns A; B nowhere in any table (`openRaw` scan) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:412:        title: \"TC-1.4 exact read-back equivalence is not satisfied for recordedAt\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:413:        evidence: \"Epic TC-1.4 requires sending the same batch to one thread by id and a second identical thread by path to produce identical results and identical read-back. The Story 2 test deliberately strips `recordedAt` before comparing read-back in `packages/lhc/test/intake.test.ts:114-128`. Public `messageEvents` calls `runMessageEvents` without a fixed clock in `packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/index.ts:58-63`; `runMessageEvents` defaults to `() => new Date()` and writes that value at `packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:62-66` and `117-124`; `listEvents` returns `recordedAt` at `pipeline.ts:189-203`. A public SDK check with a 20ms delay between the id-form and path-form writes returned `same:false` solely because the two `recordedAt` values differed. Therefore AC-1.6/TC-1.4 is not fully proven and is not satisfied under the story/test-plan wording unless `recordedAt` is ruled out of the TC or a deterministic clock path is added for this contract proof.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:429:        title: \"TC-1.4 exact read-back equivalence is not satisfied for recordedAt\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:430:        evidence: \"Epic TC-1.4 requires sending the same batch to one thread by id and a second identical thread by path to produce identical results and identical read-back. The Story 2 test deliberately strips `recordedAt` before comparing read-back in `packages/lhc/test/intake.test.ts:114-128`. Public `messageEvents` calls `runMessageEvents` without a fixed clock in `packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/index.ts:58-63`; `runMessageEvents` defaults to `() => new Date()` and writes that value at `packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:62-66` and `117-124`; `listEvents` returns `recordedAt` at `pipeline.ts:189-203`. A public SDK check with a 20ms delay between the id-form and path-form writes returned `same:false` solely because the two `recordedAt` values differed. Therefore AC-1.6/TC-1.4 is not fully proven and is not satisfied under the story/test-plan wording unless `recordedAt` is ruled out of the TC or a deterministic clock path is added for this contract proof.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:454:        - \"AC-1.6 / TC-1.4 exact read-back equality, because the Story 2 test excludes recordedAt and the public SDK path writes wall-clock recordedAt values.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:463:      - \"F-02-001: production `messageEvents` stamps `recordedAt` from wall clock, so TC-1.4 exact read-back equality across id/path twin threads is not met under the current requirement wording.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:510:    planSummary: \"Implemented Story 2 end to end: three-layer closed validation in src/domains/intake-stream/internal/validate.ts (Effect Schema closed structs under onExcessProperty:'error' for thread-ref envelope, event object, and per-kind payload; server-generated fields denied by name; turn_end empty-payload as its own named rule; first-failure eventIndex); the batch transaction skeleton in internal/pipeline.ts (pure validate → BEGIN IMMEDIATE → per-event walk [dedup-check → record] → walk-time result assembly → COMMIT, MAX(event_order) counter so skips consume no order numbers, key-only skip set read at transaction start, whole rollback on any in-transaction failure wrapped as system_error); event table added to the thread-file schema v1 migration; messageEvents/listEvents wired on the surface; CLI message-events (stdin JSON array via an injectable reader seam, TTY/empty → empty_stdin before any SDK call) and list-events made real. A fixtures-exempt test seam (setIntakeWalkHook) induces real mid-walk failures by closing the handle inside the transaction. Closed Story 1's TC-1.4 deferral. Red manifest recorded for the four new suites plus the two updated Red files before gates ran.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:547:        reason: \"Intake commands removed from the fail-closed stub list (now real); re-recorded in red manifest — same pattern Story 1 used for threads\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:550:        reason: \"TC-1.4 it.todo replaced with a closure note pointing at intake.test.ts; re-recorded in red manifest\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:592:        - \"TC-1.4 read-back equality is asserted modulo recordedAt (wall clock; the public SDK surface has no clock parameter by design) — all contractual fields including eventOrder, payload, and BatchResult compare exactly; recordedAt is asserted to be valid ISO-8601 on both\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:594:        - \"smoke.test.ts and threads.test.ts are prior-story Red files updated by this story (stub list reduction; deferral closure) and re-recorded in the red manifest — the same precedent Story 1 set when it made the threads commands real\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:599:    recommendedNextStep: \"Hand to the story verifier: all TCs (2.1, 2.8, 4.1–4.5 caller/system legs, 5.1–5.5, 1.4) and the four architecture-risk tests are green via SDK and CLI; TC-4.4's corruption leg remains Story 4's recorded debt. After acceptance, proceed to Story 3 (message projection), which extends the same per-event walk.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:712:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:713:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:796:Caller implication: Do not treat the run as advanced until evidence and ledger updates are durably recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:801:Meaning: A terminal public outcome has been recorded separately from lifecycleState and the story-lead loop will not continue automatically.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:27:Messages and blocks projected from recorded events inside the batch transaction; token estimates stamped at creation; message read-back.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:32:**User Profile** (from epic): Everything recorded becomes readable — this is the layer operators will audit and later epics derive from. The integrator sees `messageId` appear in batch results.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:34:**Objective:** Everything recorded becomes readable, with its size known. Each message-producing event yields exactly one message with kind-appropriate typed blocks, verbatim content, the actor/harness carry, and a deterministic base-unit token estimate — written in the same walk iteration that records the event, so projection can never drift from its source.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:37:- `messages.createFromEvent` wired into the walk after each recorded event\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:46:**Dependencies:** Story 2 (real recorded events in a real pipeline).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:53:- **AC-2.3**: A `turn_end` event is recorded in the event order but produces no message.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:57:- **AC-2.5**: A `tool_result` payload is recorded and read back in full, regardless of size; intake never truncates or summarizes record content.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:59:- **AC-2.6**: Each event's actor and harness identifiers are recorded as given and carried onto its message.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:69:This story adds projection to Story 2's walk: each recorded message-producing event yields its message, blocks, and token estimate in the same iteration that recorded it, inside the same transaction — projection cannot drift from its source because they are never separated. The risk profile is fidelity, not logic: kind-correct block shapes, verbatim content, and the absence of any code path that could shorten a tool result. `messages.createFromEvent` is the first cross-domain surface call through the operation context, establishing the pattern `turns.applyEvent` follows in Story 4.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:80:- A projection failure must reject the whole batch — recorded events without messages is the stranded state the transaction exists to prevent.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:153:- [ ] Batch results carry `messageId` for recorded message-producing events\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:172:**What gets mocked: nothing.** This epic has no network, no inference provider, no clock-sensitive contract beyond injected `clock`, and its filesystem behavior *is* the product (durability, atomicity, restart survival). Every test runs against real SQLite files in a per-test temp directory. The injected clock is fixed per test for deterministic `recordedAt`/`queuedAt`/`createdAt`; the tokenizer runs real because golden-counting real output is stronger than stubbing it.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:197:| `threadWith(events)` | created thread + recorded batch via real SDK | post-Chunk-2: real pipeline output |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:239:| TC-3.4 | orphan turn_end | turn_end as first event | event recorded order 1; zero turns; zero work; next prompt opens t1 |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:251:| TC-4.2 | first-failure index | valid, valid, invalid at index 2 | `eventIndex: 2`; events 0–1 not recorded |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:262:| TC-5.1 | full resend | record 5, resend same 5 | zero recorded; five skips with `duplicate_idempotency_key`; read-back unchanged |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:263:| TC-5.2 | partial resend | 3 recorded + 2 new | three skips, two recorded; orders continue dense (no gaps from skips) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:265:| TC-5.4 | skips inert | resend recorded prompt + turn_end mid-conversation | turn count/states unchanged; no transitions in result; work-item count unchanged; no duplicate message |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:266:| TC-5.5 | key wins | key K with payload A recorded; resend K with valid payload B | skipped; read-back returns A; B nowhere in any table (`openRaw` scan) |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:436:    planSummary: \"Wired message projection into the Story 2 batch walk: each recorded message-producing event now yields one message with kind-appropriate typed blocks, verbatim content, actor/harness carry, and a deterministic o200k_base token estimate, written in the same transaction iteration that recorded the event (createFromEvent is the first cross-domain surface call through OperationContext). Added message/message_block tables to thread schema v1 (same extension pattern Story 2 used for the event table), deterministic m<eventOrder> ids, messageId in batch result entries, listMessages read-back, and a live CLI `messages list`. Followed Red→Green: projection.test.ts and cli-process-projection.test.ts written and manifest-recorded first (all 7 failing on assertions), then implemented to green. turnId stays null throughout (Story 4). Projection failure rejects the whole batch, proven by an induced real failure (walk-hook drops message_block mid-transaction) asserted via read-back, not the error result alone.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:446:        reason: \"Recorded the two new Red-phase files; re-recorded smoke.test.ts and cli-process.test.ts after stub-list maintenance\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:493:        command: \"pnpm run red-verify (after Red tests recorded; suite confirmed failing on assertions only)\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:507:        - \"Initial green-verify failed because smoke.test.ts and cli-process.test.ts still expected messages list to be a fail-closed stub; applied the established rolling stub-list maintenance (Story 1 precedent — both files re-recorded in the Red manifest) rather than leaving the live command asserted as a stub\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:594:          - \"Story 3 dependency: Story 2 real recorded events\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:613:          - \"Story 3 dependency: Story 2 real recorded events\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:620:        - \"AC-2.3 / TC-2.2 on current-schema threads: `turn_end` is recorded in events and absent from messages, verified by `test/projection.test.ts`.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:689:    planSummary: \"Fixed F-03-001 with a real migration path. Restored the v1 thread-file migration to the exact accepted Story 2 schema (thread_metadata + event) and moved the message/message_block tables into a new version-2 migration, so the schema is a versioned history rather than a rewritten creation script. Added threads.openThreadDatabase — open + runMigrations to current version — and routed every thread-file open through it: runMessageEvents (migration completes before the batch BEGIN IMMEDIATE), runListEvents, and messages.listMessages. An existing Story 2 file with user_version=1 now gains the message tables on its first open by Story 3 code, on both the write and read paths. Proven with a new fixture that reproduces the accepted Story 2 on-disk layout byte-for-byte (below-SDK writer, sanctioned like corrupt.ts because current code can no longer create that shape) and three focused tests: messageEvents on a legacy file (upgrade, order continuation, m2 projection, legacy event intact, user_version 1→2), listMessages on an untouched legacy file (read-path upgrade, empty list, records unchanged), and a Story 2-recorded idempotency key still skipping after upgrade with no message created.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:705:        reason: \"Fixture building a thread file with the exact accepted Story 2 schema (user_version=1, thread_metadata + event only, optional recorded events) plus a schemaVersionOf reader\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:719:        - \"test/thread-migration.test.ts: an idempotency key recorded under Story 2 still skips after the upgrade and creates no message\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:921:        reason: \"Re-recorded thread-migration.test.ts hash after appending the F-03-002 tests\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:1086:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:1087:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:1164:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:1165:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:1242:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:1243:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:1326:Caller implication: Do not treat the run as advanced until evidence and ledger updates are durably recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-007.md:1331:Meaning: A terminal public outcome has been recorded separately from lifecycleState and the story-lead loop will not continue automatically.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/005-story-orchestrate-resume.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-orchestrate resume\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"needs-user-decision\",\"outcome\":\"interrupted\",\"result\":{\"cas