upted and recorded a terminal recovery package, so the safest replay point is the current durable story-run snapshot.\",\"validArtifactPaths\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/001-story-validate.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/003-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/001-final-package.json\"],\"requiresFreshStoryLeadSession\":false,\"requiresFreshChildProviderSession\":false},\"logHandoff\":{\"recommendedState\":\"STORY_ORCHESTRATION_INTERRUPTED\",\"recommendedCurrentStory\":\"03-readiness-sweep\",\"recommendedCurrentPhase\":\"story-orchestrate\",\"continuationHandles\":{\"storyVerifier\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019eb786-e7ae-7d92-84c3-8daefeb333c6\",\"storyId\":\"03-readiness-sweep\"}},\"storyReceiptDraft\":{\"storyId\":\"03-readiness-sweep\",\"storyTitle\":\"Story 3: Readiness Sweep\",\"implementorEvidenceRefs\":[],\"verifierEvidenceRefs\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/003-verify.json\"],\"gateCommand\":\"npm run green-verify\",\"gateResult\":\"fail\",\"dispositions\":[],\"baselineBeforeStory\":null,\"baselineAfterStory\":null,\"openRisks\":[\"The attempt was interrupted and recorded a terminal recovery package, so the safest replay point is the current durable story-run snapshot.\"]},\"cumulativeBaseline\":{\"baselineBeforeCurrentStory\":null,\"expectedAfterCurrentStory\":null,\"latestActualTotal\":null},\"commitReadiness\":{\"state\":\"not-ready\",\"reason\":\"Impl-lead acceptance remains blocked until story-lead closes the outstanding follow-up.\"},\"openRisks\":[\"The attempt was interrupted and recorded a terminal recovery package, so the safest replay point is the current durable story-run snapshot.\"]},\"cleanupHandoff\":{\"acceptedRiskItems\":[],\"deferredItems\":[],\"cleanupRequired\":false},\"rulingRequest\":null,\"recommendedImplLeadAction\":\"reopen\"},\"recoveryGuidance\":\"Use story-orchestrate resume after correcting the child operation failure; replay should start from the last safe story-run checkpoint.\",\"latestEventSequence\":16},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"story-run-current\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/001-current.json\"},{\"kind\":\"story-run-events\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/001-events.jsonl\"},{\"kind\":\"story-run-final-package\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/story-lead/001-final-package.json\"},{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/03-readiness-sweep/005-story-orchestrate-resume.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-11T16:52:05.876Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-11T16:55:50.453Z\"}\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/streams/001-story-lead.stdout.log:7:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"action\\\":\\\"run-implement\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The prior story-implement child operation was interrupted by provider unavailability before producing a recoverable child result, and no bounded child response is recorded. A fresh implementation action is the smallest safe next step to advance the story from the durable requirements.\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"promptAddendum\\\":\\\"Implement Story 4 directly from the provided story file and test plan. Preserve the Story 5 queueing deferral: close paths must work without invoking, stubbing, or faking turn-derivation work items. Produce durable implementation evidence, targeted test evidence, and note any verification that remains for story-lead follow-up.\\\"}}\"}}\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/epic/001-epic-review.json:1:{\"command\":\"epic-review\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"canonicalReview\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"reviewerLabels\":[\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"epic-reviewer-2\"],\"reconciliationSummary\":\"Two reviewers split: epic-reviewer-1 (claude-code) returned pass with five non-blocking findings; epic-reviewer-2 (codex) returned block with two majors, both verified dynamically. Independent re-verification against the code confirms both blockers, so the conservative rule holds and neither is downgraded. (1) Mode isolation: both reviewers found the same defect — reviewer-1 as minor E02-NB-002, reviewer-2 as blocking EPIC-02-BLOCK-001. Code confirms it: sdk.ts:254-257 installs the process-global scheduler poke and thread-touch seams only in background mode and manual mode 'leaves the slots alone'; shared/context.ts:40-48 holds module-global slots that nothing clears; work-queue enqueue (index.ts:136) unconditionally registers onCommit(() => fireSchedulerPoke(threadId)). A manual SDK constructed after a background SDK therefore drains automatically through the stale background scheduler, violating AC-1.7's manual-mode contract. The sdk.ts comment explicitly contemplates multi-SDK-per-process (background supersedes background), so the background-then-manual sequence is inside the design's contemplated space, not an unsupported configuration. The two findings are merged into one blocking finding; reviewer-1's minor classification is the material disagreement, resolved conservatively toward the dynamically verified blocker. (2) Deleted-pair outcomes: only reviewer-2 found EPIC-02-BLOCK-002, and every step of its claimed code path verifies: findPairedBlock (messages/internal/forms.ts:163-178) joins message with no deleted_at IS NULL filter — an unsanctioned exception to tech-design Part 3b's deleted-read filter rule, which names exactly two exceptions, neither of them the pairing read; toolCallSummaryHandler (handlers.ts:98-105) stamps outcome from that unfiltered read, so a tool_call_summary requeued after its paired result is deleted rebuilds outcome 'succeeded' from a record no longer in the readable record (against AC-2.4's no-paired-result→unknown and AC-6.1); cascadeMessageDelete (cascade.ts:209-215) drops the deleted message's own forms and clears upward only, never touching the paired counterpart's summary; and compose.ts:150-153 prefers the ready summary's stale metadata over its own mechanical outcomeFromRecord fallback, so the delete cascade's own rendering rebuild republishes the stale outcome. This partially invalidates reviewer-1's cross-story claim that the deleted-read filter is applied at every read site with only sanctioned exceptions. There is genuine spec tension behind the cascade half — AC-6.2's 'nothing else changes' excludes the counterpart summary from the cascade while AC-2.8 establishes the pair as the summary's source — carried as an unresolved item needing a human ruling; the missing read filter is an unambiguous defect regardless of that ruling. Reviewer-1's remaining non-blocking findings (E02-NB-001 wall-clock in mutations confirmed at five runInTransaction(db, () => new Date()) sites; E02-NB-003 deterministic-only registry confirmed in providers/registry.ts; E02-NB-004 thrown-handler-to-retryable confirmed at scheduler.ts:139-145; E02-NB-005 attempts asymmetry confirmed at scheduler.ts:119-125 vs 158-165) are all supported and retained. Epic gate re-run independently: pnpm run verify-all exit 0 (build, typecheck, lint, boundaries, 29 test files, 231 tests) — a passing gate does not offset the confirmed blockers, since the missing coverage (cross-SDK mode isolation, delete of a paired tool result) is exactly why the suite stays green.\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Confirmed: manual/background mode isolation does not survive SDK sequencing within one process. Background-mode construction installs process-global scheduler poke and thread-touch seams (sdk.ts:254-257, shared/context.ts:40-48) that a later manual-mode SDK never clears, and every enqueue unconditionally fires the global poke post-commit (work-queue/index.ts:136), so work queued through a manual SDK drains automatically through the leftover background scheduler — with that scheduler's provider and config — without any drain call.\",\"Confirmed: the deletion flow does not compose with paired tool-call/tool-result derivation. The pairing read crosses the deleted-read filter discipline (findPairedBlock has no deleted_at filter), the delete cascade never clears the paired counterpart's tool_call_summary even though AC-2.8 makes the pair the summary's source, and turn-rendering composition (compose.ts:150-153) trusts the stale ready summary's metadata over its own record-derived fallback — so a deleted tool result's outcome survives into rebuilt renderings and even into an explicit post-delete requeue of the summary.\",\"The story chain otherwise composes into one coherent mechanism: enqueue is the single creation point for derived_form rows, completion is UPDATE-only and source-version-checked, handlers return form writes as data, report/requeue join live work_item rows, and all three mutations reuse the identical enqueue/supersede/version machinery through the one shared cascade module (DD-8), with turns.deleteTurn reaching it only via the messages domain's public surface.\",\"The deleted-read filter rule is applied at the membership and read-back sites introduced across Stories 3-6 (message reads, member projections, chunk rows, turn reads), but reviewer-1's claim that every read site complies with only sanctioned exceptions is corrected by the confirmed blocker: the call-id pairing read is an unfiltered read of message content that the tech design's two-exception list does not sanction.\",\"Work-item identity (w-<sourceId>-<kind>-v<sourceVersion>), the DD-1 five-disposition contract, and the DD-3 stale-discard truth table hold consistently across intake queueing, drain, repair requeues, and the mutation cascade's replacement enqueues.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Confirmed drift from the architecture contract: mode selection is declared per SDK instance (DD-4: hosts see mode at construction) but enforced through process-global mutable hooks, so the mode contract is only as strong as the last background construction in the process; manual mode's AC-1.7 guarantee is not enforceable by the manual instance itself. The fix needs a small design decision — clear the slots on manual construction, scope the seams per SDK instance, or refuse multi-SDK construction — though all variants are mechanically small.\",\"Confirmed: the deleted-read filter discipline (tech design Part 3b) misses the tool pairing read path, and the mutation cascade's scope (derived structurally from the message→turn→chunk walk in cascade.ts) cannot reach the paired counterpart's summary, which the derivation architecture (AC-2.8, outcome stamping from the pair) makes a real source dependency. The epic's own cascade-scope table ('nothing else changes') conflicts with the pair-as-source model AC-2.8 introduced — a spec-level gap, not just an implementation one.\",\"Module placement otherwise matches the tech design with two approved, recorded renames (turn handlers in turns/internal/derive.ts; scheduler seams in shared/context.ts to avoid an import cycle, DD-5 semantics preserved); migration v5 implements the schema faithfully including the F-02 backfill; claimNext is the single atomic UPDATE under BEGIN IMMEDIATE with structural never-skip-ahead; provider calls never run inside a transaction; the DD-9 chunk close policy reads only stored projected-token values, which is what makes TC-3.9 replay determinism hold.\",\"Minor drift retained from reviewer-1: createSdk's injected clock governs drain and scheduler timestamps, but mutation and requeue operations construct their own wall clock (five runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), ...) sites in messages/index.ts and turns/index.ts), so deterministic time injection does not extend to the mutation surfaces (E02-NB-001).\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Epic gate independently re-run for this canonical review: pnpm run verify-all from packages/lhc exits 0 — build, typecheck, lint (75 files), boundary check, and 29 test files / 231 tests all green, including the LHC_PROCESS_SUITE spawned-process fixtures (TC-1.3 SIGKILL restart survival, TC-1.4 cross-process claim exclusion).\",\"All 46 TC ids appear verbatim in test titles and all 47 ACs trace to implemented behavior per reviewer-1's file-level audit; the four architecture-risk tests named by the test plan (TC-1.3, TC-1.4, TC-5.4, TC-3.9) are present and green; CLI parity surfaces call the same domain operations with the same validation and result JSON.\",\"Two coverage gaps correspond exactly to the confirmed blockers: no test constructs a background SDK followed by a manual SDK in one process (the AC-1.7 isolation case), and no test deletes or edits a tool result whose paired call summary already landed (the AC-2.4/AC-6.2 pairing case). Both blockers' fix paths must add these tests.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapters, stubs, placeholders, or silent provider defaults: CLI drain requires --provider or LHC_PROVIDER and fails closed with provider_not_configured; the deterministic provider is explicit-only per DD-11 and is currently the sole registered named provider (real adapters are an explicit epic scope exclusion — operators need a future adapter registration for real inference; E02-NB-003).\",\"Material production-path issue confirmed: in any process that ever constructed a background SDK, a subsequently constructed manual SDK silently behaves as background — its enqueues drain through the stale scheduler with the prior SDK's provider and config (EPIC-02-BLOCK-001).\",\"Material production-path issue confirmed: the tool pairing read returns deleted messages, so production drains and explicit requeues can land ready forms whose mechanically stamped outcomes derive from records outside the readable record (EPIC-02-BLOCK-002).\",\"Test seams compiled into production modules (intake walk hook/clock, scheduler testPassCount) are inert in production assembly and documented in place; background scheduling is gated fail-closed on hasAnyHandler; thrown handler errors are deliberately softened to retryable attempts to keep the queue from wedging (scheduler.ts:139-145, E02-NB-004).\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EPIC-02-BLOCK-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Manual SDK mode can auto-drain after background SDK construction in the same process\",\"evidence\":\"Confirmed in code (and dynamically by epic-reviewer-2; reviewer-1 independently found the same defect as E02-NB-002). createSdk installs the process-wide seams only for background mode and manual mode leaves them installed (packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:254-257: installSchedulerPoke / setThreadTouch under `if (resolved.mode === \\\"background\\\")`, with the comment documenting only background-supersedes-background); the slots are module globals nothing else clears (packages/lhc/src/shared/context.ts:40-48); enqueue unconditionally registers ctx.onCommit(() => fireSchedulerPoke(ctx.threadId)) (packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts:136); the background scheduler responds to the poke by draining (packages/lhc/src/scheduler.ts:315-319). Result: after `createSdk({mode:\\\"background\\\"})` then `createSdk({mode:\\\"manual\\\"})`, work queued via the manual SDK runs without any drain call, through the stale scheduler's provider and config — violating AC-1.7 ('queued work accumulates durably and does not run until the drain operation is invoked'). Reviewer-2 reproduced it end-to-end: w-m1-prompt_smoothing-v1 queued via the manual SDK drained with no manual drain invocation. Retained blocking per the conservative rule: the code confirms rather than disproves the blocker; assumption A3 narrows real-world exposure but the design itself contemplates multiple SDK constructions per process.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/context.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/scheduler.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.7\",\"DD-4\",\"DD-5\",\"tech-design.md Flow 1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EPIC-02-BLOCK-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Deleted tool results still determine tool-call outcomes through the unfiltered pairing read and an uncascaded counterpart summary\",\"evidence\":\"Confirmed in code at every step of reviewer-2's claimed path. (1) findPairedBlock joins message with no deleted_at IS NULL (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts:163-178) — an unsanctioned exception to tech design Part 3b's deleted-read filter rule, which names exactly two exceptions (event read-back, mutation validation's filtered existence check), not the pairing read. (2) toolCallSummaryHandler stamps the summary's outcome from that read (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts:98-105), so an explicit requeue of tool_call_summary after the paired tool_result is deleted rebuilds outcome 'succeeded' from a record no longer in the readable record — against AC-2.4's mechanical rule (no paired result → unknown) read with AC-6.1 (a deleted message no longer appears in reads). (3) cascadeMessageDelete drops the deleted message's own forms and clears only upward (turn, chunk) — the paired call's summary on a different message is never cleared (packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts:209-215). (4) Composition prefers the ready summary's stale metadata over its own record-derived outcome fallback (packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts:150-153), so the delete cascade's own turn-rendering rebuild republishes the stale 'succeeded' while the rendering's membership correctly excludes the deleted result. The read-filter half is an unambiguous defect; the cascade half sits on a spec conflict between AC-6.2's 'nothing else changes' and AC-2.8's pair-as-source rule, carried as an unresolved item for a ruling.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.4\",\"AC-2.8\",\"AC-6.1\",\"AC-6.2\",\"tech-design.md Part 3b deleted-read filter rule\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"E02-NB-001\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Mutation and requeue operations bypass the SDK-injected clock\",\"evidence\":\"Confirmed: five sites call runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), threadId, ...) — messages/index.ts:331, 421, 503 and turns/index.ts:356, 433 — so deleted_at stamps and requeued items' queuedAt use wall time regardless of SdkConfig.clock, which governs only drain/scheduler paths. Deterministic time injection does not extend to the mutation surfaces.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"DD-7\",\"AC-5.1\",\"AC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E02-NB-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Deterministic provider is the only registered production provider\",\"evidence\":\"Confirmed: src/providers/registry.ts registers exactly one name ('deterministic'). Real adapters are explicitly out of epic scope and DD-11 sanctions the double's registry placement with no default, so this is by design — but until a real adapter lands, lhc work drain in production can only produce marked deterministic artifacts, selected by explicit operator opt-in.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/providers/registry.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/providers/deterministic.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"DD-11\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E02-NB-004\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Thrown handler errors are converted to retryable attempts\",\"evidence\":\"Confirmed at scheduler.ts:139-145: drainOpenDb catches a throwing handler and routes it through failAttempt as { retryable: true }, consuming retry budget before landing failed. The error contract says bugs throw and are not contract outcomes; this deliberately softens that to protect the queue from wedging (documented in place). Reasonable trade-off, but a deterministic handler bug is retried twice before surfacing.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/scheduler.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E02-NB-005\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Inconsistent attempts accounting between terminal paths\",\"evidence\":\"Confirmed: the unknown-kind terminal path stamps attempts: item.attempts (scheduler.ts:119-125) while the blocked-source terminal path stamps attempts: item.attempts + 1 (scheduler.ts:159-165). Cosmetic — the value only feeds the drain report and the form's failure metadata, and unknown-kind items never ran a handler — but the asymmetry is undocumented.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/scheduler.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.8\",\"AC-1.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Cascade contract ruling needed for paired tool-call/tool-result dependencies: AC-6.2's exhaustive cascade scope ('nothing else changes') conflicts with AC-2.8's pair-as-source model. Decide whether deleting (or editing) one half of a call/result pair must clear and requeue the counterpart's summary, and update the epic's cascade-scope table either way. The findPairedBlock deleted-read filter fix is unambiguous and should not wait on this ruling.\",\"Design ruling needed on the mode-isolation fix shape for EPIC-02-BLOCK-001: clear the process-global seams on manual-mode construction, scope the poke/touch seams per SDK instance, or refuse multi-SDK construction per process — all small, but the choice affects the documented multi-SDK semantics in sdk.ts.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"2d547875-7ffc-45f0-93a6-e3694e338243\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"The story chain composes into one coherent mechanism with no reimplementation across stories: enqueue (Story 0) is the single creation point for derived_form rows, completion is UPDATE-only and source-version-checked in the queue util (Story 1), handlers return form writes as data (Stories 2-3), report/requeue join the same live work_item rows (Story 4), and mutations reuse the identical enqueue/supersede/version machinery (Stories 5-6).\",\"DD-8's one-cascade rule held across stories: messages/internal/cascade.ts serves edit, message delete, and turn delete; turns.deleteTurn reaches it only through the messages domain's public surface (applyTurnDeleteCascade), and the boundary script confirms no cross-domain internal imports anywhere.\",\"The deleted-read filter rule is applied consistently at every read site introduced across Stories 3-6: readMessages, readMutableMessage, readMemberMessages, readMemberProjections, readChunkRows, readTurns (both membership and turn rows), and readMutableTurn all append deleted_at IS NULL; the two sanctioned exceptions (event read-back and the handlers' readMessageSource) are deliberate and documented in place.\",\"Drain report dispositions match DD-1's five-disposition contract exactly across the scheduler, queue util, and mutation results: done/stale_discarded/failed_terminal appear only in drain reports, superseded appears only on MutationResult, and terminal rows are deleted in the same transaction that records their outcome.\",\"Work-item identity (w-<sourceId>-<kind>-v<sourceVersion>) is honored consistently by intake queueing, the AC-2.8 late-result requeue, both owners' repair requeues, and the mutation cascade's replacement enqueues, so the DD-3 stale-discard truth table holds at every write path I traced.\",\"All implementation-time deviations are recorded and ruled in the team impl log (5 in Story 0, 7 in Story 1, 5 in Story 2, 3 in Story 3, the rejected-then-fixed AC-4.7 set in Story 4, 4 in Story 5, 2 in Story 6); I found no unrecorded drift between the code and the rulings.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Module placement matches the tech design with two approved, recorded renames: turn handlers live in turns/internal/derive.ts rather than handlers.ts (Story 3 ruling), and the scheduler poke/touch seams live in shared/context.ts rather than the scheduler module to avoid an import cycle (Story 0 ruling, DD-5 semantics preserved).\",\"Migration v5 implements the tech-design schema faithfully, including the F-02 backfill of pending form rows for pre-v5 queued items, plus the approved deviation that idx_work_item_queue omits rowid (SQLite forbids rowid in index definitions; claimNext's ORDER BY rowid preserves head-first semantics).\",\"claimNext is the single atomic UPDATE under BEGIN IMMEDIATE specified in Part 3b, with the head re-read classifying empty/in_flight/waiting and the reclaim CASE incrementing attempts; the never-skip-ahead rule is structural, not procedural.\",\"Provider calls never run inside a transaction: handlers receive openDb() for short reads, return form writes as data, and the queue util owns the completion transaction; the onApplied hook makes chunk placement and summary enqueues ride the same completion commit, so a crash leaves either a placed turn with queued summaries or nothing.\",\"The chunk close policy implements DD-9's accumulation rule (close at accumulated + incoming >= target with the incoming turn starting the next chunk, single turn >= max closes its own chunk, empty chunks always accept) over stored projected-token values only, which is what makes TC-3.9 replay determinism hold.\",\"The tech design said the boundary script would gain a scheduler allowed-import line; none was added because none is needed — scheduler.ts imports only domain public indexes, which the existing rules permit. The protection the design wanted exists; the specific mechanism was moot.\",\"Minor drift: createSdk's injected clock governs drain and scheduler timestamps, but the mutation and requeue operations construct their own wall clock (runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), ...)) for deleted_at and queuedAt stamps, so deterministic time injection does not extend to the mutation surfaces (see non-blocking finding E02-NB-001).\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Epic gate pnpm run verify-all passed from packages/lhc with exit 0: 29 test files, 231 tests, including the LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 spawned-process suite covering the architecture-risk fixtures (TC-1.3 SIGKILL restart survival, TC-1.4 cross-process claim exclusion).\",\"All 46 TC ids from the epic appear verbatim in test titles across the suites (TC-1.1 through TC-6.8, plus Epic 01's TC-2.9 kind-gate amendment), matching the test plan's file mapping; the suite grew from Epic 01's 118 tests to 231, exceeding the plan's 60-70 estimate.\",\"All 47 ACs trace to implemented behavior I read directly: queue execution and both host modes (scheduler.ts, work-queue), message derivation with mechanically stamped outcomes (handlers.ts, outcome.ts), turn composition with gap recording and deterministic chunking (derive.ts, compose.ts, chunks.ts), report/repair with blocked refusal and requeue idempotency (both owners' index.ts and forms.ts), and the three mutations with one-transaction cascade, supersede, and stale-write fencing (cascade.ts, store.ts).\",\"The four architecture-risk tests named by the test plan (TC-1.3, TC-1.4, TC-5.4, TC-3.9) are all present and green in the gate run.\",\"CLI parity is real: every SDK surface (drain, report, requeue, edit, delete message, delete turn) has a CLI command that calls the same domain operation with the same validation and result JSON, and the CLI drain assembles a manual-mode SDK through createSdk rather than an in-process shortcut.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapters, stubs, placeholders, or TODO/FIXME markers exist anywhere in src/; every handler, mutation, and read path is real execution against real SQLite state.\",\"The deterministic provider ships in production source (src/providers/deterministic.ts) and is registered in the production named-provider registry. This is explicitly sanctioned by DD-11 and an approved Story 1 ruling: it is selectable only by explicit name (--provider deterministic / LHC_PROVIDER=deterministic), is never a default, and exists so spawned-CLI tests exercise the production resolution seam. A drain without a resolvable provider fails with provider_not_configured naming the flag and env var — fail-closed, never a silent no-op.\",\"The deterministic provider is currently the ONLY registered named provider, so a production CLI drain can only produce marked deterministic artifacts today. This is consistent with the epic's explicit scope exclusion (real provider adapters are out of scope; this epic ships the seam and the double), but operators should understand real inference requires a future adapter registration.\",\"Test seams compiled into production modules: setIntakeWalkHook and setIntakeClock in intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts (Epic 01 carryover, set only through test fixtures, explicit-argument-wins), and Scheduler.testPassCount plus the passes counter in scheduler.ts (documented test-only observability, not API). All are inert in production assembly and documented in place; none fakes an execution path.\",\"Background-mode scheduling is gated fail-closed on hasAnyHandler so an empty handler map can never turn queued rows into failed_terminal; in the shipped assembly both domains register real handlers, so the gate is always open in production.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"E02-NB-001\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Mutation and requeue operations bypass the SDK-injected clock\",\"evidence\":\"messages.edit, messages.deleteMessage, messages.requeue, turns.requeue, and turns.deleteTurn all call runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), threadId, ...) — deleted_at stamps and requeued items' queuedAt use wall time regardless of SdkConfig.clock, which governs only drain/scheduler paths (and intake has its own setIntakeClock seam). Deterministic time injection therefore does not extend to the mutation surfaces.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"DD-7\",\"AC-5.1\",\"AC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E02-NB-002\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Process-global scheduler seams not cleared by a later manual-mode SDK\",\"evidence\":\"createSdk installs setSchedulerPoke/setThreadTouch only in background mode and a later background SDK supersedes an earlier one (documented), but a manual-mode SDK constructed after a background one leaves the previous background scheduler installed — enqueues through the manual SDK would still poke the stale scheduler and drain with the old provider/config. Low real-world impact under assumption A3 (one host per process), but the background-then-manual sequence is unhandled.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/context.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/scheduler.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"DD-4\",\"DD-5\",\"AC-1.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E02-NB-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Deterministic provider is the only registered production provider\",\"evidence\":\"src/providers/registry.ts registers exactly one name ('deterministic'). Real adapters are explicitly out of epic scope and DD-11 sanctions the double's registry placement with no default, so this is by design — but until a real adapter lands, lhc work drain in production can only produce marked deterministic artifacts, selected by explicit operator opt-in.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/providers/registry.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/providers/deterministic.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"DD-11\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E02-NB-004\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Thrown handler errors are converted to retryable attempts\",\"evidence\":\"drainOpenDb catches a throwing handler and routes it through failAttempt as { retryable: true }, consuming retry budget before landing failed. The error contract says bugs throw and are not contract outcomes; this deliberately softens that to protect the queue from wedging (documented in scheduler.ts). The trade-off is reasonable but means a deterministic handler bug is retried twice before surfacing.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/scheduler.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E02-NB-005\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Inconsistent attempts accounting between terminal paths\",\"evidence\":\"The blocked-source terminal path stamps attempts: item.attempts + 1 while the unknown-kind terminal path stamps attempts: item.attempts (scheduler.ts lines 119-125 vs 158-165). Cosmetic: the value only feeds the drain report and the form's failure metadata, and unknown-kind items never ran a handler, but the asymmetry is undocumented.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/scheduler.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.8\",\"AC-1.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},{\"resultId\":\"b59e7106-89be-4571-bcbb-10fe91a97a03\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Manual/background mode isolation is not preserved across SDK instances: a background SDK installs process-wide scheduler hooks and a later manual SDK does not clear them, so manual intake can drain automatically without an explicit drain call.\",\"Deletion flow does not fully compose with paired tool-call/tool-result derivation: deleted tool results are excluded from turn membership but can still be read by the pairing query, and stale tool-call summary metadata can survive into rebuilt turn renderings.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"SDK mode selection drifts from the architecture contract because scheduler execution is controlled through process-global mutable hooks instead of being isolated to the SDK instance that chose background mode.\",\"The deleted-read filter discipline misses the tool pairing read path, and the mutation cascade does not repair paired counterpart summaries even though Flow 2 makes the paired message a source dependency.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Both required gates pass, and the implemented stories have broad test coverage, but the coverage misses cross-SDK mode isolation and delete/edit cases where a tool-call summary depends on a paired tool result.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No silent fake provider default was found: CLI drain requires --provider or LHC_PROVIDER, and the deterministic provider is explicit-only.\",\"Material production-path issue found: manual mode can execute through a background scheduler left by a prior SDK in the same process.\",\"Material production-path issue found: tool pairing can read deleted messages and produce real ready forms with outcomes derived from deleted records.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EPIC-02-BLOCK-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Manual SDK mode can auto-drain after background SDK construction\",\"evidence\":\"Verified by constructing a background SDK, then a manual SDK in the same process, ingesting one prompt through the manual SDK, and observing the queued work disappear without calling manual drain: queuedImmediately contained w-m1-prompt_smoothing-v1, then queuedAfterWait was empty and a ready smoothed_prompt form existed. Code path: src/sdk.ts installs setSchedulerPoke and setThreadTouch for background mode but manual mode does not clear them; src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts fires the global scheduler poke on enqueue; src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts fires the global thread touch; src/scheduler.ts responds by draining.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/context.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/scheduler.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"epic.md AC-1.7\",\"tech-design.md DD-4\",\"tech-design.md Flow 1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EPIC-02-BLOCK-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Deleted tool results can still determine tool-call outcomes\",\"evidence\":\"Verified by creating a turn with a tool_call and paired tool_result, draining, deleting the tool_result, draining again, and observing rebuilt turn rendering metadata still report the tool_call outcome as succeeded even though the live membership no longer includes the result. Requeuing the tool_call_summary after deletion still rebuilt outcome succeeded. Code path: src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts findPairedBlock joins message without m.deleted_at IS NULL; src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts stamps tool_call_summary outcome from that pair; src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts trusts ready summary metadata; src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts clears the deleted message and upward turn forms but does not clear the paired counterpart summary.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"epic.md AC-2.4\",\"epic.md Flow 6\",\"06-message-turn-delete.md AC-6.2\",\"06-message-turn-delete.md DoD\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"The cascade contract needs a ruling or update for paired tool-call/tool-result dependencies: the current delete cascade description focuses on the deleted message's upward chain, while the derivation architecture makes the paired counterpart a real source dependency.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/epic/001-epic-review.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-11T08:00:05.082Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-11T08:12:20.828Z\"}\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:244:| TC-3.2 | Fail one prompt's smoothing past budget; close turn; drain | Rendering ready; contains raw prompt text; gap recorded `{message, smoothed_prompt}` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:288:Two Epic 02 changes touch Epic 01's exact assertions. Both amendments are **sanctioned in advance** — the red-manifest immutability gate requires regenerating `test/red-manifest.json` as an explicit step of the story that makes each change, recorded in its deviation notes:\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:400:        reason: \"recorded the two new Story 4 test files, following the per-story red-phase locking pattern\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:428:        - \"TC-4.2's risk-reminder mechanism (maxItems:1 + backoff 0) cannot stop a drain mid-retry: non-terminal failed attempts never count toward maxItems and a zero backoff makes the head immediately re-claimable. Implemented with frozen clock + non-zero backoff producing the identical observable contract; recorded in the story deviation table\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:429:        - \"Tech-design Flow 4 says requeue enqueues 'at the form's current source version' while this story's Test Mapping, TC-4.4, and Flow 3's rebuild rule all say the version increments; implemented increment (current + 1), recorded as a deviation flagged for spec wording cleanup\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:455:No older response entries are recorded yet.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:494:  summary: \"No prior bounded child response is recorded. The story requirements and test plan are sufficient to start the first implementation slice for report, requeue, blocked-state handling, CLI parity, and TC-4.1 through TC-4.7 coverage.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:547:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:548:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:598:Caller implication: Do not treat the run as advanced until evidence and ledger updates are durably recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/04-derivation-state-report-repair/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:603:Meaning: A terminal public outcome has been recorded separately from lifecycleState and the story-lead loop will not continue automatically.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:27:The `turns` derivation layer: turn rendering composed from message-level forms with recorded fallback gaps, lower-band projection, deterministic chunk close policy, and the two chunk summaries.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:40:- Chunk placement at turn derivation: a turn whose projection succeeded joins the open chunk, placement recorded with the turn; when accumulated projected size plus the incoming turn's would cross the close target, the chunk closes *without* the incoming turn, which starts the next chunk (AC-3.6); a single turn whose projection alone meets the max forms its own chunk immediately (AC-3.7)\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:54:  - **TC-3.2** (AC-3.2): Close a turn where one prompt's smoothing failed → rendering `ready`, contains that message's raw content, other forms composed, gap recorded naming the message and form.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:59:- **AC-3.5**: A turn whose lower-band projection succeeded joins the open chunk; placement is recorded with the turn and readable through `turns`.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:75:The `turns` derivation layer, and the epic's biggest single handler: `turn_derivation` composes the rendering from message-level forms (`compose.ts`: ready forms verbatim; non-ready fall back to raw/truncated content, one gap recorded per fallback; consecutive tool activity grouped into outcome-explicit run accounts), sends it through `composeTurnRendering` then `projectLowerBand`, lands both as turn forms — then placement runs *in the completion transaction*: append to the open chunk, close on the accumulated policy (DD-9), and closing enqueues both summary kinds as separate items with independent lifecycles.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:77:Two invariants govern: **gaps are recorded facts, not live links** (AC-3.3 — a repaired dependency changes nothing until the dependent is explicitly rebuilt; this is the no-auto-cascade rule the epic's reviewers converged on), and **placement is pure arithmetic** (DD-9 — close decisions from stored projected token counts only, so identical streams re-chunk identically, AC-3.9). The close rule: when accumulated + incoming would cross the target, the chunk closes *without* the incoming turn, which opens the next chunk; a single projection ≥ max forms its own chunk. This is the v1 bug's fix — the MVP checked only the incoming turn's size, so small turns accumulated forever.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:137:**Dependency Gap contract** (epic Data Contracts): recorded on the composed artifact at derivation time; names the source record (messageId or turnId) and the form that fell back; the artifact is `ready` and usable. Lifecycle: created with the composition, persists through dependency repair (no auto-cascade — AC-3.3's no-silent-rebuild rule), cleared only by explicit rebuild of the gapped artifact (Flow 4 re-queue or mutation cascade).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:244:| TC-3.2 | Fail one prompt's smoothing past budget; close turn; drain | Rendering ready; contains raw prompt text; gap recorded `{message, smoothed_prompt}` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:288:Two Epic 02 changes touch Epic 01's exact assertions. Both amendments are **sanctioned in advance** — the red-manifest immutability gate requires regenerating `test/red-manifest.json` as an explicit step of the story that makes each change, recorded in its deviation notes:\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:321:- current_summary: Caller ruling recorded and story-lead finalization is resuming.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:450:    planSummary: \"Implemented the turns derivation layer (Story 3, TC-3.1–3.9). Added a completion-transaction hook to the work-queue util (complete() gains an optional onApplied callback invoked inside the completion's BEGIN IMMEDIATE, only when the version-checked form writes hit, with onCommit registrations flushed post-commit) so chunk placement and the close→summary enqueues ride the same commit as the rendering/projection writes — the story's placement-atomicity requirement — while the util stays domain-blind. New turns-internal modules: compose.ts (pure (messages, forms) → {parts, gaps}: ready forms verbatim, non-ready fall back to raw/truncated content with one DependencyGap per fallback, tool parts carry mechanically derived outcomes in message order so a run's outcome structurally cannot be lost), chunks.ts (placeTurn with the DD-9 accumulated close policy — close when accumulated + incoming ≥ target excluding the incoming turn, single projection ≥ max self-chunks immediately, empty chunks never close, already-placed turns keep their placement on rebuild — plus enqueueChunkSummaries and placement read-back), forms.ts (deleted-filtered turn/member/form/projection reads), derive.ts (turn_derivation handler: compose → composeTurnRendering → projectLowerBand → two form writes + placement hook with estimateTokens computed exactly once at landing; chunk_summary_detailed/brief handlers reading member projections in member_idx order). Registered turns.workHandlers; turn read-back now carries chunkId/memberIdx. Gaps are recorded facts: repair of a dependency changes nothing (TC-3.3 byte-equal assertion); explicit re-queues in tests drive the queue util directly per the story note.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:738:        reason: \"Re-recorded for the revised derivation-turns suite per the sanctioned procedure\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:764:        - \"Receipt account text reflects what composition used: a tool form that fell back at rendering time yields a truncated-fallback account in the receipt, consistent with the gap-as-recorded-fact rule — an explicit rebuild restates receipts from current form states.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:770:      - \"test/red-manifest.json re-recorded for the revised derivation-turns.test.ts (the suite this follow-up explicitly amends), per the F-03 regenerate-and-note procedure.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:798:currentSummary: \"Caller ruling recorded and story-lead finalization is resuming.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:915:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:916:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:993:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:994:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:1124:Caller implication: Do not treat the run as advanced until evidence and ledger updates are durably recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:1129:Meaning: A terminal public outcome has been recorded separately from lifecycleState and the story-lead loop will not continue automatically.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:243:| TC-3.2 | Fail one prompt's smoothing past budget; close turn; drain | Rendering ready; contains raw prompt text; gap recorded `{message, smoothed_prompt}` |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:287:Two Epic 02 changes touch Epic 01's exact assertions. Both amendments are **sanctioned in advance** — the red-manifest immutability gate requires regenerating `test/red-manifest.json` as an explicit step of the story that makes each change, recorded in its deviation notes:\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:320:- current_summary: Caller ruling recorded and story-lead finalization is resuming.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:472:        reason: \"recorded the two new test files' hashes (green may add files; the record step locks them)\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:707:currentSummary: \"Caller ruling recorded and story-lead finalization is resuming.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:823:  type: \"story-lead-self-note-recorded\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:824:  summary: \"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:1020:Caller implication: Do not treat the run as advanced until evidence and ledger updates are durably recorded.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:1025:Meaning: A terminal public outcome has been recorded separately from lifecycleState and the story-lead loop will not continue automatically.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/001-events.jsonl:4:{\"storyRunId\":\"04-turn-state-machine-story-run-001\",\"sequence\":4,\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-10T14:19:51.232Z\",\"type\":\"story-lead-self-note-recorded\",\"summary\":\"Story-lead recorded a durable self-note for a future planner turn.\",\"data\":{\"note\":\"After implementation, require verifier evidence and the configured story gate before considering acceptance.\",\"actionSequence\":3,\"actionType\":\"run-implement\",\"turn\":1}}\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/001-events.jsonl:6:{\"storyRunId\":\"04-turn-state-machine-story-run-001\",\"sequence\":6,\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-10T14:24:09.015Z\",\"type\":\"child-operation-failed\",\"summary\":\"story-implement returned a failed runtime envelope before producing a recoverable child result.\",\"artifact\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/001-final-package.json\",\"data\":{\"terminalDecision\":\"interrupted\",\"recoveryBoundary\":{\"smallestSafeStep\":\"resume-current-attempt\",\"reasoning\":\"The attempt was interrupted and recorded a terminal recovery package, so the safest replay point is the current durable story-run snapshot.\",\"validArtifactPaths\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/001-story-validate.json\"],\"requiresFreshStoryLeadSession\":false,\"requiresFreshChildProviderSession\":false},\"command\":\"story-implement\",\"outcome\":\"blocked\",\"status\":\"blocked\",\"errors\":[{\"code\":\"PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE\",\"message\":\"Provider execution failed for claude-code.\"}],\"artifactPaths\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/003-implementor.json\"]}}\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/epic/fix-batch-002.md:5:- [ ] **Fix 1 (P2): Background backoff stall — scheduler never wakes for eligible_at.** In background mode, when a drain pass ends with `stoppedBecause: \"waiting\"`, schedule a wake at the report's `waitingUntil` (`setTimeout` clamped to a sane minimum) that runs through the existing single-flight/coalesce poke path. At most one pending wake per thread — a poke or newer wake replaces/clears the old timer; `unref()` the timer so it never keeps the process alive; clear timers on drainSettled completion paths and any dispose/shutdown. Manual mode unchanged: `waiting` stays a terminal drain outcome with no timers. Use the SDK clock seam for computing the delay where applicable (do not worsen recorded deviation E02-NB-001). Test: background SDK, backoffBaseMs ~25ms, provider fails retryably once then succeeds; await `drainSettled` with no external poke after the failure → form `ready`, attempts = 2, elapsed ≥ backoff delay; companion negative asserts no retry ran before `eligible_at`. Existing manual-mode waiting tests (work-execution.test.ts) stay as-is.\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/epic/fix-batch-002.md:6:- [ ] **Fix 2 (P2): Tool-run grouping in turn rendering (AC-3.4 / Story 3 anti-shim restoration).** In `composeRenderingInput` (src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts), group maximal runs of consecutive tool activity (tool_call/tool_result in record order, unbroken by prompts or assistant text; thinking and runtime notes do NOT break a run — record that decision in the story deviation table). Each run becomes ONE RenderingPart and ONE receipt: tools used, call count, per-call mechanical outcomes joined into a run-level account; mixed outcomes stay explicit (e.g. \"2 succeeded, 1 failed: <reason>\"), never collapsed into vague success. Outcomes remain record-derived from derived_form.metadata (mechanical stamping untouched); non-tool parts unchanged. Check src/providers/deterministic.ts join still produces sensible output with grouped parts; adjust only if the input contract changed shape. Tests: turn with prompt, call, result, call, result, text, call, result → exactly two tool-run parts (sizes 2 and 1), receipts outcome-explicit; rendering contains run accounts and does NOT contain one entry per tool message; add a mixed-outcome run case naming the failure. Ripple: confirm chunk-summary tests still pass after re-derivation (no recorded goldens exist; the double derives from input).\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/001-quick-fix.stdout.log:30:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_012UkgYmk1yDq3V8FVSMqPb8\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\timport { existsSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\n2\\timport { runInTransaction, type OperationContext } from \\\"../../shared/context.js\\\";\\n3\\timport type { FormKind, FormReportEntry, WorkHandler } from \\\"../../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\n4\\timport { storageFailure, type ErrorResult, type OpResult } from \\\"../../shared/errors.js\\\";\\n5\\timport {\\n6\\t  enqueue,\\n7\\t  hasLiveItem,\\n8\\t  listItems,\\n9\\t  type WorkItemRecord,\\n10\\t  type WorkKind,\\n11\\t} from \\\"../../tech-utils/work-queue/index.js\\\";\\n12\\timport type { EventKind, EventRecord } from \\\"../intake-stream/index.js\\\";\\n13\\timport {\\n14\\t  openThreadDatabase,\\n15\\t  resolveThreadRef,\\n16\\t  type ThreadRef,\\n17\\t} from \\\"../threads/index.js\\\";\\n18\\timport type { DerivedForm } from \\\"../../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\n19\\timport {\\n20\\t  findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary,\\n21\\t  readMessageFormRow,\\n22\\t  readMessageForms,\\n23\\t  reportMessageForms,\\n24\\t} from \\\"./internal/forms.js\\\";\\n25\\timport { messageWorkHandlers } from \\\"./internal/handlers.js\\\";\\n26\\timport { projectEvent } from \\\"./internal/project.js\\\";\\n27\\timport { cascadeFromMessage, type CascadeClear } from \\\"./internal/cascade.js\\\";\\n28\\timport {\\n29\\t  applyMessageEdit,\\n30\\t  insertMessage,\\n31\\t  readMessages,\\n32\\t  readMutableMessage,\\n33\\t} from \\\"./internal/store.js\\\";\\n34\\t\\n35\\texport type BlockType = \\\"text\\\" | \\\"tool_call\\\" | \\\"tool_result\\\";\\n36\\t\\n37\\texport interface Block {\\n38\\t  blockType: BlockType;\\n39\\t  content: Record<string, unknown>; // per-kind shape as projected, verbatim source content\\n40\\t}\\n41\\t\\n42\\texport interface MessageRecord {\\n43\\t  messageId: string;\\n44\\t  sourceEventOrder: number;\\n45\\t  kind: Exclude<EventKind, \\\"turn_end\\\">;\\n46\\t  blocks: Block[];\\n47\\t  tokenEstimate: number;\\n48\\t  actor: string;\\n49\\t  harness: string;\\n50\\t  turnId?: string;\\n51\\t  // The message's derived forms as stored (Epic 02 Story 2): present only\\n52\\t  // for messages that are derivation sources — kinds with no derivable form\\n53\\t  // carry no rows and no key (AC-2.7). Stored state returned verbatim,\\n54\\t  // never re-derived on read.\\n55\\t  forms?: DerivedForm[];\\n56\\t}\\n57\\t\\n58\\t// The event as the walk holds it after recording: the validated input plus\\n59\\t// its server-stamped order and timestamp.\\n60\\texport type RecordedEvent = EventRecord;\\n61\\t\\n62\\texport type MessageCreated = {\\n63\\t  messageId: string;\\n64\\t  kind: Exclude<EventKind, \\\"turn_end\\\">;\\n65\\t  // Carried for tool activity only: the pairing key the queue sites need —\\n66\\t  // tool_result projection runs the AC-2.8 late-result lookup against it.\\n67\\t  toolCallId?: string;\\n68\\t} | null;\\n69\\t\\n70\\t// Cross-domain surface, called by intake-stream inside the batch transaction\\n71\\t// (the first such call through the operation context; turns.applyEvent\\n72\\t// follows the pattern in Story 4). Synchronous and throwing by design: a\\n73\\t// projection failure propagates to the pipeline's catch and rejects the\\n74\\t// whole batch — recorded events without messages is the stranded state the\\n75\\t// transaction exists to prevent. Returns null for turn_end (no message).\\n76\\t// turnId is the membership stamp, settled by the pipeline before this call:\\n77\\t// the turn open *after* this event's transition (so a prompt belongs to the\\n78\\t// turn it just opened), or null in a gap — written once, never updated.\\n79\\texport function createFromEvent(\\n80\\t  ctx: OperationContext,\\n81\\t  event: RecordedEvent,\\n82\\t  turnId: string | null,\\n83\\t): MessageCreated {\\n84\\t  const projected = projectEvent(event);\\n85\\t  if (projected === null) return null;\\n86\\t  const kind = event.eventKind as Exclude<EventKind, \\\"turn_end\\\">;\\n87\\t  const messageId = `m${event.eventOrder}`;\\n88\\t  insertMessage(ctx.db, {\\n89\\t    messageId,\\n90\\t    sourceEventOrder: event.eventOrder,\\n91\\t    kind,\\n92\\t    tokenEstimate: projected.tokenEstimate,\\n93\\t    actor: event.actor,\\n94\\t    harness: event.harness,\\n95\\t    turnId,\\n96\\t    blocks: projected.blocks,\\n97\\t  });\\n98\\t  if (event.eventKind === \\\"tool_call\\\" || event.eventKind === \\\"tool_result\\\") {\\n99\\t    return { messageId, kind, toolCallId: event.payload.toolCallId };\\n100\\t  }\\n101\\t  return { messageId, kind };\\n102\\t}\\n103\\t\\n104\\t// The kind gate, exact by design: a prompt queues prompt_smoothing, a tool\\n105\\t// call queues tool_call_summary (Epic 02 Story 2's additive extension), a\\n106\\t// tool result queues tool_result_summary, nothing else queues anything —\\n107\\t// text, thinking, and note messages are not derivation sources (Epic 01\\n108\\t// AC-2.8/TC-2.9; Epic 02 AC-2.2/AC-2.7). Cross-domain surface, called by\\n109\\t// intake-stream inside the batch transaction for every recorded message, so\\n110\\t// the item commits (or rolls back) with the batch.\\n111\\tconst MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS: Partial<Record<EventKind, WorkKind>> = {\\n112\\t  user_prompt: \\\"prompt_smoothing\\\",\\n113\\t  tool_call: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n114\\t  tool_result: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n115\\t};\\n116\\t\\n117\\t// Which derived form each message-owned kind produces — the owning domain's\\n118\\t// knowledge, handed to the meaning-blind enqueue so the form's pending row\\n119\\t// rides the same transaction (DD-5).\\n120\\tconst MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS: Partial<Record<WorkKind, FormKind>> = {\\n121\\t  prompt_smoothing: \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\",\\n122\\t  tool_call_summary: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n123\\t  tool_result_summary: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n124\\t};\\n125\\t\\n126\\t// Message-owned work handlers, merged into the SDK's dispatch map at\\n127\\t// construction (DD-6): prompt smoothing and the two tool-activity summaries.\\n128\\texport const workHandlers: Readonly<Partial<Record<WorkKind, WorkHandler>>> =\\n129\\t  messageWorkHandlers;\\n130\\t\\n131\\texport function queueMessageWork(\\n132\\t  ctx: OperationContext,\\n133\\t  message: MessageCreated,\\n134\\t): WorkItemRecord[] {\\n135\\t  if (message === null) return [];\\n136\\t  const items: WorkItemRecord[] = [];\\n137\\t  const kind = MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS[message.kind];\\n138\\t  if (kind !== undefined) {\\n139\\t    const form = MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS[kind];\\n140\\t    if (form === undefined) {\\n141\\t      // Every queuing kind names its form above; a miss is a wiring bug.\\n142\\t      throw new Error(`no derived form mapped for message work kind ${kind}`);\\n143\\t    }\\n144\\t    items.push(\\n145\\t      enqueue(ctx, {\\n146\\t        owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n147\\t        kind,\\n148\\t        sourceRef: { messageId: message.messageId },\\n149\\t        forms: [{ subjectKind: \\\"message\\\", subjectId: message.messageId, form }],\\n150\\t      }),\\n151\\t    );\\n152\\t  }\\n153\\t  // Late-result repair (AC-2.8): a tool result landing after its call's\\n154\\t  // summary already derived with outcome \\\"unknown\\\" means the summary's\\n155\\t  // source — the call+result pair — completed underneath it; clear and\\n156\\t  // regenerate at the next source version, in this same batch transaction.\\n157\\t  // One indexed lookup; pending summaries (metadata NULL) never match, so\\n158\\t  // the common call-and-result-in-one-batch case never triggers, and the\\n159\\t  // version-scoped item id keeps the requeue idempotent.\\n160\\t  if (message.kind === \\\"tool_result\\\" && message.toolCallId !== undefined) {\\n161\\t    const stale = findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary(ctx.db, message.toolCallId);\\n162\\t    if (stale !== undefined) {\\n163\\t      items.push(\\n164\\t        enqueue(ctx, {\\n165\\t          owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n166\\t          kind: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n167\\t          sourceRef: { messageId: stale.messageId },\\n168\\t          sourceVersion: stale.sourceVersion + 1,\\n169\\t          forms: [\\n170\\t            {\\n171\\t              subjectKind: \\\"message\\\",\\n172\\t              subjectId: stale.messageId,\\n173\\t              form: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n174\\t            },\\n175\\t          ],\\n176\\t        }),\\n177\\t      );\\n178\\t    }\\n179\\t  }\\n180\\t  return items;\\n181\\t}\\n182\\t\\n183\\tfunction threadNotFound(filePath: string): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n184\\t  return {\\n185\\t    ok: false,\\n186\\t    error: {\\n187\\t      errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n188\\t      code: \\\"thread_not_found\\\",\\n189\\t      reason: `no thread file exists at ${filePath}`,\\n190\\t    },\\n191\\t  };\\n192\\t}\\n193\\t\\n194\\texport async function listMessages(\\n195\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n196\\t): Promise<OpResult<MessageRecord[]>> {\\n197\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n198\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n199\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n200\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n201\\t\\n202\\t  // openThreadDatabase verifies the file is a real thread file and migrates\\n203\\t  // a pre-Story-3 one before the read, so a thread recorded under an earlier\\n204\\t  // story lists cleanly (F-03-001) and a non-thread file is rejected\\n205\\t  // unmutated (F-03-002).\\n206\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n207\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n208\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n209\\t  try {\\n210\\t    // Form read-back rides the message read (AC-2.1): each record carries\\n211\\t    // its stored derived forms, attached from one grouped query — the\\n212\\t    // production path for \\\"readable alongside the message\\\".\\n213\\t    const formsByMessage = readMessageForms(db);\\n214\\t    const records = readMessages(db).map((record) => {\\n215\\t      const forms = formsByMessage.get(record.messageId);\\n216\\t      return forms === undefined ? record : { ...record, forms };\\n217\\t    });\\n218\\t    return { ok: true, value: records };\\n219\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n220\\t    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n221\\t    return storageFailure(`message read-back failed: ${reason}`);\\n222\\t  } finally {\\n223\\t    db.close();\\n224\\t  }\\n225\\t}\\n226\\t\\n227\\texport async function listQueuedWork(\\n228\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n229\\t): Promise<OpResult<WorkItemRecord[]>> {\\n230\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n231\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n232\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n233\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n234\\t\\n235\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n236\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n237\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n238\\t  try {\\n239\\t    return { ok: true, value: listItems(db, \\\"messages\\\") };\\n240\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n241\\t    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n242\\t    return storageFailure(`queued-work read-back failed: ${reason}`);\\n243\\t  } finally {\\n244\\t    db.close();\\n245\\t  }\\n246\\t}\\n247\\t\\n248\\t// ── report and repair (Epic 02 Story 4, Flow 4) ──────────────────\\n249\\t\\n250\\t// This owner's repair report: every message-owned form's durable state\\n251\\t// joined with live queue detail in one query — the five operational\\n252\\t// situations (waiting, retrying, ready, failed, blocked) read from the rows\\n253\\t// without any queue API. Needs no provider; reads degrade, never block.\\n254\\texport async function report(\\n255\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n256\\t  opts?: { notReady?: boolean; messageId?: string },\\n257\\t): Promise<OpResult<FormReportEntry[]>> {\\n258\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n259\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n260\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n261\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n262\\t\\n263\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n264\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n265\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n266\\t  try {\\n267\\t    return { ok: true, value: reportMessageForms(db, opts ?? {}) };\\n268\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n269\\t    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n270\\t    return storageFailure(`report read failed: ${reason}`);\\n271\\t  } finally {\\n272\\t    db.close();\\n273\\t  }\\n274\\t}\\n275\\t\\n276\\texport type RequeueOutcome = { workItemId: string } | { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" };\\n277\\t\\n278\\t// Which work kind rebuilds each message-owned form — MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS\\n279\\t// inverted; the requeue's join from the named form back to its queue site.\\n280\\tconst MESSAGE_FORM_KINDS: Partial<Record<FormKind, WorkKind>> = {\\n281\\t  smoothed_prompt: \\\"prompt_smoothing\\\",\\n282\\t  tool_call_summary: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n283\\t  tool_result_summary: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n284\\t};\\n285\\t\\n286\\t// Explicit re-queue through the owning surface (AC-4.4): the public,\\n287\\t// supported rebuild act. Refused for blocked forms with the form's stored\\n288\\t// damage reason (AC-4.6) and for missing rows; a no-op against work already\\n289\\t// queued or in flight at the form's current source version (AC-4.5).\\n290\\t// Otherwise the form clears to pending and re-enqueues at the next source\\n291\\t// version — the same enqueue path intake uses, poke-on-commit included, so\\n292\\t// background mode processes the repair with no further call. The no-op check\\n293\\t// and the enqueue commit in one transaction (anti-shim: a split would\\n294\\t// reintroduce the duplicate-work race).\\n295\\texport async function requeue(\\n296\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n297\\t  target: { messageId: string; form: FormKind },\\n298\\t): Promise<OpResult<RequeueOutcome>> {\\n299\\t  const kind = MESSAGE_FORM_KINDS[target.form];\\n300\\t  if (kind === undefined) {\\n301\\t    return {\\n302\\t      ok: false,\\n303\\t      error: {\\n304\\t        errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n305\\t        code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n306\\t        reason: `form ${target.form} is not message-owned; messages.requeue repairs smoothed_prompt, tool_call_summary, tool_result_summary`,\\n307\\t      },\\n308\\t    };\\n309\\t  }\\n310\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n311\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n312\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n313\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n314\\t\\n315\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n316\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n317\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n318\\t  try {\\n319\\t    const meta = db\\n320\\t      .prepare(`SELECT thread_id FROM thread_metadata WHERE id = 1`)\\n321\\t      .get() as { thread_id: string } | undefined;\\n322\\t    const threadId = meta?.thread_id ?? \\\"\\\";\\n323\\t    return runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), threadId, (ctx): OpResult<RequeueOutcome> => {\\n324\\t      const row = readMessageFormRow(ctx.db, target.messageId, target.form);\\n325\\t      if (row === undefined) {\\n326\\t        return {\\n327\\t          ok: false,\\n328\\t          error: {\\n329\\t            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n330\\t            code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n331\\t            reason: `no derived form ${target.form} exists for message ${target.messageId}`,\\n332\\t          },\\n333\\t        };\\n334\\t      }\\n335\\t      if (row.state === \\\"blocked\\\") {\\n336\\t        // The refusal carries the form's stored reason — the damage named at\\n337\\t        // blocking time, not a generic string (AC-4.6).\\n338\\t        return {\\n339\\t          ok: false,\\n340\\t          error: {\\n341\\t            errorClass: \\\"state_corruption\\\",\\n342\\t            code: \\\"source_damaged\\\",\\n343\\t            reason: row.reason ?? `form ${target.form} for message ${target.messageId} is blocked`,\\n344\\t          },\\n345\\t        };\\n346\\t      }\\n347\\t      const sourceRef = { messageId: target.messageId };\\n348\\t      if (hasLiveItem(ctx.db, kind, sourceRef, row.sourceVersion)) {\\n349\\t        return { ok: true, value: { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" } };\\n350\\t      }\\n351\\t      const item = enqueue(ctx, {\\n352\\t        owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n353\\t        kind,\\n354\\t        sourceRef,\\n355\\t        sourceVersion: row.sourceVersion + 1,\\n356\\t        forms: [{ subjectKind: \\\"message\\\", subjectId: target.messageId, form: target.form }],\\n357\\t      });\\n358\\t      return { ok: true, value: { workItemId: item.workItemId } };\\n359\\t    });\\n360\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n361\\t    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n362\\t    return storageFailure(`requeue failed: ${reason}`);\\n363\\t  } finally {\\n364\\t    db.close();\\n365\\t  }\\n366\\t}\\n367\\t\\n368\\t// ── mutations (Epic 02 Story 5, Flow 5) ──────────────────────────\\n369\\t\\n370\\t// The mutation result contract (tech design §Interfaces): what changed in\\n371\\t// the record, which dependent forms cleared, which dropped (delete only),\\n372\\t// what replacement work queued, and which still-queued old items the cascade\\n373\\t// tidied away (issue 1). Shared by edit and the Story 6 deletes.\\n374\\texport interface MutationResult {\\n375\\t  changed: { messageIds: string[]; turnIds: string[] };\\n376\\t  cleared: CascadeClear[];\\n377\\t  dropped: CascadeClear[];\\n378\\t  queued: Array<{ workItemId: string; kind: WorkKind }>;\\n379\\t  superseded: string[];\\n380\\t}\\n381\\t\\n382\\t// The record's first sanctioned mutation (AC-5.1–5.5): change a closed-turn\\n383\\t// message's content and blocks, re-stamp the token estimate, and walk the\\n384\\t// full dependent chain — clear to pending, supersede queued old work,\\n385\\t// enqueue replacements at the next source version — in one transaction.\\n386\\t// Synchronous and local by contract: everything above commits before this\\n387\\t// returns; the re-queued rebuilds run through the normal drain (background\\n388\\t// mode needs no further call — the enqueue pokes ride the commit). Events\\n389\\t// are never touched (projection-level mutation, DD-12), and no generated\\n390\\t// thread-view is either — visibility arrives at the next compact/rebuild.\\n391\\t// Refusals read through the deleted-filtered view: an open-turn target is\\n392\\t// turn_open, a missing or deleted message is message_not_found, and a\\n393\\t// refusal changes nothing.\\n394\\texport async function edit(\\n395\\t  thread: ThreadRef,\\n396\\t  input: { messageId: string; content: string },\\n397\\t): Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>> {\\n398\\t  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n399\\t  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n400\\t  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n401\\t  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n402\\t\\n403\\t  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n404\\t  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n405\\t  const db = opened.value;\\n406\\t  try {\\n407\\t    const meta = db\\n408\\t      .prepare(`SELECT thread_id FROM thread_metadata WHERE id = 1`)\\n409\\t      .get() as { thread_id: string } | undefined;\\n410\\t    const threadId = meta?.thread_id ?? \\\"\\\";\\n411\\t    return runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), threadId, (ctx): OpResult<MutationResult> => {\\n412\\t      const target = readMutableMessage(ctx.db, input.messageId);\\n413\\t      if (target === undefined) {\\n414\\t        return {\\n415\\t          ok: false,\\n416\\t          error: {\\n417\\t            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n418\\t            code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n419\\t            reason: `no message ${input.messageId} exists in this thread`,\\n420\\t          },\\n421\\t        };\\n422\\t      }\\n423\\t      if (target.turnStatus === \\\"open\\\") {\\n424\\t        return {\\n425\\t          ok: false,\\n426\\t          error: {\\n427\\t            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n428\\t            code: \\\"turn_open\\\",\\n429\\t            reason: `message ${input.messageId} belongs to open turn ${target.turnId ?? \\\"\\\"}; open-turn messages cannot be edited (v1 boundary)`,\\n430\\t          },\\n431\\t        };\\n432\\t      }\\n433\\t      applyMessageEdit(ctx.db, input.messageId, input.content);\\n434\\t      const cascade = cascadeFromMessage(ctx, input.messageId);\\n435\\t      return {\\n436\\t        ok: true,\\n437\\t        value: {\\n438\\t          changed: { messageIds: [input.messageId], turnIds: [] },\\n439\\t          cleared: cascade.cleared,\\n440\\t          dropped: [],\\n441\\t          queued: cascade.queued,\\n442\\t          superseded: cascade.superseded,\\n443\\t        },\\n444\\t      };\\n445\\t    });\\n446\\t  } catch (cause) {\\n447\\t    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n448\\t    return storageFailure(`edit failed: ${reason}`);\\n449\\t  } finally {\\n450\\t    db.close();\\n451\\t  }\\n452\\t}\\n453\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"c1de3f50-133a-4f79-8a5b-672d328b384b\",\"uuid\":\"324f4dc4-32a1-497e-9e62-01a2db30d222\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-11T06:20:02.976Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\",\"content\":\"import { existsSync } from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\nimport { runInTransaction, type OperationContext } from \\\"../../shared/context.js\\\";\\nimport type { FormKind, FormReportEntry, WorkHandler } from \\\"../../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\nimport { storageFailure, type ErrorResult, type OpResult } from \\\"../../shared/errors.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  enqueue,\\n  hasLiveItem,\\n  listItems,\\n  type WorkItemRecord,\\n  type WorkKind,\\n} from \\\"../../tech-utils/work-queue/index.js\\\";\\nimport type { EventKind, EventRecord } from \\\"../intake-stream/index.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  openThreadDatabase,\\n  resolveThreadRef,\\n  type ThreadRef,\\n} from \\\"../threads/index.js\\\";\\nimport type { DerivedForm } from \\\"../../shared/derivation.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary,\\n  readMessageFormRow,\\n  readMessageForms,\\n  reportMessageForms,\\n} from \\\"./internal/forms.js\\\";\\nimport { messageWorkHandlers } from \\\"./internal/handlers.js\\\";\\nimport { projectEvent } from \\\"./internal/project.js\\\";\\nimport { cascadeFromMessage, type CascadeClear } from \\\"./internal/cascade.js\\\";\\nimport {\\n  applyMessageEdit,\\n  insertMessage,\\n  readMessages,\\n  readMutableMessage,\\n} from \\\"./internal/store.js\\\";\\n\\nexport type BlockType = \\\"text\\\" | \\\"tool_call\\\" | \\\"tool_result\\\";\\n\\nexport interface Block {\\n  blockType: BlockType;\\n  content: Record<string, unknown>; // per-kind shape as projected, verbatim source content\\n}\\n\\nexport interface MessageRecord {\\n  messageId: string;\\n  sourceEventOrder: number;\\n  kind: Exclude<EventKind, \\\"turn_end\\\">;\\n  blocks: Block[];\\n  tokenEstimate: number;\\n  actor: string;\\n  harness: string;\\n  turnId?: string;\\n  // The message's derived forms as stored (Epic 02 Story 2): present only\\n  // for messages that are derivation sources — kinds with no derivable form\\n  // carry no rows and no key (AC-2.7). Stored state returned verbatim,\\n  // never re-derived on read.\\n  forms?: DerivedForm[];\\n}\\n\\n// The event as the walk holds it after recording: the validated input plus\\n// its server-stamped order and timestamp.\\nexport type RecordedEvent = EventRecord;\\n\\nexport type MessageCreated = {\\n  messageId: string;\\n  kind: Exclude<EventKind, \\\"turn_end\\\">;\\n  // Carried for tool activity only: the pairing key the queue sites need —\\n  // tool_result projection runs the AC-2.8 late-result lookup against it.\\n  toolCallId?: string;\\n} | null;\\n\\n// Cross-domain surface, called by intake-stream inside the batch transaction\\n// (the first such call through the operation context; turns.applyEvent\\n// follows the pattern in Story 4). Synchronous and throwing by design: a\\n// projection failure propagates to the pipeline's catch and rejects the\\n// whole batch — recorded events without messages is the stranded state the\\n// transaction exists to prevent. Returns null for turn_end (no message).\\n// turnId is the membership stamp, settled by the pipeline before this call:\\n// the turn open *after* this event's transition (so a prompt belongs to the\\n// turn it just opened), or null in a gap — written once, never updated.\\nexport function createFromEvent(\\n  ctx: OperationContext,\\n  event: RecordedEvent,\\n  turnId: string | null,\\n): MessageCreated {\\n  const projected = projectEvent(event);\\n  if (projected === null) return null;\\n  const kind = event.eventKind as Exclude<EventKind, \\\"turn_end\\\">;\\n  const messageId = `m${event.eventOrder}`;\\n  insertMessage(ctx.db, {\\n    messageId,\\n    sourceEventOrder: event.eventOrder,\\n    kind,\\n    tokenEstimate: projected.tokenEstimate,\\n    actor: event.actor,\\n    harness: event.harness,\\n    turnId,\\n    blocks: projected.blocks,\\n  });\\n  if (event.eventKind === \\\"tool_call\\\" || event.eventKind === \\\"tool_result\\\") {\\n    return { messageId, kind, toolCallId: event.payload.toolCallId };\\n  }\\n  return { messageId, kind };\\n}\\n\\n// The kind gate, exact by design: a prompt queues prompt_smoothing, a tool\\n// call queues tool_call_summary (Epic 02 Story 2's additive extension), a\\n// tool result queues tool_result_summary, nothing else queues anything —\\n// text, thinking, and note messages are not derivation sources (Epic 01\\n// AC-2.8/TC-2.9; Epic 02 AC-2.2/AC-2.7). Cross-domain surface, called by\\n// intake-stream inside the batch transaction for every recorded message, so\\n// the item commits (or rolls back) with the batch.\\nconst MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS: Partial<Record<EventKind, WorkKind>> = {\\n  user_prompt: \\\"prompt_smoothing\\\",\\n  tool_call: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n  tool_result: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n};\\n\\n// Which derived form each message-owned kind produces — the owning domain's\\n// knowledge, handed to the meaning-blind enqueue so the form's pending row\\n// rides the same transaction (DD-5).\\nconst MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS: Partial<Record<WorkKind, FormKind>> = {\\n  prompt_smoothing: \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\",\\n  tool_call_summary: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n  tool_result_summary: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n};\\n\\n// Message-owned work handlers, merged into the SDK's dispatch map at\\n// construction (DD-6): prompt smoothing and the two tool-activity summaries.\\nexport const workHandlers: Readonly<Partial<Record<WorkKind, WorkHandler>>> =\\n  messageWorkHandlers;\\n\\nexport function queueMessageWork(\\n  ctx: OperationContext,\\n  message: MessageCreated,\\n): WorkItemRecord[] {\\n  if (message === null) return [];\\n  const items: WorkItemRecord[] = [];\\n  const kind = MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS[message.kind];\\n  if (kind !== undefined) {\\n    const form = MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS[kind];\\n    if (form === undefined) {\\n      // Every queuing kind names its form above; a miss is a wiring bug.\\n      throw new Error(`no derived form mapped for message work kind ${kind}`);\\n    }\\n    items.push(\\n      enqueue(ctx, {\\n        owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n        kind,\\n        sourceRef: { messageId: message.messageId },\\n        forms: [{ subjectKind: \\\"message\\\", subjectId: message.messageId, form }],\\n      }),\\n    );\\n  }\\n  // Late-result repair (AC-2.8): a tool result landing after its call's\\n  // summary already derived with outcome \\\"unknown\\\" means the summary's\\n  // source — the call+result pair — completed underneath it; clear and\\n  // regenerate at the next source version, in this same batch transaction.\\n  // One indexed lookup; pending summaries (metadata NULL) never match, so\\n  // the common call-and-result-in-one-batch case never triggers, and the\\n  // version-scoped item id keeps the requeue idempotent.\\n  if (message.kind === \\\"tool_result\\\" && message.toolCallId !== undefined) {\\n    const stale = findUnknownOutcomeCallSummary(ctx.db, message.toolCallId);\\n    if (stale !== undefined) {\\n      items.push(\\n        enqueue(ctx, {\\n          owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n          kind: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n          sourceRef: { messageId: stale.messageId },\\n          sourceVersion: stale.sourceVersion + 1,\\n          forms: [\\n            {\\n              subjectKind: \\\"message\\\",\\n              subjectId: stale.messageId,\\n              form: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n            },\\n          ],\\n        }),\\n      );\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return items;\\n}\\n\\nfunction threadNotFound(filePath: string): { ok: false; error: ErrorResult } {\\n  return {\\n    ok: false,\\n    error: {\\n      errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n      code: \\\"thread_not_found\\\",\\n      reason: `no thread file exists at ${filePath}`,\\n    },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport async function listMessages(\\n  thread: ThreadRef,\\n): Promise<OpResult<MessageRecord[]>> {\\n  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n\\n  // openThreadDatabase verifies the file is a real thread file and migrates\\n  // a pre-Story-3 one before the read, so a thread recorded under an earlier\\n  // story lists cleanly (F-03-001) and a non-thread file is rejected\\n  // unmutated (F-03-002).\\n  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n  const db = opened.value;\\n  try {\\n    // Form read-back rides the message read (AC-2.1): each record carries\\n    // its stored derived forms, attached from one grouped query — the\\n    // production path for \\\"readable alongside the message\\\".\\n    const formsByMessage = readMessageForms(db);\\n    const records = readMessages(db).map((record) => {\\n      const forms = formsByMessage.get(record.messageId);\\n      return forms === undefined ? record : { ...record, forms };\\n    });\\n    return { ok: true, value: records };\\n  } catch (cause) {\\n    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n    return storageFailure(`message read-back failed: ${reason}`);\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport async function listQueuedWork(\\n  thread: ThreadRef,\\n): Promise<OpResult<WorkItemRecord[]>> {\\n  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n\\n  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n  const db = opened.value;\\n  try {\\n    return { ok: true, value: listItems(db, \\\"messages\\\") };\\n  } catch (cause) {\\n    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n    return storageFailure(`queued-work read-back failed: ${reason}`);\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// ── report and repair (Epic 02 Story 4, Flow 4) ──────────────────\\n\\n// This owner's repair report: every message-owned form's durable state\\n// joined with live queue detail in one query — the five operational\\n// situations (waiting, retrying, ready, failed, blocked) read from the rows\\n// without any queue API. Needs no provider; reads degrade, never block.\\nexport async function report(\\n  thread: ThreadRef,\\n  opts?: { notReady?: boolean; messageId?: string },\\n): Promise<OpResult<FormReportEntry[]>> {\\n  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n\\n  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n  const db = opened.value;\\n  try {\\n    return { ok: true, value: reportMessageForms(db, opts ?? {}) };\\n  } catch (cause) {\\n    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n    return storageFailure(`report read failed: ${reason}`);\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport type RequeueOutcome = { workItemId: string } | { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" };\\n\\n// Which work kind rebuilds each message-owned form — MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS\\n// inverted; the requeue's join from the named form back to its queue site.\\nconst MESSAGE_FORM_KINDS: Partial<Record<FormKind, WorkKind>> = {\\n  smoothed_prompt: \\\"prompt_smoothing\\\",\\n  tool_call_summary: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\",\\n  tool_result_summary: \\\"tool_result_summary\\\",\\n};\\n\\n// Explicit re-queue through the owning surface (AC-4.4): the public,\\n// supported rebuild act. Refused for blocked forms with the form's stored\\n// damage reason (AC-4.6) and for missing rows; a no-op against work already\\n// queued or in flight at the form's current source version (AC-4.5).\\n// Otherwise the form clears to pending and re-enqueues at the next source\\n// version — the same enqueue path intake uses, poke-on-commit included, so\\n// background mode processes the repair with no further call. The no-op check\\n// and the enqueue commit in one transaction (anti-shim: a split would\\n// reintroduce the duplicate-work race).\\nexport async function requeue(\\n  thread: ThreadRef,\\n  target: { messageId: string; form: FormKind },\\n): Promise<OpResult<RequeueOutcome>> {\\n  const kind = MESSAGE_FORM_KINDS[target.form];\\n  if (kind === undefined) {\\n    return {\\n      ok: false,\\n      error: {\\n        errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n        code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n        reason: `form ${target.form} is not message-owned; messages.requeue repairs smoothed_prompt, tool_call_summary, tool_result_summary`,\\n      },\\n    };\\n  }\\n  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n\\n  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n  const db = opened.value;\\n  try {\\n    const meta = db\\n      .prepare(`SELECT thread_id FROM thread_metadata WHERE id = 1`)\\n      .get() as { thread_id: string } | undefined;\\n    const threadId = meta?.thread_id ?? \\\"\\\";\\n    return runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), threadId, (ctx): OpResult<RequeueOutcome> => {\\n      const row = readMessageFormRow(ctx.db, target.messageId, target.form);\\n      if (row === undefined) {\\n        return {\\n          ok: false,\\n          error: {\\n            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n            code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n            reason: `no derived form ${target.form} exists for message ${target.messageId}`,\\n          },\\n        };\\n      }\\n      if (row.state === \\\"blocked\\\") {\\n        // The refusal carries the form's stored reason — the damage named at\\n        // blocking time, not a generic string (AC-4.6).\\n        return {\\n          ok: false,\\n          error: {\\n            errorClass: \\\"state_corruption\\\",\\n            code: \\\"source_damaged\\\",\\n            reason: row.reason ?? `form ${target.form} for message ${target.messageId} is blocked`,\\n          },\\n        };\\n      }\\n      const sourceRef = { messageId: target.messageId };\\n      if (hasLiveItem(ctx.db, kind, sourceRef, row.sourceVersion)) {\\n        return { ok: true, value: { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" } };\\n      }\\n      const item = enqueue(ctx, {\\n        owner: \\\"messages\\\",\\n        kind,\\n        sourceRef,\\n        sourceVersion: row.sourceVersion + 1,\\n        forms: [{ subjectKind: \\\"message\\\", subjectId: target.messageId, form: target.form }],\\n      });\\n      return { ok: true, value: { workItemId: item.workItemId } };\\n    });\\n  } catch (cause) {\\n    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n    return storageFailure(`requeue failed: ${reason}`);\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// ── mutations (Epic 02 Story 5, Flow 5) ──────────────────────────\\n\\n// The mutation result contract (tech design §Interfaces): what changed in\\n// the record, which dependent forms cleared, which dropped (delete only),\\n// what replacement work queued, and which still-queued old items the cascade\\n// tidied away (issue 1). Shared by edit and the Story 6 deletes.\\nexport interface MutationResult {\\n  changed: { messageIds: string[]; turnIds: string[] };\\n  cleared: CascadeClear[];\\n  dropped: CascadeClear[];\\n  queued: Array<{ workItemId: string; kind: WorkKind }>;\\n  superseded: string[];\\n}\\n\\n// The record's first sanctioned mutation (AC-5.1–5.5): change a closed-turn\\n// message's content and blocks, re-stamp the token estimate, and walk the\\n// full dependent chain — clear to pending, supersede queued old work,\\n// enqueue replacements at the next source version — in one transaction.\\n// Synchronous and local by contract: everything above commits before this\\n// returns; the re-queued rebuilds run through the normal drain (background\\n// mode needs no further call — the enqueue pokes ride the commit). Events\\n// are never touched (projection-level mutation, DD-12), and no generated\\n// thread-view is either — visibility arrives at the next compact/rebuild.\\n// Refusals read through the deleted-filtered view: an open-turn target is\\n// turn_open, a missing or deleted message is message_not_found, and a\\n// refusal changes nothing.\\nexport async function edit(\\n  thread: ThreadRef,\\n  input: { messageId: string; content: string },\\n): Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>> {\\n  const resolved = await resolveThreadRef(thread);\\n  if (!resolved.ok) return resolved;\\n  const { filePath } = resolved.value;\\n  if (!existsSync(filePath)) return threadNotFound(filePath);\\n\\n  const opened = openThreadDatabase(filePath);\\n  if (!opened.ok) return opened;\\n  const db = opened.value;\\n  try {\\n    const meta = db\\n      .prepare(`SELECT thread_id FROM thread_metadata WHERE id = 1`)\\n      .get() as { thread_id: string } | undefined;\\n    const threadId = meta?.thread_id ?? \\\"\\\";\\n    return runInTransaction(db, () => new Date(), threadId, (ctx): OpResult<MutationResult> => {\\n      const target = readMutableMessage(ctx.db, input.messageId);\\n      if (target === undefined) {\\n        return {\\n          ok: false,\\n          error: {\\n            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n            code: \\\"message_not_found\\\",\\n            reason: `no message ${input.messageId} exists in this thread`,\\n          },\\n        };\\n      }\\n      if (target.turnStatus === \\\"open\\\") {\\n        return {\\n          ok: false,\\n          error: {\\n            errorClass: \\\"caller_error\\\",\\n            code: \\\"turn_open\\\",\\n            reason: `message ${input.messageId} belongs to open turn ${target.turnId ?? \\\"\\\"}; open-turn messages cannot be edited (v1 boundary)`,\\n          },\\n        };\\n      }\\n      applyMessageEdit(ctx.db, input.messageId, input.content);\\n      const cascade = cascadeFromMessage(ctx, input.messageId);\\n      return {\\n        ok: true,\\n        value: {\\n          changed: { messageIds: [input.messageId], turnIds: [] },\\n          cleared: cascade.cleared,\\n          dropped: [],\\n          queued: cascade.queued,\\n          superseded: cascade.superseded,\\n        },\\n      };\\n    });\\n  } catch (cause) {\\n    const reason = cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause);\\n    return storageFailure(`edit failed: ${reason}`);\\n  } finally {\\n    db.close();\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"numLines\":453,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":453}}}\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/001-quick-fix.stdout.log:103:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"signature_delta\",\"signature\":\"\"}},\"session_id\":\"c1de3f50-133a-4f79-8a5b-672d328b384b\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"8be5eda3-9717-4309-ba83-ca2777d2e947\"}\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/001-quick-fix.stdout.log:104:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_01K2eqHMRBUnwyTzVVYpfoyD\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":891,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":11290,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":35291,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":11290},\"output_tokens\":5,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"c1de3f50-133a-4f79-8a5b-672d328b384b\",\"uuid\":\"2378dda3-3b9f-4e7d-9550-7c4fd41eed2f\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CbvzHbeNFuuhBGd2eW49t\"}\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/001-quick-fix.stdout.log:198:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"signature_delta\",\"signature\":\"\"}},\"session_id\":\"c1de3f50-133a-4f79-8a5b-672d328b384b\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"9b5c3959-6ae0-4cb6-aaea-5a823a244dfc\"}\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/001-quick-fix.stdout.log:199:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_01B5MwTAEDgLaGWJHGYiSm7Y\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":6174,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":51975,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":6174},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"c1de3f50-133a-4f79-8a5b-672d328b384b\",\"uuid\":\"194f0fdc-7767-4dca-bfb9-b4742ff2a646\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CbvzK6eAFHEKYtf6mTYHv\"}\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/001-quick-fix.stdout.log:216:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_011Nuc53UmYxMfq8KBsmtAUj\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"233\\t  else idle\\n234\\t    SCH->>DR: start (unawaited)\\n235\\t  end\\n236\\t  loop until queue empty\\n237\\t    DR->>WQ: claimNext(db) — BEGIN IMMEDIATE, oldest queued, lease stamp\\n238\\t    DR->>H: handlers[kind](runCtx, item)\\n239\\t    H-->>DR: outcome\\n240\\t    DR->>WQ: complete / failAttempt — short txn, version-checked write\\n241\\t  end\\n242\\t  DR->>SCH: finished → rerun once if pending\\n243\\t```\\n244\\t\\n245\\tThe drain claims under `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` (claim is a write); runs the handler with **no open transaction** (provider call lives here); completes in a second short transaction. A drain finding the head item claimed with an unexpired lease stops with `stoppedBecause: \\\"in_flight\\\"` and processes nothing (AC-1.4); a head gated by backoff stops it with `\\\"waiting\\\"` — the never-skip-ahead rule in Part 3b governs both. Expired lease → reclaim: attempts increment, item runs again; the source-version check and idempotent artifact write make a double-run harmless (the first run's write either landed before reclaim — completing the item — or lands stale and discards). Lease default 120s (config), chosen >> p99 provider latency.\\n246\\t\\n247\\tRetry/backoff: budget 3 attempts (config). `failAttempt` under budget: status back to `queued`, `attempts++`, eligibility delayed by `min(2^attempts × 5s, 60s)` encoded as a `claim_expires_at`-style `eligible_at` check in `claimNext`'s WHERE. At budget: status `failed_terminal`, form → `failed` with the final reason (AC-1.9). Backoff values are config; tests set them to 0.\\n248\\t\\n249\\t**Flow 2 — Message-level derivation.** Handlers read the message row + blocks; tool-call summary additionally reads its paired result by `tool_call_id` (`outcome.ts` derives `succeeded | failed | unknown` mechanically from `isError`/presence — the provider's text never touches the outcome field, AC-2.4). The outcome lands in `derived_form.metadata`, not in `content`: machine-readable apart from provider text. Intake's `MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS` map gains `tool_call: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\"` (AC-2.2). The second intake touch is the late-result repair (AC-2.8): when projecting a `tool_result`, one indexed lookup — does a `tool_call_summary` form exist for the paired call with `metadata.outcome = \\\"unknown\\\"`? If so, requeue it in the batch transaction (the requeue no-op rule makes this idempotent). Both touches are deterministic and local. Forms land via `forms.ts` **UPDATE-only writes with the source-version check** (never upsert — the pending row exists from enqueue; a write that finds no matching row discards as stale).\\n250\\t\\n251\\t**Flow 3 — Turn composition and chunks.** `turn_derivation` handler: load member messages (deleted-filtered), collect their message-level forms, compose rendering (`compose.ts`) — ready forms verbatim, non-ready fall back to raw/truncated content **recording a gap per fallback** (AC-3.2); tool runs become outcome-explicit accounts grouped by consecutive tool activity (AC-3.4). Rendering → provider `composeTurnRendering`; projection → `projectLowerBand`. Both land as turn forms; placement then runs in the completion transaction: append to open chunk (`chunks.ts`), close on accumulated policy (DD-9), closing enqueues `chunk_summary_detailed` + `chunk_summary_brief` (two items, independent retry — AC-3.8) whose handlers read member projections and call their provider ops.\\n252\\t\\n253\\tGap semantics (AC-3.3): gaps are recorded facts on the landed artifact. A dependency later repairing does not touch dependents; `report` surfaces gapped artifacts; explicit `requeue` rebuilds (next source version, gaps recomputed from current dependency states).\\n254\\t\\n255\\t**Flow 4 — Report and repair.** `report(ref, { owner, notReady? })` is one query: `derived_form` LEFT JOIN live `work_item` rows for the subject's forms, exposing state + reason + gaps + queue detail (`attempts`, `last_error`, `eligible_at`). The five distinctions read: `pending` & no attempts = waiting; `pending` & attempts>0 = retrying; `ready`; `failed`; `blocked`. `requeue(ref, { subjectKind, subjectId, form })`: refused for `blocked` (with the blocking reason) and for missing rows; no-op if a live item already targets the form at its current source version (AC-4.5, one EXISTS check); otherwise enqueue at the form's current source version. Requeue of a `failed` form never collides with old work: the failed item's row was deleted at terminal transition (DD-1), and the deterministic id is scoped to the current source version.\\n256\\t\\n257\\t**Flows 5/6 — Mutations.** One transaction (`runInTransaction`): validate (exists via deleted-filtered read; turn closed; for message-delete: not turn-initiating — else `message_initiates_turn` naming the turn and the turns-delete path), apply record change (content+blocks+token re-stamp for edit; `deleted_at` stamp for deletes), run cascade (DD-8): bump source version + `pending` on cleared forms, drop forms whose subject is deleted (state rows removed — dropped, not failed, AC-6.6), supersede-delete still-queued old-version items (issue 1), enqueue replacements with target source version, register poke. Claimed old-version items may still finish; DD-3 discards their stale results because their source version no longer matches. Result reports changed/cleared/dropped/queued/superseded. Refusals: `turn_open`, `message_not_found`/`turn_not_found`, second delete of the same id → `message_not_found` by the filtered read (AC-6.7's \\\"refusal, not silent success\\\").\\n258\\t\\n259\\t---\\n260\\t\\n261\\t## Part 3: Interfaces\\n262\\t\\n263\\t```typescript\\n264\\t// ── shared/derivation.ts ─────────────────────────────────────────\\n265\\texport type FormKind =\\n266\\t  | \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\" | \\\"tool_call_summary\\\" | \\\"tool_result_summary\\\"\\n267\\t  | \\\"turn_rendering\\\" | \\\"lower_band_projection\\\"\\n268\\t  | \\\"chunk_summary_detailed\\\" | \\\"chunk_summary_brief\\\";\\n269\\t\\n270\\texport type DerivedFormState = \\\"pending\\\" | \\\"ready\\\" | \\\"failed\\\" | \\\"blocked\\\";\\n271\\t\\n272\\texport interface DependencyGap { subjectKind: \\\"message\\\" | \\\"turn\\\" | \\\"chunk\\\"; subjectId: string; form: FormKind; }\\n273\\t\\n274\\texport interface DerivedForm {\\n275\\t  subjectKind: \\\"message\\\" | \\\"turn\\\" | \\\"chunk\\\";\\n276\\t  subjectId: string;\\n277\\t  form: FormKind;\\n278\\t  state: DerivedFormState;\\n279\\t  content?: string;          // ready only\\n280\\t  reason?: string;           // failed | blocked\\n281\\t  sourceVersion: number;     // which version of the source this form derives from (DD-3)\\n282\\t  gaps?: DependencyGap[];    // composed forms; landed-with-fallback record\\n283\\t  metadata?: { outcome?: ToolOutcome };  // mechanically stamped fields; never provider-authored\\n284\\t  derivedAt?: string;\\n285\\t}\\n286\\t\\n287\\t// outcome on tool-activity summaries — mechanically stamped (AC-2.4)\\n288\\texport type ToolOutcome = \\\"succeeded\\\" | \\\"failed\\\" | \\\"unknown\\\";\\n289\\t\\n290\\t// ── provider seam (injected at createSdk) ────────────────────────\\n291\\texport type ProviderResult =\\n292\\t  | { ok: true; text: string }\\n293\\t  | { ok: false; retryable: boolean; reason: string };\\n294\\t\\n295\\texport interface DerivationProvider {\\n296\\t  smoothPrompt(i: { text: string }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n297\\t  summarizeToolCall(i: { toolName: string; argsJson: string;\\n298\\t    pairedResult?: { content: string; isError: boolean } }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n299\\t  summarizeToolResult(i: { toolName: string; content: string }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n300\\t  composeTurnRendering(i: { parts: RenderingPart[] }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n301\\t  projectLowerBand(i: { rendering: string }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n302\\t  summarizeChunkDetailed(i: { memberProjections: string[] }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n303\\t  summarizeChunkBrief(i: { memberProjections: string[] }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n304\\t}\\n305\\t\\n306\\texport interface RenderingPart {\\n307\\t  messageId: string;\\n308\\t  kind: EventKind;\\n309\\t  text: string;                    // ready form content, or raw/truncated fallback\\n310\\t  fallback: boolean;               // true ⇒ gap recorded\\n311\\t  outcome?: ToolOutcome;           // tool activity only\\n312\\t}\\n313\\t\\n314\\t// ── SDK assembly ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n315\\texport interface SdkConfig {\\n316\\t  provider: DerivationProvider;\\n317\\t  mode: \\\"background\\\" | \\\"manual\\\";\\n318\\t  clock?: () => Date;\\n319\\t  retry?: { budget: number; backoffBaseMs: number; backoffCapMs: number };   // 3 / 5000 / 60000\\n320\\t  lease?: { durationMs: number };                                            // 120000\\n321\\t  chunkPolicy?: { targetProjectedTokens: number; maxProjectedTokens: number }; // 2200 / 4400\\n322\\t}\\n323\\texport function createSdk(config: SdkConfig): Lhc;\\n324\\t\\n325\\texport interface Lhc {\\n326\\t  threads: /* Epic 01 surface, unchanged */;\\n327\\t  intakeStream: /* Epic 01 surface; tool_call now queues work */;\\n328\\t  messages: MessagesSurface;\\n329\\t  turns: TurnsSurface;\\n330\\t  work: WorkSurface;\\n331\\t  drainSettled(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<void>;   // issue 3: resolves when no running/pending drain (internal resolution to thread id)\\n332\\t}\\n333\\t\\n334\\t// ── work surface (CLI: lhc work …) ───────────────────────────────\\n335\\texport interface WorkSurface {\\n336\\t  drain(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { maxItems?: number }): Promise<OpResult<DrainReport>>;\\n337\\t}\\n338\\texport interface DrainReport {\\n339\\t  ran: Array<{ workItemId: string; kind: WorkKind; sourceRef: WorkSourceRef;\\n340\\t    disposition: \\\"done\\\" | \\\"failed_terminal\\\" | \\\"stale_discarded\\\";  // superseded never reaches a drain — cascade deletes + reports it on MutationResult\\n341\\t    attempts: number; reason?: string }>;\\n342\\t  stoppedBecause: \\\"empty\\\" | \\\"in_flight\\\" | \\\"waiting\\\" | \\\"max_items\\\";\\n343\\t  waitingUntil?: string;    // head's eligible_at when stoppedBecause = \\\"waiting\\\"\\n344\\t  remaining: number;        // live items left behind the stop point\\n345\\t}\\n346\\t\\n347\\t// ── per-owner report + repair (CLI: lhc messages report / lhc turns report …) ──\\n348\\texport interface FormReportEntry extends DerivedForm {\\n349\\t  queue?: { status: \\\"queued\\\" | \\\"claimed\\\"; attempts: number;\\n350\\t    lastError?: string; eligibleAt?: string };   // live item, if any\\n351\\t}\\n352\\texport interface MessagesSurface /* extends Epic 01 */ {\\n353\\t  workHandlers: Record<WorkKind, WorkHandler>;\\n354\\t  report(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { notReady?: boolean; messageId?: string }):\\n355\\t    Promise<OpResult<FormReportEntry[]>>;\\n356\\t  requeue(ref: ThreadRef, target: { messageId: string; form: FormKind }):\\n357\\t    Promise<OpResult<{ workItemId: string } | { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" }>>;\\n358\\t  edit(ref: ThreadRef, input: { messageId: string; content: string }):\\n359\\t    Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>>;\\n360\\t  deleteMessage(ref: ThreadRef, input: { messageId: string }):\\n361\\t    Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>>;\\n362\\t}\\n363\\texport interface TurnsSurface /* extends Epic 01 */ {\\n364\\t  workHandlers: Record<WorkKind, WorkHandler>;\\n365\\t  report(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { notReady?: boolean; turnId?: string; chunkId?: string }):\\n366\\t    Promise<OpResult<FormReportEntry[]>>;\\n367\\t  requeue(ref: ThreadRef, target: { subjectKind: \\\"turn\\\" | \\\"chunk\\\"; subjectId: string; form: FormKind }):\\n368\\t    Promise<OpResult<{ workItemId: string } | { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" }>>;\\n369\\t  deleteTurn(ref: ThreadRef, input: { turnId: string }): Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>>;\\n370\\t}\\n371\\texport interface MutationResult {\\n372\\t  changed: { messageIds: string[]; turnIds: string[] };\\n373\\t  cleared: Array<{ subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: FormKind }>;\\n374\\t  dropped: Array<{ subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: FormKind }>;\\n375\\t  queued: Array<{ workItemId: string; kind: WorkKind }>;\\n376\\t  superseded: string[];      // work item ids tidied by the cascade (issue 1)\\n377\\t}\\n378\\t\\n379\\t// ── handler contract (internal; the map's value type) ────────────\\n380\\texport type WorkHandler = (run: HandlerRunContext, item: WorkItemRecord)\\n381\\t  => Promise<HandlerOutcome>;\\n382\\texport interface HandlerRunContext {\\n383\\t  openDb(): DatabaseSync;            // short-txn access; NEVER held across provider calls\\n384\\t  provider: DerivationProvider;\\n385\\t  clock: () => Date;\\n386\\t  config: Required<SdkConfig>;\\n387\\t}\\n388\\texport type HandlerOutcome =\\n389\\t  | { ok: true }                                   // forms written by handler, version-checked\\n390\\t  | { ok: false; retryable: boolean; reason: string }\\n391\\t  | { ok: false; blocked: true; reason: string };  // source damage → form blocked, item terminal\\n392\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"c1de3f50-133a-4f79-8a5b-672d328b384b\",\"uuid\":\"d32b1a0d-5b09-437e-b984-178dbfeb5ed4\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-11T06:20:54.263Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/tech-design.md\",\"content\":\"  else idle\\n    SCH->>DR: start (unawaited)\\n  end\\n  loop until queue empty\\n    DR->>WQ: claimNext(db) — BEGIN IMMEDIATE, oldest queued, lease stamp\\n    DR->>H: handlers[kind](runCtx, item)\\n    H-->>DR: outcome\\n    DR->>WQ: complete / failAttempt — short txn, version-checked write\\n  end\\n  DR->>SCH: finished → rerun once if pending\\n```\\n\\nThe drain claims under `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` (claim is a write); runs the handler with **no open transaction** (provider call lives here); completes in a second short transaction. A drain finding the head item claimed with an unexpired lease stops with `stoppedBecause: \\\"in_flight\\\"` and processes nothing (AC-1.4); a head gated by backoff stops it with `\\\"waiting\\\"` — the never-skip-ahead rule in Part 3b governs both. Expired lease → reclaim: attempts increment, item runs again; the source-version check and idempotent artifact write make a double-run harmless (the first run's write either landed before reclaim — completing the item — or lands stale and discards). Lease default 120s (config), chosen >> p99 provider latency.\\n\\nRetry/backoff: budget 3 attempts (config). `failAttempt` under budget: status back to `queued`, `attempts++`, eligibility delayed by `min(2^attempts × 5s, 60s)` encoded as a `claim_expires_at`-style `eligible_at` check in `claimNext`'s WHERE. At budget: status `failed_terminal`, form → `failed` with the final reason (AC-1.9). Backoff values are config; tests set them to 0.\\n\\n**Flow 2 — Message-level derivation.** Handlers read the message row + blocks; tool-call summary additionally reads its paired result by `tool_call_id` (`outcome.ts` derives `succeeded | failed | unknown` mechanically from `isError`/presence — the provider's text never touches the outcome field, AC-2.4). The outcome lands in `derived_form.metadata`, not in `content`: machine-readable apart from provider text. Intake's `MESSAGE_WORK_KINDS` map gains `tool_call: \\\"tool_call_summary\\\"` (AC-2.2). The second intake touch is the late-result repair (AC-2.8): when projecting a `tool_result`, one indexed lookup — does a `tool_call_summary` form exist for the paired call with `metadata.outcome = \\\"unknown\\\"`? If so, requeue it in the batch transaction (the requeue no-op rule makes this idempotent). Both touches are deterministic and local. Forms land via `forms.ts` **UPDATE-only writes with the source-version check** (never upsert — the pending row exists from enqueue; a write that finds no matching row discards as stale).\\n\\n**Flow 3 — Turn composition and chunks.** `turn_derivation` handler: load member messages (deleted-filtered), collect their message-level forms, compose rendering (`compose.ts`) — ready forms verbatim, non-ready fall back to raw/truncated content **recording a gap per fallback** (AC-3.2); tool runs become outcome-explicit accounts grouped by consecutive tool activity (AC-3.4). Rendering → provider `composeTurnRendering`; projection → `projectLowerBand`. Both land as turn forms; placement then runs in the completion transaction: append to open chunk (`chunks.ts`), close on accumulated policy (DD-9), closing enqueues `chunk_summary_detailed` + `chunk_summary_brief` (two items, independent retry — AC-3.8) whose handlers read member projections and call their provider ops.\\n\\nGap semantics (AC-3.3): gaps are recorded facts on the landed artifact. A dependency later repairing does not touch dependents; `report` surfaces gapped artifacts; explicit `requeue` rebuilds (next source version, gaps recomputed from current dependency states).\\n\\n**Flow 4 — Report and repair.** `report(ref, { owner, notReady? })` is one query: `derived_form` LEFT JOIN live `work_item` rows for the subject's forms, exposing state + reason + gaps + queue detail (`attempts`, `last_error`, `eligible_at`). The five distinctions read: `pending` & no attempts = waiting; `pending` & attempts>0 = retrying; `ready`; `failed`; `blocked`. `requeue(ref, { subjectKind, subjectId, form })`: refused for `blocked` (with the blocking reason) and for missing rows; no-op if a live item already targets the form at its current source version (AC-4.5, one EXISTS check); otherwise enqueue at the form's current source version. Requeue of a `failed` form never collides with old work: the failed item's row was deleted at terminal transition (DD-1), and the deterministic id is scoped to the current source version.\\n\\n**Flows 5/6 — Mutations.** One transaction (`runInTransaction`): validate (exists via deleted-filtered read; turn closed; for message-delete: not turn-initiating — else `message_initiates_turn` naming the turn and the turns-delete path), apply record change (content+blocks+token re-stamp for edit; `deleted_at` stamp for deletes), run cascade (DD-8): bump source version + `pending` on cleared forms, drop forms whose subject is deleted (state rows removed — dropped, not failed, AC-6.6), supersede-delete still-queued old-version items (issue 1), enqueue replacements with target source version, register poke. Claimed old-version items may still finish; DD-3 discards their stale results because their source version no longer matches. Result reports changed/cleared/dropped/queued/superseded. Refusals: `turn_open`, `message_not_found`/`turn_not_found`, second delete of the same id → `message_not_found` by the filtered read (AC-6.7's \\\"refusal, not silent success\\\").\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Part 3: Interfaces\\n\\n```typescript\\n// ── shared/derivation.ts ─────────────────────────────────────────\\nexport type FormKind =\\n  | \\\"smoothed_prompt\\\" | \\\"tool_call_summary\\\" | \\\"tool_result_summary\\\"\\n  | \\\"turn_rendering\\\" | \\\"lower_band_projection\\\"\\n  | \\\"chunk_summary_detailed\\\" | \\\"chunk_summary_brief\\\";\\n\\nexport type DerivedFormState = \\\"pending\\\" | \\\"ready\\\" | \\\"failed\\\" | \\\"blocked\\\";\\n\\nexport interface DependencyGap { subjectKind: \\\"message\\\" | \\\"turn\\\" | \\\"chunk\\\"; subjectId: string; form: FormKind; }\\n\\nexport interface DerivedForm {\\n  subjectKind: \\\"message\\\" | \\\"turn\\\" | \\\"chunk\\\";\\n  subjectId: string;\\n  form: FormKind;\\n  state: DerivedFormState;\\n  content?: string;          // ready only\\n  reason?: string;           // failed | blocked\\n  sourceVersion: number;     // which version of the source this form derives from (DD-3)\\n  gaps?: DependencyGap[];    // composed forms; landed-with-fallback record\\n  metadata?: { outcome?: ToolOutcome };  // mechanically stamped fields; never provider-authored\\n  derivedAt?: string;\\n}\\n\\n// outcome on tool-activity summaries — mechanically stamped (AC-2.4)\\nexport type ToolOutcome = \\\"succeeded\\\" | \\\"failed\\\" | \\\"unknown\\\";\\n\\n// ── provider seam (injected at createSdk) ────────────────────────\\nexport type ProviderResult =\\n  | { ok: true; text: string }\\n  | { ok: false; retryable: boolean; reason: string };\\n\\nexport interface DerivationProvider {\\n  smoothPrompt(i: { text: string }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n  summarizeToolCall(i: { toolName: string; argsJson: string;\\n    pairedResult?: { content: string; isError: boolean } }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n  summarizeToolResult(i: { toolName: string; content: string }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n  composeTurnRendering(i: { parts: RenderingPart[] }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n  projectLowerBand(i: { rendering: string }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n  summarizeChunkDetailed(i: { memberProjections: string[] }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n  summarizeChunkBrief(i: { memberProjections: string[] }): Promise<ProviderResult>;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface RenderingPart {\\n  messageId: string;\\n  kind: EventKind;\\n  text: string;                    // ready form content, or raw/truncated fallback\\n  fallback: boolean;               // true ⇒ gap recorded\\n  outcome?: ToolOutcome;           // tool activity only\\n}\\n\\n// ── SDK assembly ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\\nexport interface SdkConfig {\\n  provider: DerivationProvider;\\n  mode: \\\"background\\\" | \\\"manual\\\";\\n  clock?: () => Date;\\n  retry?: { budget: number; backoffBaseMs: number; backoffCapMs: number };   // 3 / 5000 / 60000\\n  lease?: { durationMs: number };                                            // 120000\\n  chunkPolicy?: { targetProjectedTokens: number; maxProjectedTokens: number }; // 2200 / 4400\\n}\\nexport function createSdk(config: SdkConfig): Lhc;\\n\\nexport interface Lhc {\\n  threads: /* Epic 01 surface, unchanged */;\\n  intakeStream: /* Epic 01 surface; tool_call now queues work */;\\n  messages: MessagesSurface;\\n  turns: TurnsSurface;\\n  work: WorkSurface;\\n  drainSettled(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<void>;   // issue 3: resolves when no running/pending drain (internal resolution to thread id)\\n}\\n\\n// ── work surface (CLI: lhc work …) ───────────────────────────────\\nexport interface WorkSurface {\\n  drain(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { maxItems?: number }): Promise<OpResult<DrainReport>>;\\n}\\nexport interface DrainReport {\\n  ran: Array<{ workItemId: string; kind: WorkKind; sourceRef: WorkSourceRef;\\n    disposition: \\\"done\\\" | \\\"failed_terminal\\\" | \\\"stale_discarded\\\";  // superseded never reaches a drain — cascade deletes + reports it on MutationResult\\n    attempts: number; reason?: string }>;\\n  stoppedBecause: \\\"empty\\\" | \\\"in_flight\\\" | \\\"waiting\\\" | \\\"max_items\\\";\\n  waitingUntil?: string;    // head's eligible_at when stoppedBecause = \\\"waiting\\\"\\n  remaining: number;        // live items left behind the stop point\\n}\\n\\n// ── per-owner report + repair (CLI: lhc messages report / lhc turns report …) ──\\nexport interface FormReportEntry extends DerivedForm {\\n  queue?: { status: \\\"queued\\\" | \\\"claimed\\\"; attempts: number;\\n    lastError?: string; eligibleAt?: string };   // live item, if any\\n}\\nexport interface MessagesSurface /* extends Epic 01 */ {\\n  workHandlers: Record<WorkKind, WorkHandler>;\\n  report(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { notReady?: boolean; messageId?: string }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<FormReportEntry[]>>;\\n  requeue(ref: ThreadRef, target: { messageId: string; form: FormKind }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<{ workItemId: string } | { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" }>>;\\n  edit(ref: ThreadRef, input: { messageId: string; content: string }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>>;\\n  deleteMessage(ref: ThreadRef, input: { messageId: string }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>>;\\n}\\nexport interface TurnsSurface /* extends Epic 01 */ {\\n  workHandlers: Record<WorkKind, WorkHandler>;\\n  report(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { notReady?: boolean; turnId?: string; chunkId?: string }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<FormReportEntry[]>>;\\n  requeue(ref: ThreadRef, target: { subjectKind: \\\"turn\\\" | \\\"chunk\\\"; subjectId: string; form: FormKind }):\\n    Promise<OpResult<{ workItemId: string } | { noop: \\\"already_queued\\\" }>>;\\n  deleteTurn(ref: ThreadRef, input: { turnId: string }): Promise<OpResult<MutationResult>>;\\n}\\nexport interface MutationResult {\\n  changed: { messageIds: string[]; turnIds: string[] };\\n  cleared: Array<{ subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: FormKind }>;\\n  dropped: Array<{ subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: FormKind }>;\\n  queued: Array<{ workItemId: string; kind: WorkKind }>;\\n  superseded: string[];      // work item ids tidied by the cascade (issue 1)\\n}\\n\\n// ── handler contract (internal; the map's value type) ────────────\\nexport type WorkHandler = (run: HandlerRunContext, item: WorkItemRecord)\\n  => Promise<HandlerOutcome>;\\nexport interface HandlerRunContext {\\n  openDb(): DatabaseSync;            // short-txn access; NEVER held across provider calls\\n  provider: DerivationProvider;\\n  clock: () => Date;\\n  config: Required<SdkConfig>;\\n}\\nexport type HandlerOutcome =\\n  | { ok: true }                                   // forms written by handler, version-checked\\n  | { ok: false; retryable: boolean; reason: string }\\n  | { ok: false; blocked: true; reason: string };  // source damage → form blocked, item terminal\\n\",\"numLines\":160,\"startLine\":233,\"totalLines\":490}}}\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/001-quick-fix.stdout.log:289:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"signature_delta\",\"signature\":\"\"}},\"session_id\":\"c1de3f50-133a-4f79-8a5b-672d328b384b\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"30dde6a6-eb8a-4815-bfd2-96c75acddf0a\"}\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/quick-fix/streams/001-quick-fix.stdout.log:290:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"id\":\"msg_01VU4KqfxJeFXeiYoixFFP