ant message composition.** Confirmed `[thinking, text]`, `[thinking, toolCall]`, `[toolCall×N]` all occur; thinking carries an encrypted `thinkingSignature` (provider reasoning token — opaque, store-or-drop is an LHC call). The fan-out order in one message is thinking → text → toolCalls.\\\\n132:- **session_start reason.** `\\\\\\\"startup\\\\\\\"` on fresh and on resume alike in print mode; `previousSessionFile` was absent. The reason-code taxonomy (`new/resume/reload/fork`) from the docs may surface differently in interactive vs print mode — worth confirming interactively, but not blocking.\\\\n134:**Fork (`--fork`), captured solo:** forking a session creates a **new** session file (UUID-named); the original is untouched. The fork inherited all prior history via the `context` hook (11 messages present). In print mode `session_start` still reported `reason=startup` and carried no fork lineage in the payload — the lineage lives in the session file's `parentId` chain (below), not the event. `session_before_fork` did not fire in print-mode `--fork` (likely an interactive-command hook). **Fork-as-new-thread (the PRD decision) matches PI's own behavior — PI already makes a new file.**\\\\n139:- First line: `{type:\\\\\\\"session\\\\\\\", version:3, id, timestamp, cwd}`.\\\\n149:- **Graceful interrupt (Esc):** the partial assistant message gets a normal `message_end` with content preserved (`[thinking, text]`, ~120 lines kept) and **`stopReason: \\\\\\\"aborted\\\\\\\"`**; `turn_end` fires, also `stopReason: \\\\\\\"aborted\\\\\\\"`; `agent_end` fires. A graceful abort is a *complete, well-formed turn marked aborted* — partial content is real and worth keeping. The session continues normally on the next prompt (verified: follow-up ran `stopReason: \\\\\\\"stop\\\\\\\"`, no recovery path).\\\\n151:- Mapper carries `stopReason` through; LHC distinguishes \\\\\\\"aborted-but-complete\\\\\\\" from \\\\\\\"crashed-open.\\\\\\\"\\\\n156:| Transition | Sequence | `session_start.reason` | `previousSessionFile` |\\\\n160:| `/resume` | `session_before_switch{resume}` → `session_shutdown{resume}` → re-init → `session_start{resume}` | `resume` | populated (left session) |\\\\n161:- **`session_before_switch`** is the pre-transition hook (fires for new/resume, not reload) — where the extension disposes the old LHC instance and flushes before the swap.\\\\n162:- **Reload wipes extension in-memory state** (`_loaded` re-fires) but continues the same session — so the thread mapping must reconstruct from the session file, not closures (confirms the PRD extension-state-discipline decision with evidence). `reason: \\\\\\\"reload\\\\\\\"` lets Lifecycle detect-and-reattach rather than create.\\\\n163:- **Resume re-fires zero `message_end` events** (confirmed interactively, matching §5a) — history served via `context` only. Dedup is needed for `/reload` + crash-replay, not normal resume.\\\\n182:5. **What resume actually replays.** ANSWERED (§5a): resume does not re-fire history; PI serves prior context through the `context` hook. Aborts and the context-hook mid-turn view still need the recording period.\\\\n191:**Epic A — Connector core (intake + lifecycle + inference host):** ~5–6 stories. SDK construction/teardown on session lifecycle, thread mapping + resume/reload/fork handling, message/turn event mapper (converter productionized), `ModelCall` + assignments config + startup validation, ordering/idempotency proof against recorded corpora.\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"interrupted\\\":false,\\\"isImage\\\":false,\\\"noOutputExpected\\\":false}}\\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:699:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_017BJttBzkdEmVK7dov3ssyd\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"1\\\\timport { describe, expect, it } from \\\\\\\"vitest\\\\\\\";\\\\n2\\\\timport { activate, createConnector, disposeInstance, EPIC_1_HOOKS, initInstance } from \\\\\\\"../../src/index.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n3\\\\timport { createSessionState } from \\\\\\\"../../src/lifecycle/state.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n4\\\\timport type { ExtensionAPI, ExtensionContext, PiHookName } from \\\\\\\"../../src/pi/types.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n5\\\\timport { makeAgentEnd, makeMessageEnd, makeSessionStart, makeUserMessage } from \\\\\\\"../fixtures/synthetic.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n6\\\\t\\\\n7\\\\t// A fake ExtensionAPI that records what the extension registers.\\\\n8\\\\tfunction recordingPi(): {\\\\n9\\\\t  pi: ExtensionAPI;\\\\n10\\\\t  registered: PiHookName[];\\\\n11\\\\t  commands: string[];\\\\n12\\\\t  tools: string[];\\\\n13\\\\t} {\\\\n14\\\\t  const registered: PiHookName[] = [];\\\\n15\\\\t  const commands: string[] = [];\\\\n16\\\\t  const tools: string[] = [];\\\\n17\\\\t  const pi: ExtensionAPI = {\\\\n18\\\\t    registerHook(name) {\\\\n19\\\\t      registered.push(name);\\\\n20\\\\t    },\\\\n21\\\\t    registerCommand(name) {\\\\n22\\\\t      commands.push(name);\\\\n23\\\\t    },\\\\n24\\\\t    registerTool(tool) {\\\\n25\\\\t      tools.push(tool.name);\\\\n26\\\\t    },\\\\n27\\\\t    appendEntry() {},\\\\n28\\\\t  };\\\\n29\\\\t  return { pi, registered, commands, tools };\\\\n30\\\\t}\\\\n31\\\\t\\\\n32\\\\t// A synthetic per-hook ctx carrying METHODS (not plain data) and a unique\\\\n33\\\\t// marker — so a retained ctx would break the structuredClone plain-data guard.\\\\n34\\\\tfunction syntheticCtx(marker: string): ExtensionContext {\\\\n35\\\\t  return {\\\\n36\\\\t    cwd: `/tmp/${marker}`,\\\\n37\\\\t    hasUI: false,\\\\n38\\\\t    modelRegistry: {\\\\n39\\\\t      find: () => undefined,\\\\n40\\\\t      hasConfiguredAuth: () => false,\\\\n41\\\\t      getAvailable: () => [],\\\\n42\\\\t    },\\\\n43\\\\t    ui: { notify: () => {} },\\\\n44\\\\t    sessionManager: { getEntries: () => [] },\\\\n45\\\\t  };\\\\n46\\\\t}\\\\n47\\\\t\\\\n48\\\\tdescribe(\\\\\\\"extension load + hook rail\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n49\\\\t  it(\\\\\\\"registers exactly the Epic 1 observe-only hook rail and not the context hook\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n50\\\\t    const { pi, registered, commands, tools } = recordingPi();\\\\n51\\\\t    activate(pi);\\\\n52\\\\t\\\\n53\\\\t    expect(new Set(registered)).toEqual(new Set(EPIC_1_HOOKS));\\\\n54\\\\t    expect(registered).toHaveLength(9);\\\\n55\\\\t    expect(registered).not.toContain(\\\\\\\"context\\\\\\\"); // context serving is Epic 2\\\\n56\\\\t    // observe-only: no operator commands / agent tools registered yet (Epic 3)\\\\n57\\\\t    expect(commands).toEqual([]);\\\\n58\\\\t    expect(tools).toEqual([]);\\\\n59\\\\t  });\\\\n60\\\\t\\\\n61\\\\t  it(\\\\\\\"routes every hook to a guarded handler that never throws into PI and retains only plain data\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n62\\\\t    const connector = createConnector();\\\\n63\\\\t    // fire several hooks with DISTINCT ctx objects carrying methods\\\\n64\\\\t    await connector.handlers.session_start(syntheticCtx(\\\\\\\"ctx-1\\\\\\\"), makeSessionStart(\\\\\\\"startup\\\\\\\"));\\\\n65\\\\t    await connector.handlers.message_end(syntheticCtx(\\\\\\\"ctx-2\\\\\\\"), makeMessageEnd(makeUserMessage(\\\\\\\"hi\\\\\\\")));\\\\n66\\\\t    await connector.handlers.agent_end(syntheticCtx(\\\\\\\"ctx-3\\\\\\\"), makeAgentEnd([]));\\\\n67\\\\t\\\\n68\\\\t    // (the awaits above completing is the \\\\\\\"never throws into PI\\\\\\\" assertion)\\\\n69\\\\t    // retained state is plain data: structuredClone throws on a stored PI ctx (it has methods)\\\\n70\\\\t    expect(() => structuredClone(connector.snapshot())).not.toThrow();\\\\n71\\\\t  });\\\\n72\\\\t\\\\n73\\\\t  it(\\\\\\\"keeps SessionState plain-data-only — it survives structuredClone with every field populated\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n74\\\\t    const state = createSessionState({ filePath: \\\\\\\"/tmp/thread.sqlite\\\\\\\" });\\\\n75\\\\t    state.flags.startupValidationReported = true;\\\\n76\\\\t    state.flags.toldUserAboutGap = true; // open index signature, still plain data\\\\n77\\\\t    state.health.lastCaptureFailure = { code: \\\\\\\"malformed_event\\\\\\\", message: \\\\\\\"bad shape\\\\\\\", recordedGap: true };\\\\n78\\\\t    state.health.startupValidation = { unreachable: [] };\\\\n79\\\\t\\\\n80\\\\t    const clone = structuredClone(state);\\\\n81\\\\t    expect(clone).toEqual(state);\\\\n82\\\\t    expect(clone).not.toBe(state);\\\\n83\\\\t  });\\\\n84\\\\t\\\\n85\\\\t  it(\\\\\\\"exposes a stubbed init/dispose seam that returns a typed fail-closed result\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n86\\\\t    const initResult = await initInstance({ filePath: \\\\\\\"/tmp/thread.sqlite\\\\\\\" }, { mode: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\" });\\\\n87\\\\t    expect(initResult.ok).toBe(false);\\\\n88\\\\t    if (!initResult.ok) {\\\\n89\\\\t      expect(initResult.error).toEqual({\\\\n90\\\\t        errorClass: \\\\\\\"system_error\\\\\\\",\\\\n91\\\\t        code: \\\\\\\"not_implemented\\\\\\\",\\\\n92\\\\t        reason: \\\\\\\"lifecycle.initInstance is not implemented yet (Epic 1 foundation stub)\\\\\\\",\\\\n93\\\\t      });\\\\n94\\\\t    }\\\\n95\\\\t\\\\n96\\\\t    const disposeResult = await disposeInstance(null);\\\\n97\\\\t    expect(disposeResult.ok).toBe(false);\\\\n98\\\\t    if (!disposeResult.ok) {\\\\n99\\\\t      expect(disposeResult.error).toEqual({\\\\n100\\\\t        errorClass: \\\\\\\"system_error\\\\\\\",\\\\n101\\\\t        code: \\\\\\\"not_implemented\\\\\\\",\\\\n102\\\\t        reason: \\\\\\\"lifecycle.disposeInstance is not implemented yet (Epic 1 foundation stub)\\\\\\\",\\\\n103\\\\t      });\\\\n104\\\\t    }\\\\n105\\\\t  });\\\\n106\\\\t});\\\\n107\\\\t\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"a3966ea6-6869-416b-ab8c-4e847e617766\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-14T04:08:39.278Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"file\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"import { describe, expect, it } from \\\\\\\"vitest\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { activate, createConnector, disposeInstance, EPIC_1_HOOKS, initInstance } from \\\\\\\"../../src/index.js\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { createSessionState } from \\\\\\\"../../src/lifecycle/state.js\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport type { ExtensionAPI, ExtensionContext, PiHookName } from \\\\\\\"../../src/pi/types.js\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { makeAgentEnd, makeMessageEnd, makeSessionStart, makeUserMessage } from \\\\\\\"../fixtures/synthetic.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\n// A fake ExtensionAPI that records what the extension registers.\\\\nfunction recordingPi(): {\\\\n  pi: ExtensionAPI;\\\\n  registered: PiHookName[];\\\\n  commands: string[];\\\\n  tools: string[];\\\\n} {\\\\n  const registered: PiHookName[] = [];\\\\n  const commands: string[] = [];\\\\n  const tools: string[] = [];\\\\n  const pi: ExtensionAPI = {\\\\n    registerHook(name) {\\\\n      registered.push(name);\\\\n    },\\\\n    registerCommand(name) {\\\\n      commands.push(name);\\\\n    },\\\\n    registerTool(tool) {\\\\n      tools.push(tool.name);\\\\n    },\\\\n    appendEntry() {},\\\\n  };\\\\n  return { pi, registered, commands, tools };\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n// A synthetic per-hook ctx carrying METHODS (not plain data) and a unique\\\\n// marker — so a retained ctx would break the structuredClone plain-data guard.\\\\nfunction syntheticCtx(marker: string): ExtensionContext {\\\\n  return {\\\\n    cwd: `/tmp/${marker}`,\\\\n    hasUI: false,\\\\n    modelRegistry: {\\\\n      find: () => undefined,\\\\n      hasConfiguredAuth: () => false,\\\\n      getAvailable: () => [],\\\\n    },\\\\n    ui: { notify: () => {} },\\\\n    sessionManager: { getEntries: () => [] },\\\\n  };\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\ndescribe(\\\\\\\"extension load + hook rail\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n  it(\\\\\\\"registers exactly the Epic 1 observe-only hook rail and not the context hook\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n    const { pi, registered, commands, tools } = recordingPi();\\\\n    activate(pi);\\\\n\\\\n    expect(new Set(registered)).toEqual(new Set(EPIC_1_HOOKS));\\\\n    expect(registered).toHaveLength(9);\\\\n    expect(registered).not.toContain(\\\\\\\"context\\\\\\\"); // context serving is Epic 2\\\\n    // observe-only: no operator commands / agent tools registered yet (Epic 3)\\\\n    expect(commands).toEqual([]);\\\\n    expect(tools).toEqual([]);\\\\n  });\\\\n\\\\n  it(\\\\\\\"routes every hook to a guarded handler that never throws into PI and retains only plain data\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n    const connector = createConnector();\\\\n    // fire several hooks with DISTINCT ctx objects carrying methods\\\\n    await connector.handlers.session_start(syntheticCtx(\\\\\\\"ctx-1\\\\\\\"), makeSessionStart(\\\\\\\"startup\\\\\\\"));\\\\n    await connector.handlers.message_end(syntheticCtx(\\\\\\\"ctx-2\\\\\\\"), makeMessageEnd(makeUserMessage(\\\\\\\"hi\\\\\\\")));\\\\n    await connector.handlers.agent_end(syntheticCtx(\\\\\\\"ctx-3\\\\\\\"), makeAgentEnd([]));\\\\n\\\\n    // (the awaits above completing is the \\\\\\\"never throws into PI\\\\\\\" assertion)\\\\n    // retained state is plain data: structuredClone throws on a stored PI ctx (it has methods)\\\\n    expect(() => structuredClone(connector.snapshot())).not.toThrow();\\\\n  });\\\\n\\\\n  it(\\\\\\\"keeps SessionState plain-data-only — it survives structuredClone with every field populated\\\\\\\", () => {\\\\n    const state = createSessionState({ filePath: \\\\\\\"/tmp/thread.sqlite\\\\\\\" });\\\\n    state.flags.startupValidationReported = true;\\\\n    state.flags.toldUserAboutGap = true; // open index signature, still plain data\\\\n    state.health.lastCaptureFailure = { code: \\\\\\\"malformed_event\\\\\\\", message: \\\\\\\"bad shape\\\\\\\", recordedGap: true };\\\\n    state.health.startupValidation = { unreachable: [] };\\\\n\\\\n    const clone = structuredClone(state);\\\\n    expect(clone).toEqual(state);\\\\n    expect(clone).not.toBe(state);\\\\n  });\\\\n\\\\n  it(\\\\\\\"exposes a stubbed init/dispose seam that returns a typed fail-closed result\\\\\\\", async () => {\\\\n    const initResult = await initInstance({ filePath: \\\\\\\"/tmp/thread.sqlite\\\\\\\" }, { mode: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\" });\\\\n    expect(initResult.ok).toBe(false);\\\\n    if (!initResult.ok) {\\\\n      expect(initResult.error).toEqual({\\\\n        errorClass: \\\\\\\"system_error\\\\\\\",\\\\n        code: \\\\\\\"not_implemented\\\\\\\",\\\\n        reason: \\\\\\\"lifecycle.initInstance is not implemented yet (Epic 1 foundation stub)\\\\\\\",\\\\n      });\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    const disposeResult = await disposeInstance(null);\\\\n    expect(disposeResult.ok).toBe(false);\\\\n    if (!disposeResult.ok) {\\\\n      expect(disposeResult.error).toEqual({\\\\n        errorClass: \\\\\\\"system_error\\\\\\\",\\\\n        code: \\\\\\\"not_implemented\\\\\\\",\\\\n        reason: \\\\\\\"lifecycle.disposeInstance is not implemented yet (Epic 1 foundation stub)\\\\\\\",\\\\n      });\\\\n    }\\\\n  });\\\\n});\\\\n\\\",\\\"numLines\\\":107,\\\"startLine\\\":1,\\\"totalLines\\\":107}}}\\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:3086:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"stream_event\\\",\\\"event\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"content_block_delta\\\",\\\"index\\\":0,\\\"delta\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"input_json_delta\\\",\\\"partial_json\\\":\\\"_HOOKS = [\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"session_start\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"message_end\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"turn_end\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"agent_end\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"model_select\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"th\\\"}},\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\\\",\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"57e1c1b0-4cf3-45c8-9af8-edb5ec3359d6\\\"}\\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:3153:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"stream_event\\\",\\\"event\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"content_block_delta\\\",\\\"index\\\":0,\\\"delta\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"input_json_delta\\\",\\\"partial_json\\\":\\\"};\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n  // Observe-only foundation: capture-bearing hooks (message_end, turn_end,\\\"}},\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\\\",\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"bdfdcc69-f18b-4391-83d1-f6a02a62b75b\\\"}\\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:3158:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"stream_event\\\",\\\"event\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"content_block_delta\\\",\\\"index\\\":0,\\\"delta\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"input_json_delta\\\",\\\"partial_json\\\":\\\" PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook>,\\\\\\\\n    session_before_switch: onDispose,\\\\\\\\n    session_shutdown: onDispose,\\\\\\\\n    message_end: noop,\\\\\\\\n    turn_end: noop,\\\"}},\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\\\",\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"63ab22a9-407f-422f-b1b8-ca8395eff762\\\"}\\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/streams/003-implementor.stdout.log:3169:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-opus-4-8\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_01L1thhg7edm6LJR3kzjoEje\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"toolu_016CwHShWBADCx8WWmqCHpU1\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Write\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"file_path\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"// Extension entry. PI loads this module and calls `activate(pi)`; it registers\\\\n// the Epic 1 observe-only hook rail and routes each hook to a fail-closed\\\\n// handler. The connector owns only plain-data `SessionState` plus the live\\\\n// `LhcInstance` it constructs per session — never a PI `ctx`/session object,\\\\n// which PI replaces on new/resume/fork (tech design Flow 1, plain-data rule).\\\\nimport { mkdirSync } from \\\\\\\"node:fs\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { homedir } from \\\\\\\"node:os\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { join } from \\\\\\\"node:path\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { randomUUID } from \\\\\\\"node:crypto\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport type { OpResult, SdkConfig, ThreadRef } from \\\\\\\"lhc\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport type {\\\\n  ExtensionAPI,\\\\n  ExtensionContext,\\\\n  PiHookHandler,\\\\n  PiHookName,\\\\n} from \\\\\\\"./pi/types.js\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport type { CaptureFailureDiagnostic, SessionState } from \\\\\\\"./lifecycle/state.js\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { createSessionState } from \\\\\\\"./lifecycle/state.js\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { disposeInstance, initInstance } from \\\\\\\"./lifecycle/instance.js\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport {\\\\n  parseLaunchFlags,\\\\n  resolveThread,\\\\n  type LaunchFlags,\\\\n} from \\\\\\\"./lifecycle/thread-resolution.js\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport { pickThread, type ThreadChoice } from \\\\\\\"./lifecycle/picker.js\\\\\\\";\\\\nimport type { LhcInstance } from \\\\\\\"./shared/instance.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\nexport { disposeInstance, initInstance, initLhc } from \\\\\\\"./lifecycle/instance.js\\\\\\\";\\\\nexport type { LhcInstance } from \\\\\\\"./shared/instance.js\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\n/** The Epic 1 observe-only hook rail: every PI hook the connector consumes.\\\\n *  Deliberately NOT `context` — context serving is Epic 2 and this epic\\\\n *  registers no handler for it (story Scope Out). */\\\\nexport const EPIC_1_HOOKS = [\\\\n  \\\\\\\"session_start\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"message_end\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"turn_end\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"agent_end\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"model_select\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"thinking_level_select\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"session_before_fork\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"session_before_switch\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"session_shutdown\\\\\\\",\\\\n] as const satisfies readonly PiHookName[];\\\\n\\\\nexport type Epic1Hook = (typeof EPIC_1_HOOKS)[number];\\\\n\\\\n/** What the connector needs from the host to run a session. All injectable so\\\\n *  the lifecycle is exercised against a real temp registry/thread in tests and\\\\n *  the default `~/.lhc` registry in production.\\\\n *\\\\n *  `buildSdkConfig` is the inference seam: it returns the SdkConfig (provider /\\\\n *  inference + policy) to construct the instance from. In Story 1 the real\\\\n *  config — the PI-model-registry-backed `ModelCall` and assignments — is not\\\\n *  wired yet (that is Stories 5/6), so the default fails closed; the connector\\\\n *  then resolves nothing and records a diagnostic rather than faking a session.\\\\n */\\\\nexport interface ConnectorDeps {\\\\n  buildSdkConfig?: (ctx: ExtensionContext) => OpResult<SdkConfig>;\\\\n  registryPath?: string;\\\\n  newThreadFilePath?: () => string;\\\\n  parseLaunch?: () => LaunchFlags;\\\\n  selectThread?: (\\\\n    choices: readonly ThreadChoice[],\\\\n    ctx: ExtensionContext,\\\\n  ) => Promise<string | null>;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n/** Everything the connector retains across hooks as PLAIN data — by\\\\n *  construction structuredClone-able. The live `LhcInstance` is held separately\\\\n *  in the closure (it is the connector's own engine, rebuilt on reload) and is\\\\n *  deliberately not part of the snapshot. */\\\\nexport interface ConnectorSnapshot {\\\\n  state: SessionState | null;\\\\n  lastDiagnostic: CaptureFailureDiagnostic | null;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport interface Connector {\\\\n  /** Register the observe-only hook rail on the PI extension API. */\\\\n  register(pi: ExtensionAPI): void;\\\\n  /** The plain-data state retained across hooks. `null` until a session\\\\n   *  resolves a thread; never holds a PI ctx. */\\\\n  getState(): SessionState | null;\\\\n  /** The live LHC instance for the current session, or `null`. A test/inspection\\\\n   *  seam — held by the connector but never part of the plain-data snapshot. */\\\\n  getInstance(): LhcInstance | null;\\\\n  /** Plain-data snapshot of all retained state (inspection/test seam). */\\\\n  snapshot(): ConnectorSnapshot;\\\\n  /** The hook handlers, keyed by event — exposed so tests can drive them with\\\\n   *  synthetic ctx/events without a live PI. */\\\\n  readonly handlers: Readonly<Record<Epic1Hook, PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook>>>;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nconst DEFAULT_LHC_DIR = join(homedir(), \\\\\\\".lhc\\\\\\\");\\\\n\\\\n/** Inference host not wired yet (Story 5/6): fail closed so a session resolves\\\\n *  nothing and records a diagnostic instead of constructing a faked instance. */\\\\nfunction inferenceNotConfigured(): OpResult<SdkConfig> {\\\\n  return {\\\\n    ok: false,\\\\n    error: {\\\\n      errorClass: \\\\\\\"system_error\\\\\\\",\\\\n      code: \\\\\\\"not_implemented\\\\\\\",\\\\n      reason:\\\\n        \\\\\\\"pi-lhc inference host not wired yet (Epic 1 Story 5); SDK construction deferred\\\\\\\",\\\\n    },\\\\n  };\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n/** Default new-thread file location: `~/.lhc/threads/<uuid>.sqlite`. The id is\\\\n *  generated by the registry at creation, so the file name is just a unique\\\\n *  handle; the directory is ensured up front (DatabaseSync does not create\\\\n *  parents). */\\\\nfunction defaultNewThreadFilePath(): string {\\\\n  const dir = join(DEFAULT_LHC_DIR, \\\\\\\"threads\\\\\\\");\\\\n  mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\\\\n  return join(dir, `${randomUUID()}.sqlite`);\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nfunction threadIdOf(ref: ThreadRef): string | null {\\\\n  return \\\\\\\"threadId\\\\\\\" in ref ? ref.threadId : null;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n/** Build a connector instance. Its mutable state lives in this closure; the\\\\n *  registered handlers capture it, so the instance stays live for the session\\\\n *  even when `activate` discards the returned object. */\\\\nexport function createConnector(deps: ConnectorDeps = {}): Connector {\\\\n  // The connector's retained state. `state` is plain data (the durable thread\\\\n  // reference + flags); `instance` is the live SDK engine (rebuilt on reload);\\\\n  // `rememberedThreadId` is the durable id the reload path reattaches by; and\\\\n  // `lastDiagnostic` is the plain-data health signal. None is a PI object.\\\\n  let state: SessionState | null = null;\\\\n  let instance: LhcInstance | null = null;\\\\n  let rememberedThreadId: string | null = null;\\\\n  let lastDiagnostic: CaptureFailureDiagnostic | null = null;\\\\n\\\\n  const buildSdkConfig = deps.buildSdkConfig ?? (() => inferenceNotConfigured());\\\\n  const newThreadFilePath = deps.newThreadFilePath ?? defaultNewThreadFilePath;\\\\n  const parseLaunch = deps.parseLaunch ?? (() => parseLaunchFlags(process.argv));\\\\n  const selectThread =\\\\n    deps.selectThread ?? ((): Promise<string | null> => Promise.resolve(null));\\\\n\\\\n  function diag(code: string, message: string): CaptureFailureDiagnostic {\\\\n    return { code, message, recordedGap: false };\\\\n  }\\\\n\\\\n  // On reload (same session continues, in-memory state wiped) reconstruct the\\\\n  // SAME thread from its durable id rather than re-running the launch — a\\\\n  // no-flag session would otherwise create a duplicate (AC-1.5). The launch\\\\n  // (process.argv) is the fallback when no id is remembered, which covers\\\\n  // --session/--continue/--resume reloads. The permanent home for reload\\\\n  // lineage is LHC thread metadata (Feature 2+).\\\\n  function launchFor(event: { reason: string }): LaunchFlags {\\\\n    if (event.reason === \\\\\\\"reload\\\\\\\" && rememberedThreadId !== null) {\\\\n      return { session: rememberedThreadId };\\\\n    }\\\\n    return parseLaunch();\\\\n  }\\\\n\\\\n  async function resolveForLaunch(\\\\n    launch: LaunchFlags,\\\\n    ctx: ExtensionContext,\\\\n  ): Promise<OpResult<ThreadRef | null>> {\\\\n    if (launch.resume === true) {\\\\n      const pickerDeps: {\\\\n        registryPath?: string;\\\\n        select: (choices: readonly ThreadChoice[]) => Promise<string | null>;\\\\n      } = { select: (choices) => selectThread(choices, ctx) };\\\\n      if (deps.registryPath !== undefined) pickerDeps.registryPath = deps.registryPath;\\\\n      return pickThread(ctx.cwd, pickerDeps);\\\\n    }\\\\n    const resolveDeps: { cwd: string; registryPath?: string; newThreadFilePath: () => string } = {\\\\n      cwd: ctx.cwd,\\\\n      newThreadFilePath,\\\\n    };\\\\n    if (deps.registryPath !== undefined) resolveDeps.registryPath = deps.registryPath;\\\\n    return resolveThread(launch, resolveDeps);\\\\n  }\\\\n\\\\n  // session_start: resolve the recording thread from the launch and construct\\\\n  // one background instance against it. Config is gated first so a session with\\\\n  // no usable inference config resolves/creates nothing (no orphan thread).\\\\n  const onSessionStart: PiHookHandler<\\\\\\\"session_start\\\\\\\"> = async (ctx, event) => {\\\\n    const config = buildSdkConfig(ctx);\\\\n    if (!config.ok) {\\\\n      lastDiagnostic = diag(\\\\\\\"instance_not_configured\\\\\\\", config.error.reason);\\\\n      return;\\\\n    }\\\\n    const resolved = await resolveForLaunch(launchFor(event), ctx);\\\\n    if (!resolved.ok) {\\\\n      lastDiagnostic = diag(\\\\\\\"thread_resolution_failed\\\\\\\", resolved.error.reason);\\\\n      return;\\\\n    }\\\\n    if (resolved.value === null) {\\\\n      lastDiagnostic = diag(\\\\\\\"no_thread_selected\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"--resume resolved no thread\\\\\\\");\\\\n      return;\\\\n    }\\\\n    const built = await initInstance(resolved.value, config.value);\\\\n    if (!built.ok) {\\\\n      lastDiagnostic = diag(\\\\\\\"instance_init_failed\\\\\\\", built.error.reason);\\\\n      return;\\\\n    }\\\\n    instance = built.value;\\\\n    state = createSessionState(resolved.value);\\\\n    rememberedThreadId = threadIdOf(resolved.value);\\\\n  };\\\\n\\\\n  // Dispose with flush before any session swap (session_before_switch fires\\\\n  // pre-new/resume) and on shutdown/reload. Idempotent: disposing twice or with\\\\n  // no live instance is a no-op.\\\\n  const onDispose: PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook> = async () => {\\\\n    const result = await disposeInstance(instance);\\\\n    if (!result.ok) lastDiagnostic = diag(\\\\\\\"dispose_failed\\\\\\\", result.error.reason);\\\\n    instance = null;\\\\n  };\\\\n\\\\n  // Contain every handler: an observe-only hook must never throw back into PI\\\\n  // (a thrown hook breaks the user's session). A caught error becomes a\\\\n  // plain-data diagnostic; it is never rethrown.\\\\n  const guard = (\\\\n    name: Epic1Hook,\\\\n    body: PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook>,\\\\n  ): PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook> => {\\\\n    return async (ctx, event): Promise<void> => {\\\\n      try {\\\\n        await body(ctx, event);\\\\n      } catch (err) {\\\\n        lastDiagnostic = {\\\\n          code: \\\\\\\"hook_handler_error\\\\\\\",\\\\n          message: `${name}: ${err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)}`,\\\\n          recordedGap: false,\\\\n        };\\\\n      }\\\\n    };\\\\n  };\\\\n\\\\n  // Observe-only foundation: capture-bearing hooks (message_end, turn_end,\\\\n  // agent_end, runtime changes, fork) stay no-ops in Story 1 — capture and fork\\\\n  // land in later stories. Each receives a FRESH ctx and retains none of it.\\\\n  const noop: PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook> = () => {\\\\n    // Intentionally empty — later stories replace this with real routing.\\\\n  };\\\\n\\\\n  // Bodies per hook: session lifecycle is live in Story 1; the rest are no-ops.\\\\n  const bodies: Record<Epic1Hook, PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook>> = {\\\\n    session_start: onSessionStart as PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook>,\\\\n    session_before_switch: onDispose,\\\\n    session_shutdown: onDispose,\\\\n    message_end: noop,\\\\n    turn_end: noop,\\\\n    agent_end: noop,\\\\n    model_select: noop,\\\\n    thinking_level_select: noop,\\\\n    session_before_fork: noop,\\\\n  };\\\\n\\\\n  const handlers = {} as Record<Epic1Hook, PiHookHandler<Epic1Hook>>;\\\\n  for (const name of EPIC_1_HOOKS) handlers[name] = guard(name, bodies[name]);\\\\n\\\\n  return {\\\\n    handlers,\\\\n    register(pi: ExtensionAPI): void {\\\\n      for (const name of EPIC_1_HOOKS) pi.registerHook(name, handlers[name]);\\\\n    },\\\\n    getState(): SessionState | null {\\\\n      return state;\\\\n    },\\\\n    getInstance(): LhcInstance | null {\\\\n      return instance;\\\\n    },\\\\n    snapshot(): ConnectorSnapshot {\\\\n      return { state, lastDiagnostic };\\\\n    },\\\\n  };\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n/** PI entry point: PI calls this with the ExtensionAPI when the extension\\\\n *  loads (and again on `/reload`). Registers the observe-only hook rail with\\\\n *  the production defaults (the `~/.lhc` registry, `process.argv` launch flags).\\\\n *  The inference-backed `buildSdkConfig` is wired in Stories 5/6; until then a\\\\n *  live session resolves nothing and records a diagnostic rather than faking. */\\\\nexport function activate(pi: ExtensionAPI): void {\\\\n  createConnector().register(pi);\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport default activate;\\\\n\\\"},\\\"caller\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"direct\\\"}}],\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"stop_details\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":2,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":5940,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":266166,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":5940},\\\"output_tokens\\\":35,\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"not_available\\\"},\\\"diagnostics\\\":null,\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"3bd99b80-3187-4d52-9c3e-b6b2c0cfc11e\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"71820be1-0492-4542-897b-b4786f11387d\\\",\\\"request_id\\\":\\\"req_011Cc2XLXTZbhz97M76SSSee\\\"}\\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-